1 NAME Hugh /ap Lewis/
2 GIVN Hugh
2 SURN ap Lewis
2 _MARNM ap Lewis
2 NICK Huw
2 NICK Captain Hugh Lewis
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1638
2 ADDR
3 STAE Probably Wales
1 DEAT
2 DATE 29 APR 1689
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia Colony
1 OCCU
1 TITL Capt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Capt Hugh ap Lewis married Margaret DALLATHY, daughter of William DALLATHY and Elizabeth. (Margaret DALLATHY was born about 1645 and died on 28 Nov 1700.)  They were named in his 1677 will along with their children
2 CONC : Elizabeth, Margarett, William, John, & Benjamin.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''This [https://www.geni.com/people/Abadieh-Davis/387950014690003153 Abadieh] is not a daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-Lewis/381946979340013407. 
2 CONT
2 CONT At least one source records his date of birth as 1652, but given the date of birth of his daughter Elizabeth, that seems unlikely.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abadiah is not listed in Margaret’s fathers 1677 will:
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of WILLIAM DALLATHY, GENT. OF BDOS St. Michaels Parish, Barbados 20 Nov 1677, RB6/10, P. 188
2 CONT * Dau Margrett Lewis, wf of Capt. Hugh Lewis;
2 CONT * Wife Elizabeth Dallathy ? Executrx;
2 CONT * gr chn Elizabeth, Margarett, William, John, & Benjamin, all at 18; Capt. John Farmer, Margarett Farmer, Samuell Farmer, & Elizabeth Farmer, the sons & daus of Samuel Farmer Esq of Bdos; James Cowes, gr ch of said Samuel.
2 CONT * Signed William Dallathy.
2 CONT * Wit: John Sparke, William (x) Lukus [or Curtis?], Susannah (x) Barnes
2 CONT * Proved 29 JUNE 1680, court says Hon. John Sparke is also decd.
2 CONT * (Barbados Records Wills and Administrations Volume 1, 2 and 3. Joanne McRee Sanders
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Comments 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/lewis/17668/
2 CONT
2 CONT >Hugh Lewis of Wales, probably born about 1638/1640, came over to Virginia and married Margaret (research indicated her full name as Margaret Dallathy -- I find no proof of this). Margaret reportedly died 28 Nov 1700, but I find n
2 CONC o proof of this at this time. Their daughter, Elizabeth, was born 10 May 1664 in New Kent, VA. She married 1) John Nix and 2) Abraham Venable Sr. I believe they also had a son, Hugh Lewis Jr. Again, no proof. Just a hunch. They mo
2 CONC st probably had others, but at this time I can't tie anyone else to them.
2 CONT
2 CONT >There is a record in Ancestry.com of a Hugh Lewis, Thomas Lewis, William Lewis and "Isabell" Lewis residing in Virginia in 1670. This could be our Hugh with other family members.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Hugh Lewis Jr. (b. abt 1675) was the father of Abadiah Lewis (b. abt 1703). If it is accurate that her father was "Hugh Lewis" then he had to be of a younger generation than Hugh married to Margaret. Possibly Hugh Jr. married an 
2 CONC Elizabeth. They undoubtedly had other children. I find Virginia land patents for a Hugh Lewis in both 1701 and 1717 on the Ancestry.com database. I need to research these patents further to see what area they were in. As Hugh who 
2 CONC married Margaret died supposedly before 29 Apr 1689, then these land patents could in no way be his.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/LT4K-S3X/captain-hugh-lewis-1642-1689
2 CONT * http://www.choicemn.com/trees/gibson-tullis/4895.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Lewis was a slave . Hugh Lewis was the captain of a slave trading ship. He lived in Barbados with Elizabeth AND he had a wife in Virginia named Margaret Dallathy. Abadiah Lewis is the daughter of Hugh and Elizabeth Lewis
2 CONC .
