1 NOTE {geni:about_me} James was born in Barbados, where his father, an English Planter, had moved in 1634. James married an apparent widow, Mrs. James Lewis, in Barbados. Her late husband must have been related somehow to James' mother,
2 CONC  Elizabeth Lewis. James and wife became the ancestors of our Nix line, and of most (if not all) of the Nixes of VA, SC, GA, MS, and elsewhere in the US such as those who migrated from GA to CO in the early 1900's. Family tradition
2 CONC  in GA says that somewhere down this line, one Nix wife of VA was related to US Presidents John Adams, and John Quincy Adams.
2 CONT
2 CONT James left Barbados and sailed for New Kent, VA, and died soon after his son James was born there, (about 1665.) He was his only child. This son James had sons George and Edward, also born in VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/genealogy/Nix-Family-Tree-296
2 CONT
2 CONT James Nix (son of John Nix and Sarah Elizabeth Lewis) was born 1663 in St Petersparish, New Kent, Virginia, and died 1686 in New Kent, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Elizabeth Lewis on 1685 in Virginia, daughter of Hugh Lewis and Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT  More About James Nix: Date born 2: 20 Oct 1642, British West Indies, Barbados. Date born 3: 1656, Hanover, New Kent, Virginia. Died 2: 1687, New Kent, Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT More About James Nix and Elizabeth Lewis: Marriage 1: 1685, Virginia. Marriage 2: 1664, New Kent, Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of James Nix and Elizabeth Lewis are:
2 CONT
2 CONT  *  +Edward Nix, b. 07 Nov 1686, St. Peters Parrish, New Kent, Virginia478, d. 08 Oct 1776, Camden District, South Carolina478.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
