2 DATE 7 NOV 1686
2 ADDR
3 CITY St. Peter's Parish
3 STAE Virginia Colony
1 BURI
2 DATE OCT 1776
2 PLAC Union, South Carolina, United States
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 OCT 1776
2 ADDR
3 STAE South Carolina
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Generation No. 6
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Edward6 NIX (James (or John) (NICKES)5, John4, William3, Thomas2, Joseph Allen1) was born Nov 1686 in St Peters Parish, New Kent Co., VA, and died Oct 08, 1776 in Camden District, York Co., SC. He married Unice "Nice" GIBSON Ab
2 CONC t. 1711 in VA. She was born Abt. 1692 in New Kent, Hanover Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Edward NIX:
2 CONT
2 CONT WHO TO BELIEVE - WHAT TO BELIEVE!!!! Who has documentation!? Who can solve the mystery? Let's get this lineage right.
2 CONT
2 CONT I found some trees have Edward's parents as Samuel Jess Nix (b. 1703) and Nancy Sherman. Now doesn't this just make things really confusing? But you cannot dispute documentation and since there was a baptismal record and will, the
2 CONC  father of Edward AND the approximate year of birth and death leaves no questions or mystery. These trees have Edward being born in 1723 and being married to Unice Gibson being born in 1729. Where are these researchers getting the
2 CONC ir information/proof?
2 CONT
2 CONT From what I understand, in existence is a baptismal record which names James as the father of this Edward. There is record that a new parish was built next to his property. Edward's father-n-law had a will and in it mentions his d
2 CONC aughter, Nice who was Edward's wife. Edward left a will in 1776 (see below), which shows he died in SC. It clearly is in Camden District, SC. Some researchers show a different death location.
2 CONT
2 CONT Christening: 7 NOV 1686 
2 CONT
2 CONT alternate birth: 9 Aug 1728 - no way if someone has documentation that he was christened in 1686!!!
2 CONT
2 CONT alternate birth: 1723 - if believing his father was Samuel Jess Nix b. 1703
2 CONT
2 CONT alternate death: 24 JAN 1795 VA - although it is possible people live past 100 and this date is possible IF he was born in 1728. Being that his father was believed to be born in 1642, his father would have been 86 when Edward was 
2 CONC born (if going by the year 1728). I understand that many Nix descendants lived very long lives so it is very possible Edward fathered children when he was up there in age.
2 CONT
2 CONT *** Will information courtesy of Virginia with tree at rootsweb ***
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.choicemn.com/trees/gibson-tullis/1062.html 
2 CONT
2 CONT Will was filed in Charleston , SC will book 1774-79, p 418 (courtesy of Sharen Neal - tree at rootsweb)
2 CONT
2 CONT PROBATE RECORDS: WILL of Edward Nix of South Carolina, Camden District
2 CONT
2 CONT In the name of God Amen on this Eighth day of October 1776, I Edward Nix of the Province & District aforesaid being sick and weak in body but of perfect mind and memory thanks be to God, therefore calling unto mind the mortality o
2 CONC f my body, and knowing that it is appointed for all men once to die, do make and ordain this my last Will and Testament, that is to say principally and first of all. I give and recommend my Soul unto the hands of Almighty God that
2 CONC  gave it, and my body I recommend to the earth to be buried in a decent Christian manner at the discretion of my Executors, nothing doubting but at the general Resurrection I shall receive the same by the might power of God, and a
2 CONC s touching such worldly Estate where with it hath pleased God to bless me in this life I give demise and dispose of the same in the following manner and form.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item: I give and bequeath to my Grandson James Nix son of James Nix one shilling sterling.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item: I give and bequeath to my son Valentine Nix one shilling sterling.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item: I give and bequeath to my son George Nix one shilling sterling.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item: I give and bequeath to my daughter Sabra Lox one shilling sterling.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item: I give and bequeath to my daughter Francis Doss, one shilling sterling.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item: I give and bequeath to my Grandson Ambrose Nix one hundred and twenty five acres of land lying on the north side of Santee River in Camden District beginning on a marked hickory and running down the Santee River, for the com
2 CONC pliment of one hundred and twenty acres be the same more or less, it being part of a large track of Land granted by his Excellency Thomas Boone to Edward Nix.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item: I give and bequeath to my Grandson John Lyon and his heirs, after the death of my beloved wife my plantation whereon I now live, on the south side of Sandy River with all the Remaining part of my Land it being part of a larg
2 CONC er tract of Land granted by his Excellency Thomas Bonne, Esq., the 18th day of August 1763 to Edward Nix.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item: I give and bequeath to my Grandson John Lyon to him and his heirs the following negroes, Judy, Beck, Dick, and Mourning after the decease of my wife during her natural life, & after his decease, to be equally divided between
2 CONC  his two sons Elijah and Elisha.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item: I give to my Grandson John Lyon all the remaining part of my Stock of horses, hogs, and black cattle, household furniture, and plantation tools after paying my just debts funeral expenses, and Legacies.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item: I likewise constitute make and ordain my loving wife Unice Nix and John Lyon Executors of this my present Last will and Testament, & I do hereby utterly disallow, revoke, and disannul, all and every other former Testament, W
2 CONC ills, Legacies, and bequests, & Executors by me in any ways before mentioned willed of bequeathed, rectifying & confirming this and no other to be my Last Will and Testament. In witness whereof I have here unto set my hand and sea
2 CONC l the day & year first above written.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Nix His X (LS).
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed, Sealed, published pronounced & declared by the Edward Nix as his last will & Testament in presence of us the subscribers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wm. Farr, Richard Crosby, William Crosby
2 CONT
2 CONT *** Notes: In his will, he does not mention having a son named Ambrose - unless this son died before he did OR he just did not leave him anything. He does mention a grandson named Ambrose. He does not mention Phoebe unless she die
2 CONC d before he did OR he just did not leave her anything. He only mentions 5 children in his will. He does not mention Edward as a son. Either Edward died before he did OR he just did not leave him anything.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Unice "Nice" GIBSON:
2 CONT
2 CONT She is found in her father's will and her husband's will and her name is Nice and not Nero. It is believed with the handwriting technique back those days that her name may have appeared to be Nero. No documents have been located t
2 CONC o prove her name was Nero or contained the name Nero.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Edward NIX and Unice GIBSON:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: Abt. 1711, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Edward NIX and Unice GIBSON are:
2 CONT
2 CONT + 7 i. James "Jim"7 NIX, Sr., born Oct 20, 1758 in Hanover Co., VA; died Nov 21, 1845 in Harris Co., GA.
2 CONT
2 CONT + 8 ii. Ambrose I. NIX, born Bet. 1721 - 1726 in VA; died Abt. 1820 in Chester Co., SC.
2 CONT
2 CONT + 9 iii. Valentine NIX, born Nov 11, 1749 in Camden, York Co., SC; died Feb 10, 1826 in Pickens Co., SC.
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 iv. George Albert NIX, born Sep 04, 1754 in Camden, York Co., SC; died Abt. 1832 in York Co., SC. He married Margaret LYONS.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for George Albert NIX:
2 CONT
2 CONT George is mentioned in his father's will.
2 CONT
2 CONT Many researchers have his birth as 1754. They also have his father as Edward and mother as Unice Nero Gibson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT There are various trees either showing Edward being born 1686 or 1723, If Edward was born in 1686 and George was born in 1754, then Edward was 68 when George was born. I tend to doubt this. If Edward was born 1723 and George was b
2 CONC orn 1754, Edward was 31 when George was born. More realistic.
2 CONT
2 CONT I believe many trees have a missing generation. If the birth information is accurate for children supposedly belonging to Edward and Unice Gibson, with these children being born in the 1750's and Edward being born 1686, something 
2 CONC is wrong. I doubt these children beling to Edward and Unice. They may be grandchildren or Edward's yearof bith is wrong at being in 1686.
2 CONT
2 CONT If Edward was actually born in 1723, then his father would not have been James who was born in 1642. If Edward was born in 1723, this would mean his father James was 81 when he was born. I tend to not believe he fathered children 
2 CONC this late in life. If Edward was born in 1686 and his father was James, who was born in 1642, then James was 44 when he was born. I would tend to believe this.
2 CONT
2 CONT 11 v. Sabra (Sarah) Ann NIX, born Sep 19, 1755 in Camden, York Co., SC; died Feb 19, 1772 in Camden, York Co., SC. She married James LAX.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Sabra (Sarah) Ann NIX:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sabra is mentioned in her fath's will as Sabra Lox/Lax. Her mother would have been about 63 when she was born. Possible?
2 CONT
2 CONT 12 vi. Frances NIX, born Abt. 1720 in New Kent, Hanover Co., VA; died Abt. 1776 in Pittsylvania Co., VA. She married James DOSS, Sr. Abt. 1740 in Amelia Co., VA; born Abt. 1715 in New Kent, Hanover Co., VA; died May 1796 in Pittsy
2 CONC lvania Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Frances NIX:
2 CONT
2 CONT Frances/Francis is mentioned in her father's will as with last name of Doss.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About James DOSS and Frances NIX:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: Abt. 1740, Amelia Co., VA
2 CONT
2 CONT + 13 vii. Edward Olson NIX, born Abt. 1718 in Camden, York Co., SC; died Oct 15, 1816 in Twiggs Co, GA.
2 CONT
2 CONT 14 viii. Phoebe NIX, born Oct 17, 1747 in York Co., SC. She married Elisha LYON; born Abt. 1720 in MD.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Phoebe NIX:
2 CONT
2 CONT Phoebe IS NOT mentioned in Edward's will. She could have died before Edward died or he just did not leave her anything. She may not be the daughter of Edward            (Phoebe Nix Lyon preceded her father in death circa1760. Her 
2 CONC son, John Lyon, is mentioned prominently in his grandfather's will, and is named as an executor of the estate.  Cathy Culbertson 3/20/10)
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT NIX. Birth date is actually christening date. St. Peter's Par., New Kent Co. From informa t i on compliled by Wanda Gregory in "Doss Family Connection": In 1722, a chapel was ordered built at or near Edward Nix. In 1724, Nix paid 
2 CONC for fence raili n gs at the Allen's Creek church (Vestry book, St.Paul's Hanover). In 1731, Nix received a patent for 400 acres in Hanover, adjacent to Col. Meriweather, o n a b ranch of the Southanna River (Virginia. patent book 
2 CONC 14, p. 229) Will was filed in Charleston, South Carolina will book 1774-79, p 418. Record in the Par. registry. Edward y sone of James Nickes & Elizabeth his wife baptized y 7 day of Nov 1686 Married ca 1732 in New Kent or Hanover
2 CONC  Co., Virginia
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
