1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Martha Davis''' was born on July 14, 1702 in [Amherst County, Province of Virginia][SIC: Amherst was formed from Abermarle in 1761 so this is not possible.  She was “of” Hanover County.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha married [https://www.geni.com/profile-6589188 Abraham Venable] in 1723 in Hanover County, Virginia, United States. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-8122807 Abraham Venable]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-8311858 Hugh Lewis Venable]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-8311980 Charles Venable]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-38883421 Nathaniel Venable]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-8115179 James Venable]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-8312018 Anne King]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-34660587610 William Venable]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-36684532 Mary Moorman]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-59994007 Elizabeth Morton]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/profile-24178443 Capt. John Venable]; 
2 CONT # [https://www.geni.com/people/Martha-Shelby/6000000113055385095 Martha Shelby].
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on February 16, 1765 in Louisa County, Province of Virginia. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT William and Mary Quarterly. 247  https://archive.org/stream/jstor-1915563/1915563_djvu.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogy of the Venable Family, as Prepared by Nathaniel Venable, of Prince Edward County, Va„ Dated  December 25, 1790.  (Communicated by Joseph J. Casey.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT >Abraham Venable came from England into Virginia, U. S. A., and married the widow of John Nicks, who was the daughter of Lewis; left issue one son, Abraham Venable, who  was born 22d March, 1700, and who married '''Martha Davis,  
2 CONC daughter of Nathaniel Davis, of Hanover county. Left issue,  sons, Abraham,, Hugh Lewis, Charles, Nathaniel, James, William, and John,''' and daughters, '''Ann married to Phil King, of Cumberland county; Elizabeth married to Josia
2 CONC h Morton, of Charlotte county, and Mary married to Charles Moorman, of Louisa county.''' 
2 CONT '''''(Some sources add Martha who married Evan Shelby)''''''''
2 CONT '''
2 CONT http://dgmweb.net/FGS/V/VenableAbraham-MarthaDavis.html <broken link>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Wife:  Martha DAVIS 
2 CONT * Birth:  14/17 Jul 1702, Amherst Co., VA 
2 CONT * Death:  13 Jan 1765 or 18 Feb 1765, Louisa Co., VA 
2 CONT * Father:  '''Nathaniel DAVIS, a Quaker of Devonshire, England''' 
2 CONT * Mother?:  '''Mary Elizabeth HUGHES (c1650- )'''
2 CONT
2 CONT === Husband:  Abraham VENABLE II / Jr. 
2 CONT * Birth:  22 Mar 1699/1700, New Kent Co., VA 
2 CONT * Death:  12 Dec 1768, Louisa Co., VA 
2 CONT * Office:  Justice of the Peace, Hanover Co., VA 
2 CONT * Office:  Justice of the Peace and County Lieutenant, Louisa Co., VA 
2 CONT * Office:  Vestryman, Fredericksville Parish, [Louisa Co.,] VA  
2 CONT * Office:  1742-1756, Virginia House of Burgesses 
2 CONT * Historical:  friend and associate of Patrick HENRY 
2 CONT * Father:  Abraham VENABLE I 
2 CONT * Mother:  Elizabeth LEWIS
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT # Abraham B. VENABLE III, b. 9 Jan 1725, Louisa Co., VA 
2 CONT #Hugh Lewis VENABLE; m. Mary MARTIN, d/o William MARTIN of Albemarle Co., VA; issue: Nathaniel, John, Abraham, Martha w/o Ralph BANKS, Judith w/o William MOORMAN of Campbell Co., VA, Elizabth w/o Richard BRAGG of Fluvanna Co., VA,
2 CONC  Mary w/o John MOORMAN of Campbell Co., VA
2 CONT # Charles VENABLE; m. Elizabeth SMITH, d/o of Robert SMITH of Port Royal; issue: Robert h/o Sarah MADISON, d/o Henry MADISON of Charlotte Co., VA (his issue: Martha, Bettie, Pollie, Robert, James, Joseph), Charles, Mary w/o Robert
2 CONC  MARTIN of King & Queen Co., VA; Elizabeth w/o Massaniello WOMACK of Cumberland Co., VA; Sarah w/o Peyton GLENN of Prince Edward Co., VA, Martha w/o William BROWN of Charloote Co., VA; Ann w/o Daniel GLENN of Prince Edward Co., VA
2 CONC ; Dorothy w/o John GOODE of Charlotte Co., VA; Agnes, Nancy. 
2 CONT #Nathaniel VENABLE, b. 21 Oct 1733, Hanover Co., VA 
2 CONT #James VENABLE, b. 1734, Hanover Co., VA 
2 CONT #William VENABLE; m. Ann CLARK, d/o Isaac CLARK of Louisa Co., VA; issue: Abraham h/o Anne HUNDLY, d/o Wido Hundly of Caroline Co., VA (issue: Richard Hundly), William, James, Charles
2 CONT #John VENABLE; m. Agnes MOORMAN d/o Charles MOORMAN of Louisa Co., VA; issue: robert, Charles, Abraham, William, Nathaniel, Mary w/o Jacob VENABLE of Prince Edward Co., VA, Martha, Diana
2 CONT #Ann VENABLE; m. Phil KING of Cumberland Co., VA
2 CONT #Elizabeth VENABLE; m. Josiah MORTON of Charlotte Co., VA
2 CONT #Mary VENABLE; m. Charles MOORMAN of Louisa Co., VA
2 CONT # Martha VENABLE m. Evan Shelby.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Mary Elizabeth HUGHES Sex: F Note: ! Elizabeth m. Nathaniel Davis, a Welshman and early settler in the region. He made a large fortune by having choice river-bottom lands and trading with the Indians. Nathaniel and Elizabeth had 4
2 CONC  children: Robert Davis, ancestor of President Jefferson Davis who never publicly acknowledged his Indian heritage; Martha Davis who m. Abraham Venable; Abadiah (also called Abigail) Davis who m. William Floyd; Mary Davis who marr
2 CONC ied Samuel Burks. <Wrong--- Abadiah is a granddaughter, not daughter. See "the Dear Rush Letter.">
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/burke/1793/
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From the book Venables of Virginia by Elizabeth Marshall Venable-p. 19 Record of William Lewis Morton, son of Elizabeth Venable and Josiah Morton, concerning his family history. 
2 CONT Descendants as follows:
2 CONT * 1. Sara Davis married Thomas Bagby
2 CONT * 2.Rosanna Davis married Nathaniel Saunders
2 CONT * 3.Frances Davis married James Bagby
2 CONT * 4. Elizabeth Davis married John Bagby
2 CONT * 5. Abadiah Davis married Thomas Harding and John Gray
2 CONT * 6. Mary Davis married Thomas Banks
2 CONT * 7.Robert Davis had three wives, moved to St Mary's became rich,  and was killed by Indians.
2 CONT * 8.Isham Davis killed by Indians
2 CONT * 9. Nathaniel Davis killed by Indians
2 CONT * 10.John Davis killed by Indians
2 CONT * 11. '''Martha Davis married Abraham Venable''', my grand-father, son of Abraham Venable who came from England--Devonshire , who is of a numerous family in England.
