1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ID: I608702181 
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: John NIX 
2 CONT
2 CONT Given Name: John 
2 CONT
2 CONT Surname: Nix 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sex: M 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 20 May 1762 in Virginia/Union Co., S.C. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 12 Jan 1833 in Ga 
2 CONT
2 CONT Change Date: 31 May 2005 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Name Suffix: , Sr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Revolutionary War Veteran
2 CONT
2 CONT WFT Vol 1 #3897
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Joseph NIX b: Abt. 1736 in Union Co., S.C.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Sarah WINTERS b: in Union Co., S.C.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: in Franklin Co., Ga 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: _UID479A4283D1030C40A99B6C41D9EAB5578693
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT John was a Revolutionary War soldier. John was ambitious. He moved his family from VA to SC, thence to Franklin Co., GA. Some of the grown children stayed in Habersham Co. (the part that is now White Co.,) GA. Some of these went o
2 CONC n to help pioneer Union Co., GA, in the Appalachians. But Old John and Sarah moved on to MS for land opportunities, with their younger children. John left a sizeable estate and was considered a wealthy man. The Nix name stands pro
2 CONC ud in many parts of the US, though it seems tragic that a family would have cause to divide and live in distant lands from each other. Such were often the challenges and hardships that were required, in order to obtain livable lan
2 CONC ds and opportunities for economical survival.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT He is found in the Stewart county, GA 1850 census in his son, Larkin's household at age 81, which would make his birth year 1769, even though the headstone says 1760.
