1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Mary (Gibson) Brooks
2 CONT
2 CONT She was listed as the third daughter and as Mary Brook to whom she was bequeathed one shilling in her father's will of 1734.  She may have been born about 1700 because of information in the Ancestral File which shows she had a son
2 CONC  born about 1718 in Lunenburg Co., VA
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Brooks married Mary Gibson around 1705 in Virginia, USA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard and Mary had at least 5 children. (as mentioned as heirs in his Will)
2 CONT
2 CONT #     Robert Brooks 1705–1778.  Married Tabitha Hopkins.
2 CONT #     William Brooks 1710–1793.  
2 CONT #     Richard Brooks Jr 1712–  
2 CONT #     Sarah Brooks 1722–1765.  Married John Price.
2 CONT #     Massilva Marvula Brooks Hooper 1723–1800. Married Obediah Hooper.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Brooks is also seen as son of 1st wife Mary and born abt 1674.  See: https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Brooks-529
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT !PUBLIC RECORDS: Will of Thomas Gibson St. Martin's Parish Hanover County, Virginia Thomas Gibson's Will was found on p. 42 of the booklet by Rosalie Davis and page 151-152 of the original court record book.  See: "Barnabas Gibson
2 CONC  Family History" Compiled by Mrs. Dorothy G. Tuttle, 344 Saunders St., Murray, Utah 84107,  801-266-3443  19 Sep 1994.  See contents of Will on p. 1.  His 6 children are named. In fathers will, To my well beloved daughter Mary [Gi
2 CONC bson] Brook one shilling. 
2 CONT
