1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not Melungeon
2 CONT
2 CONT === Rev. Valentine Gibson
2 CONT *Born about Dec 1723 in Hanover, Virginia
2 CONT * Died 1800 in Stokes, North Carolina, United States
2 CONT * Son of Thomas Gibson and Mary 
2 CONT * Husband of Frances Elizabeth (Garrett) Gibson — married [date unknown] [location unknown]
2 CONT *Father of James Thomas Gibson Sr., Garrett Gibson I, Miles Ezekial Gibson, Archelous Gibson, Hannah (Gibson) Jackson and William Gibson
2 CONT === Biography  
2 CONT
2 CONT from Barnabas Gibson Family History; Compiled by Mrs. Dorothy G. Tuttle, 344 Saunders St. Murray, Utah 84107  801-266-3443  19 Sep 1994 p. 3 !
2 CONT
2 CONT PUBLIC RECORDS: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Valentine and Elizabeth moved to Halifax Co., VA before 1762 as that is when they owned land on Cascade Creek. p. 289 New entry Book halifax Co., & Pittsylvania Co., VA.  FHL # 975.5665 R2C & Film 33325 Pt 2.) Various Tax lists an
2 CONC d Polls showing Valentine on p. 3 of above book source. 1766 Pittsylvania Co. was formed from Halifax Co. , Valentine is now living in Pittsylvania Co., VA
2 CONT
2 CONT Valentine Gibson was the son of Thomas Gibson of Hanover Co., VA. (Will proved 7 Nov 1734). he must have been a minor when his father died as his sister and bro-in-law Edward nicks were left a legacy in order to bring up "my child
2 CONC ren John Gibson, Valentine Gibson and also William Robertson." 
2 CONT
2 CONT A land record dated 2 Oct 1794 proves Valentine to be the father of James Gibson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT CENSUS: 1790  for Stokes Co. One male oover 16 and 1 under 16 and 2 females 1800 Stokes Co. 1 male under 10, 1 under 16, 1 under 26 and he is over age 45; 2 females under 10, 1 under 26, 1 under 45 and 1 over 45. (Because of lack 
2 CONC of proof of the names of Valentine & Elizabeth's children, a list of possible children has been prepared using deeds and other records. The same Gibson men are always living close by each other when they moved from place to place)
2 CONC . [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/5058/images/4440913_00313?pId=198737 AncestryImage]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/KNNF-1GP
2 CONT * Believed to be a Melungeon.  Listed as a "FPC" (Free Person of Color) on the 1790 and 1800 North Carolina Census Records NOTE:  I have not located these listings as of 1 Jan 2012
2 CONT *Pittsylvania County, Virginia Deed Book 7, Page 25-Valentine Gibson sells land.
2 CONT *Hanover County, Virginia Will of Thomas Gibson dated 7 November 1734, father of Valentine Gibson
2 CONT *Archibald Gibson (unknown-1855); Find A Grave
2 CONT *Legacy NFS Source: Archibald Gibson - Government record: Probate record or will: race: Melungeon.  Listed as a Free Person of Color in 1790 and 1800 Federal Census; 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Citations 
2 CONT * Year: 1790; Census Place: Stokes, North Carolina; Series: M637; Roll: 7; Page: 541; Image: 313; Family History Library Film: 0568147
2 CONT * Year: 1800; Census Place: Salisbury, Stokes, North Carolina; Series: M32; Roll: 32; Page: 554; Image: 561; Family History Library Film: 337908
