1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT It has been stated that his wife died in childbirth. She may not be his correct wife 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Generation Four     http://sites.rootsweb.com/~richmond/ancestors/lyons001.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Elisha4 Lyon (Peter3, John2, John1)2 was born in 1720 in Dorchester Co., MD.2,1 He married Phoebe Nix.1 He married Mary Bailey.2  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Inventory of his estate was compiled by John Smith, Peter Holland, John Divers, and Daniel Ward:
2 CONT
2 CONT Six slaves (three women, two boys, and a girl), two horses, twelve head of cattle, two sheep, four beds, two tables, two chests, two trunks, a gun, and the usual farm equipment. He appeared on the census of 1786 in Franklin Co., V
2 CONC A; Personal Property Tax List - No. of Tithes - 4; Whites over 21 - 1; Whites under 21 - 0; Slaves over 16 - 3; Slaves under 16 - 4; Horses - 3; Cattle- 16.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Elisha4 Lyon and Phoebe Nix were as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT i. Mary5.1
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. John.1
2 CONT
2 CONT iii. Edward.1
2 CONT
2 CONT iv. Elizabeth.1
2 CONT
2 CONT v. Gutridge1 was born in 1748 in VA.1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Elisha4 Lyon and Mary Bailey were as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT i. Elijah5.1
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. Fanny.1
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. iii. Elisha Jr., born 1772; married Rhoda (Roda) Hatcher.
2 CONT
2 CONT iv. William.1
