1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for SOUTH CAROLINA (Soldier).  [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A083864  DAR Ancestor # A083864]
2 CONT
2 CONT John was one of eight children, and one of two sons, of Ambrose and Hannah Nix. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John enlisted and served with several units of the South Carolina Continental State Troops. His initial assignment was with Captain Davis's company of Richard Win's Regiment. He is also recorded as serving under Capt. Thomas Baker
2 CONC . He participated in the Surrender of Orangeburg (May 10-11, 1781) and the Battle of Eutaw Springs (September 8, 1781).
2 CONT
2 CONT John was married to Winnifred [?] in 1782. John and Winnifred had the following children: Margaret Alexander, Jessie P. Nix, Temple Nix, David Nix, Nancy Barnett, William Nix, Elsie Cook, Ambrose Nix, Susannah Taylor, Ephraim Nix,
2 CONC  Hannah Courtney, Elias Nix, and John Nix.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   Winnifred Nix (1764 - 1821)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children:
2 CONT   Ambrose Nix (1792 - 1860)*
2 CONT   Sarah Ann Nix Peters (1793 - 1872)*
2 CONT   David Nix (1794 - 1849)*
2 CONT   Elias Nix (1803 - 1851)*
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Nix-Judy Cemetery Pioneer Cemetery  Madison County Illinois, USA
