0 @I387949699810002915@ INDI
1 NAME Robert ‘the Black’ /Davis/
2 GIVN Robert ‘the Black’
2 SURN Davis
2 _MARNM Davis
2 NICK The Black Davis
2 NICK Nathaniel Davis
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1680
2 PLAC Hanover County, Virginia
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 5 SEP 1771
2 ADDR
3 CITY Natchez
3 STAE Luisiana
3 CTRY Reino de Nueva España
1 OCCU fur trader
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Also seen as Robert Davis of St Mary’s or Nathaniel Robert Davis, II.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Said to be children of https://www.geni.com/people/Nathaniel-Davis-of-Hanover/6000000000890121115?through=6000000020839922073:
2 CONT
2 CONT > Ref: Mary Elizabeth HUGHES Sex: F Note: ! Elizabeth m. Nathaniel Davis, a Welshman and early settler in the region. He made a large fortune by having choice river-bottom lands and trading with the Indians. Nathaniel and Elizabet
2 CONC h had 4 children: Robert Davis, ancestor of President Jefferson Davis who never publicly acknowledged his Indian heritage; Martha Davis who m. Abraham Venable; Abadiah (also called Abigail) Davis who m. William Floyd; Mary Davis w
2 CONC ho married Samuel Burks.  (https://www.geni.com/people/Abadiah-Floyd/6000000000891879821 who married https://www.geni.com/people/Col-William-Floyd/6000000010155557246?through=6000000000891879821 seems of a later generation - a dau
2 CONC ghter of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Davis/387949699810002915?through=6000000000891879821)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT King William Co. formed 1701 from King & Queen Co., VA (which formed from New Kent County in 1691).
2 CONT
2 CONT Amherst Co. formed 1761 from Albemarle Co., VA
2 CONT
2 CONT “We are not certain where Robert was born, though some say King William County, Virginia and believe Nathaniel was his father; he names his first son Nathaniel.” -- “Anna Cartlidge notes that Robert, having lost his land in Amhers
2 CONC t Co., Va. In a disputed filing by a Nicholas Davies, removed to Nachez, Miss. (then a part of Ga.), by July, 1759, where ‘. . .we find him in Georgia with his wife, five children, and thirteen slaves, petitioned for a grant on th
2 CONC e south side of the Sapala River known by the name of Cedar Point.’ 
2 CONT
2 CONT Those in his will to whom he leaves money are the children who remained east. . .His will was dated September 5th, 1771, and it was proved in 1773. (or 1790). Caraol Seales notes that we have no proof of these wives, except Grace 
2 CONC who is named in his will.” -- per Carol Seales, email dated January 2002: “. . .he married 3 times, so the span in the children’s birthdates would be wide. He acquired a large amount of land in Amherst county, but failed to patent
2 CONC  it correctly. Nicholas Davies came along and entered the patents on Robert Davis’ land and because it was not properly patented before, the court awarded all of Roberts land to Nicholas. My guess is that this made Robert so angry
2 CONC , he left for the territories. . .After Robert lost his large acreage in VA, he and his 3rd wife Grace with their sons Lewis, Landon and Hugh moved to the Southern Territory. Many entries can be found in the Natchez court records,
2 CONC  but also in the Georgia Records and sometimes sources state Florida. The documents list such rivers as Thompson Creek and the Homochitto River.” 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Stevens, Marshall, Mitchell, Washington and other Families, Pat M. Stevens IV, RootsWeb World Connect Project database)
2 CONT
2 CONT -
2 CONT
2 CONT “The Davis Family continued to be fur traders until about 1750. One fur station is thought to be one mile above the Otter Creek. In 1753, Robert Davis and his family stopped fur trading for plantation life. Robert built a plantati
2 CONC on above the Lawrence Creek (Otter). However, Robert lost this plantation to Nicholas Davies because he had neglected to get a proper title for this property. It was around 1750 that Nicholas Davies came into this peaceful settlem
2 CONC ent with land grants. These land grants caused Robert Davis and Nicholas Davies to quarrel over who had a right to this land. However, since land grants were recognized over squatter rights, Robert had to leave the county. He move
2 CONC d to. . .Natchez on the Mississippi, then part of West Florida.” 
2 CONT
2 CONT (The Stevens and Allied Families in America Since 1600s, Pat Stevens, Family Tree Maker On-line database)
2 CONT
2 CONT -
2 CONT
2 CONT “Court records in Natchez -- Court Book E, p 237, 5 Feb 1791 (Galveztown) -- concerning and estate argument between Martha Davis Foley and her former husband’s brothers show that -- 
2 CONT *Grace, widow of Robert Davis, died in the year 1784. . .
2 CONT *Martha, widow of (1) Lewis Davis, married a (2) Foley). . .-- 
2 CONT *Lewis, Landon, and Hugh Davis have made a settlement. . .on June 12, 1790 in Galveztown on the estate of their father. (editor -- confusing in the papers because Lewis died before his mother, as is noted elsewhere. . .).” 
2 CONT
2 CONT (The Stevens and Allied Families in America Since 1600s, Pat Stevens, Family Tree Maker On-line database)
2 CONT
2 CONT -
2 CONT
2 CONT Will: 5 Sept 1771, Adams County (Natchez), MS: “I Robert Davis of the Province of Georgia” 
2 CONT
2 CONT -- wife Grace 
2 CONT
2 CONT -- sons: 
2 CONT *Nathaniel; 
2 CONT *Isom; 
2 CONT *Robert; 
2 CONT *Lewis; 
2 CONT *Landon; 
2 CONT *Hugh 
2 CONT
2 CONT -- daughters: 
2 CONT *Obediah Floyd; 
2 CONT *Sarah ---rks; 
2 CONT *Elizabeth Sexton 
2 CONT
2 CONT -- “In Natchez whereof I have set my hand and seal the fifth day of September in the year of our Lord one thousand Seven hundred and Seventy One.”
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.ourfamtree.org/browse.php?pid=90805
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/lewis/8002/
2 CONT
2 CONT By Laura Lewis September 20, 2000 at 10:56:53 In reply to: Abadaih Lewis of VA 9/10/00
2 CONT
2 CONT After checking my husband's notes, I think the Abadiah Lewis you're referring to was the mother of your Robert Davis, not his wife. She appears to have been a daughter of Hugh Lewis, Jr., and Nicketti, who was a daughter of Chief 
2 CONC Opechancanough, Powhatan's brother or half-brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abadiah Lewis married Nathaniel Davis, and they were parents of Robert Davis. It's not clear whether Robert was born in Wales, England or Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT A note on this family I found (I just have my husband's earlier notes on hand) shows that Hugh Lewis, Nathaniel Davis and "Obadiah" Davis were transported to King & Queen County, VA, in 1717.This Hugh Lewis was apparently not the 
2 CONC much older "Capt." Hugh Lewis some researchers assume, and Jay's evidence for that is too detailed to include here.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel Davis and Abadiah Lewis had children:
2 CONT
2 CONT #Robert Davis (your ancestor?)
2 CONT #Mary Davis (m. Samuel Burks)
2 CONT #Martha Davis (m. Abraham Venable)
2 CONT #Abadiah Davis (m. William Floyd)
2 CONT
2 CONT The most updated information I have on the man who appears to be "your" Robert Davis (courtesy of my husband's old notes - which may well have been updated since) is this:
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Davis was an Indian trader and one of the first settlers of Amherst Co., VA. He left the area in 1752 for North Carolina, and then moved to Georgia. His will of 1771 was found in Georgia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Davis married (1st) Elizabeth Hughes and had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Nathaniel Davis (m. Elizabeth Atkins)- these are my husband's ancestors
2 CONT # Isham Davis
2 CONT # Robert Davis
2 CONT # John Davis (not mentioned in his will)
2 CONT # Abadiah Davis (m. William Floyd)
2 CONT # Sarah Davis (m. Burks)
2 CONT # Elizabeth (m. Sexton)
2 CONT
2 CONT He married (2nd) Anna Atkins. Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Absolum Davis
2 CONT
2 CONT He married (3rd) to Grace (unknown).  Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Landon Davis
2 CONT # Lewis Davis
2 CONT # Hugh Davis
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/lewis/8009/
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Davis (called The Black Davis)who married Abadiah Lewis who was his first wife and had children: Susannah who married David Cox; Martha (sometimes seen as Hannah) married Abraham B. Venable- some books have Martha as the da
2 CONC ughter of Nathaniel Davis and Elizabeth Hughes); Isham(Isom); James married Jane Black; Robert married Jane Jopling; John; Abadiah (Abby) married William Floyd (some books have Abadiah as daughter of Nathaniel Davis and Elizabeth 
2 CONC Hughes); Elizabeth married Unknown Sexton; Nathaniel married Elizabeth Atkins (who is the sister of his stepmother Anna Atkins); Evan married Mary E. Williams.
2 CONT
2 CONT Second wife was Anna Atkins - they had a son Absolom - she may have died in childbirth or shortly thereafter.
2 CONT
2 CONT His third wife was Grace Unknown - they had children Lewis, Landon, and Hugh.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Davis died in Natchez, Georgia which is now Mississippi.I have his will in my notes.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Summary:
2 CONT Robert Davis wrote his will on 5 September 1771.  He named his wife, GRACE, and his children:
2 CONT (1) Lewis Davis
2 CONT (2) Landon Davis
2 CONT (3) Hugh Davis (described as under 20 years old in 1771)
2 CONT (4) Nathaniel Davis
2 CONT (5) Isom Davis
2 CONT (6) Robert Davis
2 CONT (7) Abediah [Davis] Floyd
2 CONT (8) Sarah [Davis] Burks
2 CONT (9) Elizabeth [Davis] Sexton
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Davis was likely married twice, possibly three times.  His first wife may have been the mother of his older children.  His wife at the time of his death was GRACE, and she was probably the mother of his younger children, in
2 CONC cluding HUGH. 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/L1WL-N67
