2 CONT #WikiTree contributors, "Richard Brooks II (abt.1675-1734)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Brooks-528 : accessed 02 February 2025).
2 CONT ##     Last Will and Testament, From microfilm projections in Salt Lake City Library obtained by Robert C Kelly of Camarillo, CA, from book 13, Lunenburg County Virginia Wills page 536.  
2 CONT ##     Inventory of Estate of Richard Brooks done by the executors of his will. Found in the Hanover County Virginia court records 1734-1735, page 567  
2 CONT ##     Vestry Book of St Pauls Parish - Hanover Virginia 1706-1786, page 266 (image #287). Entry for Richard Brookes regarding the processing of his lands. 8 Feb 1719  
2 CONT ##     Vestry Book of St Pauls Parish - Hanover Virginia 1706-1786, page 225. Entry for Richard Brooks Land Processing  
2 CONT ##     Vestry Book of St Pauls Parish - Hanover Virginia 1706-1786 page 237.  
2 CONT ##     Vestry Book of St Pauls Parish - Hanover Virginia 1706-1786 page 42. List of Parish creditors that the Vestry has paid this year.  
2 CONT ##     Vestry Book of St Pauls Parish - Hanover Virginia 1706-1786 page 36. Annual Vestry meeting to settle accounts. Jonathan White is to receive 15 C:C on the account of Richard Brooks  
2 CONT ##     Excerpt from the William and Mary Quarterly dated July 1912. This volume has the records from Hanover County court. The records are from only two books of records that still exist today. The dates run from 1734-1735. Page 5
2 CONC 3 has the entry for the Will of Richard Brookes  
2 CONT # https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/L6Y3-T1Z
2 CONT # https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/9V3Y-NSN
2 CONT # JOURNAL OF GENTRY GENEALOGY, Vol.1, Issue 8. (August 2001).  Revised and updated to Part 1, Samuel Gentry II with focus on his son, NICHOLAS III, the younger, and his family and other sons. < [https://web.archive.org/web/2023032
2 CONC 8043338/https://gentryjournal.org/archives/jgg0108.htm link] > "Nicholas Gentry - Born about 1717 in Hanover County, Virginia, in the vicinity of Stone Horse Creek. Married about 1743, Louisa County, Virginia, to Mary Brooks, daug
2 CONC hter of Richard and Elizabeth Brooks. Nicholas died about 1800, Surry County, North Carolina.  Nicholas III married Mary Brooks, daughter of Richard Brooks, and their 7 children were: Nicholas IV, Samuel, Allen IV, Arthur, Agnes, 
2 CONC Jane, John. This Nicholas was married to Mary Brooks, not Nicholas II, son of Nicholas I. These two are often confused and lived in Louisa County at the same time, but they were of different generations and of different fathers. N
2 CONC icholas III was referred to as "the younger" to differentiate him from his older cousin, who was actually a "junior" as son of the senior immigrant. Nicholas II, junior, was married to Jane B...(?) Later deed records substantiate 
2 CONC that it was Nicholas III that was married to Mary Brooks. There were close ties between the two families with multiple inter-marriages; the Brooks family had multiple Sarah's and Mary's, just to confuse issues further."
2 CONT # https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LTPM-216
