1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Ref: [http://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-1/myheritage-family-trees?itemId=196575801-5-667&action=showRecord MH Family Tree record] - a number of court cases recorded involving John Doss.
2 CONT  _______________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Author: LibbieGriffin3 http://boards.rootsweb.com/surnames.doss/1172.2/mb.ashx 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Christ Church Parish Register, Middlesex Co., Va. (Referred to here as "CCPR")'''
2 CONT
2 CONT CCPR lists "Thomas Doss ye Sone of John & Ann Doss bapt. at ye lower Chapel 9th January 1686" (p.30) and repeated on page 33. [note: this is not a record of his birth, only his christening.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Doss Sr. appears to have lived in Essex Co. Va. by 1723 when he first appears in the records of the court:
2 CONT  "1723: Essex Co. Order Bk. 1723-25 Pt. 1, Sparacio, pp. 59-60: Case of John Boulware Jr. by Joseph Leemon v. John Hawkins & Grace Hawkins, exrs. of Samuel Stallord, dec'd, who was the exec. of John Boulware [Sr.]. See John Boulwa
2 CONC re Jr. Thomas Doss [sic] paid for his attendance 23 days on behalf of Boulware/Leemon. James Allen also paid for 30 days; Elizabeth Wheeton for 14 days; John Mosely paid for 9 days. 17 March 1723." This indicates that Thomas was p
2 CONC aid for 23 days attendance at the court house to give testimony in this case.
2 CONT
2 CONT We have only one indication of who Thomas Doss Sr.'s wife might be, found in this record:
2 CONT  Essex Co. Order Book 1725-1729 (Part 2), Sparacio, pp. 56-58, from original book pp. 250, 251, 251a, 252, several lawsuits involving (1) Silvester Pattie v. William Ramsey; Silvester Pattie v. James Landram, Nathaniel Conduit & h
2 CONC is wife Susanna v. William Ramsay. Thomas Dorse and Margaret Dorse were paid for two days attendance to testify on behalf of James Landram Junr. Other witnesses listed in various cases were (Pattie's witnesses) Augustine Atherton 
2 CONC (traveled 27 miles); Winifred Atkinson, Mary Short; Ramsey's witnesses: Daniel Noel Junr.; James Landram's witnesses: Thomas and Margaret Dorse, Mary Short; Nathaniel Conduit's witnesses: Abigail Bradshaw, Andrew Phillips who came
2 CONC  27 miles from Caroline Co. [In this record the name Doss is written as it's often pronounced in Virginia, "Dorse." We have many records where the name is misspelled in that way. Thomas's son James knew well a family with the some
2 CONC what unusual surname of "Patty" which may add credence to my belief that this is in fact "our" Thomas Doss and that a woman named Margaret was his wife at the time this record was created."
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/collection-40001/familysearch-family-tree?itemId=1011695045&action=showRecord FamilySearch Family Tree] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 23 2016, 1
2 CONC 9:07:26 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LK9Z-V8L FamilySearch Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 22 2019, 19:19:34 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Baptism date Jan 9 1686 Son of John and Ann Doss at the lower Chapel. He married Sarah Margaret Herring: born about 1685 - 1743. They married about 1714 per the records 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Doss-86
