1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://todmar.net/ancestry/patty_jessepaty1744.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Jesse Paty
2 CONT (Abt. 1744 in Brunswick Co., VA - Nov 9, 1795 in Union Co., SC)
2 CONT Son of James Paty (c1705-1758) and Sarah Clanton (1721-1759)
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Delilah (1752-1796) in 1765 in Amelia, VA
2 CONT (note: Delilah's last name of Doss is unproven - see Wkitree page)
2 CONT
2 CONT See site for more
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT 26. i. Jesse5 PATY married Sarah Sallie West, daughter of Joseph West and Jane Owen, at Never married. He was born in 1744/45 at Brunswick Co, VA. He married Delilah Doss, daughter of James Doss and Frances Nix, circa 1763 at VA. 
2 CONC He died after 9 November 1795 at Union Co, SC. ·       Reference: 160. He A Jesse Paty served in the Bedford County, Virginia Militia in Sept , 1758. Jesse was then about fifteen, if his dates are right. *6 Mar 1767 Jesse received
2 CONC  400 acres on Beach Tree Creek, adjacent t o James Paty on North side. (ref ltr. Corinne H Diller) *June 1767 Jesse listed with tithables taken. (Ref Hisroty of Pittsylv anis Co VA pg 289) *1768 James Paty of Berkely Co SC gave Je
2 CONC sse Paty of Pittsylvania Co , Va. power of Atty. to sell land left 'by the will of James Paty'. *Jesse is listed on both the Virginia and South Carolina census, thi s happened because he was still living in Virginia, but had alrea
2 CONC dy bought lan d in South Carolina, and was preparing to move his family there. I do not know t he exact date Jesse made this move. Jesse was still buying land in Virginia i n 1771. James Doss, father of Jesse's wife Delilah, bough
2 CONC t land next to Jess e in 1783. But Jesse had sold land on Pateys Creek by 1791 to Benjamin Canafax. This does not mean he had to be still living in Virginia. Je sse had bought land in South Carolina in 1788, and could have moved t
2 CONC  here, while still owning land in Virginia. He was living in South Car olina when he died in late 1795, early 1796. *Union Dist: SC, Book A, page 94. Indenture 21 June 1788 between George McWhorter and Jesse Patty of Un ion County
2 CONC , South Carolina, McWhorter for 150 pounds sells Patty land o n west side Broad River by McKissicks line also part of two other tra cts formerly laid for James Love and Henry Clark of 31 acres and in t he whole 231 acres. *Wit: Jo
2 CONC hn McWhorter; George McWhorter; and Elizabeth McWhorter. Recor ded 23 June 1788. *Copy of Jesse Patty's will is on record in the Union County Courthous e. I have a copy. DCL *Good Source books: Virginia Colonial Militia By William
2 CONC  Armstrong Crozier. List of the Colonial Soldiers of Virginia By H.J. Eckenrode and Colo nial. Colonial Solders of the South 1732-1774 by Murtie June Clark. *. ·       
