2 CONT =Peter Lyon (1700 - abt. 1764)
2 CONT =
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Lyon
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1700 in Dorchester, Maryland
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of John Lyon and [mother unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of John Lyon Sr. [half]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Margaret Unknown — married [date unknown] [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Elisha Lyon, Peter Lyon and Elisha Lyon Sr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died about May 1764 in Albemarle, Colony of Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter was born in 1700 in Dorchester, Maryland, USA. He was the son of John Lyon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter died at the age of about 64 in 1764 in Albemarle, Virginia, USA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Peter Lyon, Sr.[1]
2 CONT Written: 4 September 1760 Probated: May Court, 1764 Wife Margaret Lyon to receive one-third of estate. Son Peter to have plantation where he now lives. Son Nicholas to have 150 acres of land. Daughter Elizabeth Bealey (wife of Joh
2 CONC n) to have tract of land. Exrs: sons Peter and Nicholas Lyon and George Blane. Wit: Alexander Blane, Hannah Blane and George Blane.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ King, J. Estelle Stewart. 1940. Abstracts of wills, inventories, and administration accounts of Albemarle County, Virginia (1748-1800), Amherst County, Virginia (1761-1800). Beverly Hills, Calif: J.E.S. King.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Generation Three
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Peter3 Lyon (John2, John1)1 was born between 1698 and 1701 in Dorchester Co., MD.1 He married Margaret (--?--).1 He died in 1764 in Albemarle Co., VA.1
2 CONT
2 CONT He left a will; 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Name of God Amen this Fourth Day of September one thousand seven Hundred & sixty: I Petter Lyon Sen. Of the county of Albemarle & Parish of St. Ann being sick in Body but of good & perfect Memory thanks be to almighty God &
2 CONC  Calling to Remembrance e uncertain State of this Transitarry Life & that all Flesh must yield unto death when it shall Please God to Call; Do make Constitute ordain & declare this my last will and Testament in Manner & Form Follo
2 CONC wing Revokeing & Annulling by these presents al & every Testament & Testaments, Will & Wills heretofore by me made & declared either by word or writing & this is to be taken only for my Last Will & Testament & none other now for y
2 CONC e Selling of my temporal Estate & Goods & Chattles & Debts as hath ple ed God for above my Desire? To bestow upon me I do order give & Dispose the same in manner and Form Following, (that is to say) First I will that all these Deb
2 CONC ts & dues as I owe in right? or account by my Death or Funeral shall be paid or ordered to be id within Convenient time after my Decease by my Executors hereafter named: First I give & bequeath unto my Loveing wife Margret Lyon he
2 CONC r thirds of all my Estate Real & personal & that she shall have one Cow taken off the Holl for Repairing her House she now lives in & the Remainder of the said Cows price to her use, Together w h her Bed & Household Furniture she 
2 CONC now poseseth such as her & hert pot pan & putter; & further that my son Petter Lyon shall be obligest to find his Mother wood for firing and yt. Sufficiently & fall Dureing her Lifetime if not Ten Shilling in Lew the of yearly & S
2 CONC on Nicholas shall be obliged for his part to find his Mother yearly three Barrels of Corn & both of them equally shall be obliged to find her yearly a Sufficient Quantity of meat. & next I give & bequeath unto my Loveing son Pette
2 CONC r Lyon th Plantation where he now Liveth, Together with one Hundred Acres of Land now in his posesion Together with ye orchard & fields according to a Division made before Alexander Blane & John Lyon Elisha Lyon between the said P
2 CONC etter Lyon & Nicholas Lyon Togeth with all Movables? Now in his posesion & thirdly I give & bequeath unto my Loveing son Nicholas Lyon one Hundred &
2 CONT
2 CONT Fifty acres of Land Lying along ye Mountain now in his posesion with Houses, orchards fields Together with such part of the Movables? as e hath in posesion & fourthly I give & bequeath unto my Daughter Elizabeth Bealy wife to John
2 CONC  Bealey a certain Tract or parcel of Land Supposed to be Fifty Acres of Land Lying along Alexander Blanes line & Joyning Millers line upon ye Creek Runing Down the Mouth of the Spring Branch Corners upon a poplar thence to the Hea
2 CONC d of the Spring which lyeth between both plantations thence up ye Road Road to Nicholas & Joyn his Line now in the posesion of the Said Elizabeth & John Bealy for & Dureing the said lizabeth Bealey Life & John Bealy Widdowhood & a
2 CONC fter the Experation of ye aforesaid time the said Tract or parsal of Land Given unto the Elizabeth
2 CONT
2 CONT Bailey & John Bailey is to be returned unto Peter Lyon or his Heirs with all its Improvements Cleer & free f all Debts & Incumbrances and further I will that my Stock & other Materals should be equally Devided into three Equal Par
2 CONC ts that is to say Between my two Sons & my wife and lastly I will yt. If the said Nicholas Lyon should Dye without an Heir Lawfull begotten of his own Body that ye said Petter Lyon Bro to Nicholas Lyon shall be Heir of all his Rea
2 CONC l Estate: I do hereby constitute & ordain Petter Lyon Nicholas Lyon & George Blane for my Executors In Witness hereof I have hereunto set my Hand & Seal t Day & Year above written.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Lyon his Mark (a "P&L" in a "logo")
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed Sealed & Delivered In the presence of us* Alexander Blane (his) Hannah H. Blane (mark) George Blane
2 CONT
2 CONT At Albemarle May Court 1764 This Will was proved by the Oaths of Alexander Blane & Hannah Blane two of the Witnesses thereto & ordered to be recorded
2 CONT
2 CONT And at a Court held for Albemarle County the Eleventh Day of October 1764
2 CONT
2 CONT On the Motion of Peter Lyon & Nicholas Lyon who made oath according to Law
2 CONT
2 CONT Certificate is granted them for obtaining probat of the said Will in due from Given Security which they with John Lyon there Security entered into & acknowledged their Bond accordingly.
2 CONT
2 CONT Test.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Nicholas, Clerk.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Peter3 Lyon and Margaret (--?--) were as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT i. Philadelphia4.1
2 CONT
2 CONT ii. John.1
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. iii. Elisha, born 1720 in Dorchester Co., MD; married Phoebe Nix; married Mary Bailey.
2 CONT
2 CONT iv. Elizabeth1 was born circa 1741 in Dorchester Co., MD.1 She married John Bailey.1
2 CONT
2 CONT v. Nicholas1 was born circa 1745 in Dorchester Co., MD.1 He married Martha (--?--).1
2 CONT
2 CONT vi. Peter1 was born in 1750 in Dorchester Co., MD.1 He died in 1820 in Albemarle Co., VA.
