1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/greer/3395/
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Joseph and Fanny, 1786-1823 By Ronald Couch May 05, 2003 at 09:10:15
2 CONT
2 CONT Alright, people!Prove this wrong!!
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Greer, Jr. was born about 1762 in Bedford County, Virginia.He was married to Fanny Lyon, daughter of Elisha Lyon and Mary Bailey, on May 1, 1786.She was born in 1771.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:"Joseph Greer ... issue 23 children." (Dates and other information about the family and descendants of Joseph Greer, Jr. were taken from a genealogical chart by Richard L. Greer, Marion, Virginia, 1985.) (NOTE FROM RALPH TERR
2 CONC Y: Joseph is said to have 23 children, but Richard lists only one, with his children. This chart is hard to understand in places and this is one of those places, so there could be some error in reading this chart.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:Information about the children of this couple is extremely difficult to discover.Thomas Jefferson Greer, son of Madison Shelby Greer, insisted that Madison’s parents had “only” seventeen children.Whatever the number, the fami
2 CONC ly was known to have been overwhelmed by a cruel and malicious stork, and many of their children were given to other families to rear.In this way, we believe, Madison came to be a part of the family of Charlotte Greer and James Jo
2 CONC nes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Joseph Greer and Fanny Lyon are:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Alexander Greer, born 1810, Virginia; in Missouri before 1840, married Virginia, born 1820, Maryland; Children all born Missouri:Mary R., Laura A., Marian R., Sarah F., Robert L., and Joseph W.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Greenberry Greer, 1813, Virginia, married Nancy, 1812, Kentucky; Children all born Missouri: James L., 1838, Mary F., 1840, Edward C., 1843, and Ben Leo, 1846
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Harrison W. Greer, 1818, Tennessee, married Dorinda H., Tennessee; Children born Tennessee:Wm. M., 1842, Mary C.. 1844, Sarah M., 1846, and Susan E., 1849, born Missouri
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.. James Greer, 1815, Virginia, married Martha, 1817, Virginia; Children all born Missouri:Mary A., 1848
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Peter B. Greer, 1808, Virginia, married Mary A., 1809, Virginia; Children:Judith F., 1833, Virginia, Charles, 1836, Missouri, Catherine A., 1838, Missouri, Euphemia, 1841, Missouri
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Samuel Greer, 1800, Virginia, Children:Joseph Greer, 1823, Virginia, Serafina, 1830, Virginia; Moses, 1833, Virginia, Frances (F) 1837, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. William Greer, 1805, Virginia, married Anna, 1805, Tenessee; Children all born Missouri:Maryann, 1834, Nancy E. 1839, Precilla F. 1842, Eliza T., 1844, Charlotte, 1846
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. Nathan Greer, 1811, Virginia, married Elizabeth E., 1817, Virginia; Children:Jemima F. 1837, Charles N. 1839, James L. 1841, Mary J. 1845, Elizabeth A. 1849, Missouri
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. Thomas Greer, 1816, Tennessee (Baptist clergyman in Missouri by 1834), married Nancy, 1815, Kentucky; Children all born Missouri:James, 1835, Elizabeth 1837, William, 1835, Jesse, 1841, Nancy 1844, Patrick, 1845, Martha, 1847, 
2 CONC Oliver, 1849
2 CONT
2 CONT 10. Garrett Greer, 1820, Tennessee, married Martha J., 1824, Alabama; Children:Wm. V., 1842, Martha L., 1845. Malinda J. S., 1847. David P., 1850, Rosana, 1851, Amanda 1854, Samuel H. E., 1856 and Milissa C., 1859.All Children bor
2 CONC n in Arkansas.Also in Household:Elizabeth C. Beller, 1834, Albert Beller, 1856, James J. C. Beller, 1848 and Garrett G. Beller,1850
2 CONT
2 CONT 11. Madison Shelby Greer, born January 13, 1823, Tennessee
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:I believe that there were, at least,seven others.Given the fact that Fanny Lyon Greer was born 1771, married 1786; given the proven fertility of this couple; I would be amazed if there were not several children born in the la
2 CONC te 1780’s and 1790’s.These shown are all male, and there were, probably, several females, who will be agonizing to discover.Also, there may have been other males who did not join the mass migration to Missouri, and are lost in Vir
2 CONC ginia or Tennessee.I'm afraid that, unless someone finds a Bible with a Greer claiming 22 brothers and sisters, we will never know for sure.The only alternative is exhumation for DNA testing, and the number of Greers we'd have to 
2 CONC dig up would make us a bigger environmental threat than Peabody Coal Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of Joseph Greer SR/Ann Lowe-GREER (DeMoss)
2 CONT
2 CONT As per the "virginia,  Marriages, 1785-1940"
2 CONT Name:  Joseph  GREER
2 CONT Date of Event:  1  May 1786
2 CONT place:  Franklin County,  Virginia
2 CONT Spouse:
2 CONT Name:   Fanny  Lyon
2 CONT Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT the rootsweb.com Ralph Terry capenoch TREE says he received info that Joseph fathered  23 children but Mr. Terry was only given one name  John Greer  B:  1796 Virginia.
2 CONT
