2 CONT
2 CONT Death notice from Altus News-Weekly and Leger News-Times, May 29, 1902:
2 CONT Death of E. Nix
2 CONT Mr. E. Nix, an aged and highly respected citizen of the Plew Valley neighborhood, died of old age at the home of his son four miles north of town Friday night [May 23], and was buried at the Leger Cemetery Saturday afternoon.  He 
2 CONC was one of the pioneers of Greer County, having been here about 13 years, and was universally liked in this country.  A large concourse of sympathizing friends followed the remains of Mr. Nix which were the first to be carried in 
2 CONC Russell and Baucum's new hearse, to their final resting place, where the funeral services were impressingly delivered by Rev. R. J. Morgan.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/23062481/edward_l_nix Find A Grave Memori
2 CONC al] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 21 2024, 16:43:51 UTC''
