1 NAME Samuel /Burks/
2 GIVN Samuel
2 SURN Burks
2 _MARNM Burks
2 NICK Samuel “King” Burke
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1680
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia Colony
1 DEAT
2 DATE 12 FEB 1756
2 ADDR
3 CITY St. Anne's Parish
3 STAE Virginia
1 OCCU Farmer and Indian Trader
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Samuel Burks''' is believed to have been born in Virginia c.1680. His parents are unknown. He was a farmer and Indian trader by occupation. He died after October 6, 1755, the date of his will, in St. Anne's Pari
2 CONC sh, Albemarle County, Virginia. He was sometimes described in documents as Samuel Burks of Hanover, leading to conjecture that he was born in that county, however no records from that period in that county have been found. Hanover
2 CONC  court records were lost in fires during Revolutionary and Civil Wars.
2 CONT
2 CONT One theory for the parents of Samuel Burks is based on the name of his youngest son - John ''Peartree'' Burks. The Peartree or Partree name is repeated often in the early generations of the family. Therefore it has been suggested 
2 CONC that his parents were a John Burk https://www.geni.com/people/John-Burks/6000000052417238879?through=6000000052417052980 and a Mary Peartree or Partree https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Burks/6000000052417052980?through=60000000763
2 CONC 44457094. No documents have been found to prove this but is is a plausible reason for the unusual name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel married Mary Davis, daughter of Nathaniel Davis and Elizabeth Hughes. She was born c.1682 in Albemarle County, Virginia and died after February 12, 1756 in Albemarle County. Family lore claims that she was descended from Po
2 CONC whatan through his daughter who adopted the name Cleopatra. Family lore also claims that she is an ancestor of Jefferson Davis.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel left a detailed will  [see below] in which he named all his children except two. He did not name one daughter, Frances. It is not known why she did not receive a legacy. Her date of death is not known. It is possible that s
2 CONC he died before her father's will was written. He also did not name one son, Charles, known to have died before his father, but did leave legacies for Charles' children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Samuel Burks and Mary Davis:
2 CONT # Frances Burks - married William Smith https://www.geni.com/people/Frances-Smith/6000000032798297475?through=6000000032794208823
2 CONT # Elizabeth Burks - married Capt. William Cabell  https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Cabell/6000000002955696963?through=6000000032794208823
2 CONT # Mary Burks - married Obediah Smith  https://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Smith/6000000032864136850?through=6000000032794208823
2 CONT # Samuel Burks - married Elizabeth (unk)  https://www.geni.com/people/Samuel-Burks-II/6000000032891009856?through=6000000032794208823 
2 CONT # Richard Burks - married Frances Horsely  https://www.geni.com/people/Richard-Burks/6000000032793790261?through=6000000032794208823
2 CONT # Charles Burkes - married Sarah Llewellyn  https://www.geni.com/people/Charles-Burks/6000000191257645826?through=6000000032794208823
2 CONT # John Peartee Burks - married Sarah or Catherine Isham  https://www.geni.com/people/John-Burks/6000000008219166147?through=6000000032794208823
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Will of Samuel Burks===
2 CONT 6 Oct 1755, St. Anne's Parish, Albemarle Co., Virginia. 
2 CONT Will probated 12 Feb 1756
2 CONT
2 CONT IN THE NAME OF GOD AMEN: I '''Samuel Burks''' of Saint Annes Parrish, county of Albemarle, being of sound mind and memory do make and declare this to be my last will and testament...First, I give to my son John Peartree Burks...my
2 CONC  negro boy named Prince...to my daughter Mary Smith...my negro girl named Lyddia...to my beloved wife Mary Burks during her natural life the use of the following slaves now belonging to me...Toby, Frank, Nan, Phillis, Tom, Simon, 
2 CONC Flora, Bess, Sammy, Will and Lucy...to my wife Mary Burks...the use of all my houses and lands...the use of all my personal estate not already disposed of...after my wife's decease the tract of land whereon I now live containing s
2 CONC ix hundred acres* shall be sold...money arising from the sale...distributed in the following manner...to my daughter Elizabeth Cabell one shilling sterling money...to my son Samuel Burks...one shilling sterling money...my son Rich
2 CONC ard Burks...one shilling sterling money, the residue of the said money shall be equally divided between my son John Peartree Burks, Charles Burks and my daughter Mary Smith and my Grandson Samuel Burks...it is my will that my wife
2 CONC  shall have all the uses of my lands and of the slaves and the rest of my personal estate...during her life. I desire she may be undistured in that possession and...if any person or persons on any pretense whatsoever shall endeave
2 CONC r to disturb or molest her in her said right he, she or they shall be deprived of all benefit of this my will except one shilling sterling money and the rest of his or her legacies...shall be vested in my said wife...
2 CONT
2 CONT Lastly, I do appoint my said wife Mary Burks and my friend John Smith, Jnr. Executors of this my last will and testament. In Witness Whereof I have hereunto set my hand and seal this 6th day of October in the year of Our Lord 1755
2 CONC . His Samuel X mark Burks (L.S.). Signed, sealed and published in the presence of Sameul Hopkins, Jos. Thompson and William X Moore (his mark)
2 CONT
2 CONT *Court records show that July 9, 1770 the 600 acres in Albemarle Co., on the north side joining the Rivanna River, 200 acres of which were granted to Samuel by Patent date Sept. 28, 1732, and 400 acres by Patent date June 5, 1754 
2 CONC were sold for 100 pounds to Obediah Smith, husband of Samuel's daughter, Mary.
2 CONT
2 CONT  ==========
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT *http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~harrisonrep/Harrison/d0068/g0000067.html
2 CONT *http://www.theheritagegazette.com/theheritagegazette1_008.htm
2 CONT *http://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Burks-26
2 CONT *http://files.usgwarchives.net/ga/wilkes/bios/burksfam.txt
2 CONT * https://freepages.rootsweb.com/~harrisonrep/genealogy/Harrison/d0068/g0000067.html#I12341
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Botetourt County, Virginia, British Colonial America
