2 DATE 15 MAY 1837
2 ADDR
3 CITY Springfield
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary was born to Judge Paul Carrington Sr. & Margaret Read at "Mullberry Hill", Charlotte County, VA. She died at "Springfield", Prince Edward County, VA. The following is a description given of her in the 1925 Ven
2 CONC ables of Virginia book. "A woman of uncommon vivacity, wit and power of sarcasm. She added to these gifts with great practical judgement which she displayed in the management of her household, and the rearing of her large family,-
2 CONC and all was crowned and chastened by earnest piety.
2 CONT
2 CONT  In powers of conversation she is said to have had few equals. Her company was always enjoyed on account of her bright wit and amusing criticisms on men, and passing events. She frequently visited Virginia Springs where she was us
2 CONC ually surrounded by groups of young people entertained by her conversation. Her fame was so great that she was often referred as "John Randolph in petticoats." By her will she left considerable household chattles in "Springfield" 
2 CONC to her numerous children. "Springfield" was at some point lost to fire. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=74461498
2 CONT
