1 OCCU Furnished supplies during the Rev. War, Fought in Revolutionary War (furnished supplies). DAR Ancestor #A080077
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Achilles Moorman
2 CONT * Birth:	Oct 26 1713
2 CONT * Death:	Circa 1784
2 CONT * Parents:	Charles Moorman, Elizabeth Reynolds
2 CONT * Wife:	Elizabeth Adams
2 CONT *Children: Charles, Silas, Judith, Andrew, William, Jesse, James, Robert, Mary
2 CONT
2 CONT Fought in Revolutionary War (furnished supplies)  [http://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A080077 DAR Ancestor # A080077] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Achilles was a Patriot during the American Revolution and furnished supplies to the Patriots. Achilles and his son, Andrew, are eligible ancestors for the Daughters Of the American Revolution. Several of his sons served with disti
2 CONC nction in the Revolution. Two of his sons migrated to Kentucky and received free land for their military service.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~sunnyann/moorman.html
2 CONT
2 CONT ELIZABETH2 ADAMS (ROBERT1) was born October 29, 1713 in Louisa Co., VA, and died October 27, 1793. She married ACHILLES MOORMAN February 22, 1736/37. He was born October 26, 1713, and died December 01, 1783 in Campbell Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of ELIZABETH ADAMS and ACHILLES MOORMAN are:
2 CONT *         i.       CHARLES3 MOORMAN, b. 1737; d. Bef. June 11, 1798; m. MARY VENABLE2; b. May 22, 1739; d. March 10, 1804.
2 CONT *         ii.       SILAS MOORMAN, b. 1740; m. MARY (POSSIBLY SALLY) MOON3.
2 CONT *         iii.       ANDREW MOORMAN, b. December 02, 1744; d. March 10, 1791; m. JUDITH CLARK.
2 CONT *         iv.       WILLIAM MOORMAN, b. 1746; d. January 25, 1829; m. JUDITH VENABLE.
2 CONT *         v.       JESSE ADAMS MOORMAN, b. December 15, 1759; d. July 09, 1843; m. ELIZABETH BUCKNOR STITH; b. October 25, 1762; d. October 20, 1823.
2 CONT *         vi.       JAMES MOORMAN, b. June 26, 1748.
2 CONT *         vii.       MARY MOORMAN, b. 1750; m. ANDREW ALLEGRE.
2 CONT *         viii.       JUDITH MOORMAN, b. 1752; m. WILLIAM HADEN.
2 CONT *         ix.       ROBERT MOORMAN, b. December 15, 1759.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT Achilles was born in 1713 in New Kent, Virginia. He was the son of Charles Moorman and Elizabeth Reynolds. He married Elizabeth Adams. They were Quakers who regularly attended the Camp Spring Meeting but came often to worship at C
2 CONC larksville.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Moorman - born in 1737 in , Louisa Co., VA; died in 1798. a private in the Revolutionary War and later a Major, he married Mary Venable daughter of Abraham Venable and Martha Davis. Mary was born on 22 May 1739 in Louisa C
2 CONC ounty, VA. She died on 10 Mar 1807 in Breckenridge, Kentucky.
2 CONT Silas Moorman - born in 1740 in Louisa Co., VA; died in 1777. He married Sally Moon who remarried Michael Gilbert.
2 CONT Andrew Moorman - born 02 Dec 1744 in Campbell Co., VA and was a Revolutionary Patriot who furnished supplies. . He married his first cousin, Judith Clark, daughter of Micajah Clark and Judith (Adams) about 1770/1771 in Virginia. J
2 CONC udith was born on 13 Feb 1749 in Albemarle Co., VA and died in 1794. Andrew died 10 Mar 1791.
2 CONT William Moorman - born in Louisa Co., VA. He married (1) Jane Haden; (2) Judith Venable; (3) Elizabeth (Haden) Miller.
2 CONT James Moorman - born in 1748 in Campbell Co., VA
2 CONT Jesse Moorman - born in Louisa Co., VA. He married Elizabeth Buckner-Stith on 14 Jan 1785.
2 CONT Mary Moorman - born in 1750 in Campbell Co., VA; married Matthew or Andrew Allegre.
2 CONT Judith Moorman - born in 1752 in Campbell Co., VA; married William M. Haden.
2 CONT Robert Jesse Moorman - born 15 Dec 1753 in Campbell Co., VA; died in Jul 1843.
2 CONT Jesse Adams Moorman - born 15 Dec 1759 in Campbell Co., VA; died 9 Jul 1843 in Brandenburg, Meade, Kentucky; married Elizabeth Buckner Stith daughter of Richard Stith Jr and Lucy Cocke Hall.
2 CONT Mary Moorman - born in 1763 in Campbell Co., VA.
2 CONT Living in Campbell County, VA, it is here he passed away in 1785.
2 CONT
2 CONT Probate
2 CONT 1 DEC 1785, Campbell County, Virginia[1]
2 CONT Achilles' will mentions wife Elizabeth, and children Jesse, Charles, Andrew, and William. [2]
2 CONT Occupation: Furnished supplies during the Rev. War, Fought in Revolutionary War (furnished supplies). DAR Ancestor #A080077.
2 CONT
2 CONT .
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT ↑ Campbell County, Will Book 1, p. 74
2 CONT ↑ William M. Clemens. Virginia Wills Before 1799: A Complete Abstract Register of All Names Mentioned in Over Six Hundred Recorded Wills: Copied from the Court House Records of Amherst, Bedford, Campbell, Loudoun, Prince William, 
2 CONC and Rockbridge Counties. Pompton Lakes, N.J: Biblio Co, 1924. Print.
2 CONT Daughters of the American Revolution, DAR Genealogical Research Databases, database online, (http://www.dar.org/ : accessed 10 Dec 2016), "Record of Achilles Moorman", Ancestor # A080077.
2 CONT WikiTree profile Moorman-175 created through the import of MOORMAN FAMILY.GED on May 31, 2011 by Mary Elizabeth Stewart. See the Changes page for the details of edits by Mary Elizabeth and others.
2 CONT WikiTree profile Moorman-241 created through the import of EBENSTEIN-GRANGER.GED on Aug 19, 2011 by Merryann Palmer. See the Changes page for the details of edits by Merryann and others.
2 CONT U.S. and International Marriage Records, 1560-1900; Achilles Moorman, b. 1713, Virginia, married Elizabeth Adams, b 1720, Virginia.
2 CONT U.S., Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy, Vol I–VI, 1607-1943: Hinshaw, William Wade, et al., compilers. Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy. 6 vols. 1936–1950. Reprint, Baltimore, Maryland: Genealogical Publishing Co
2 CONC ., 1991–1994. Volume: Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy Vol. VI.
2 CONT Will of Achilles Moorman, 1783, Inventory, 1785-1786 - Campbell Co. VA
2 CONT The Virginia Genealogical Society. Virginia Genealogical Society Quarterly and Magazine of Virginia Genealogy. Albemarle Quarter, 1742-1754, page 27.
2 CONT McNaught, Virginia Eliza Hodge,. James Clark, Mansfield, Christopher Clark : and allied families. Oakland, Calif.: V.E.H. McNaught, 1934. Section: James Clark Mansfield Christopher Clark and allied families.
2 CONT U.S., Quaker Meeting Records, 1681-1935Haverford College; Haverford, Pennsylvania; Philadelphia Yearly Meeting Minutes. Yearly Meeting: Baltimore Yearly Meeting, Meeting State: Virginia, Meeting County: Lynchburg City. Date:
2 CONT 17 Dec 1774
