1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth:  Jun. 3, 1769 Botetourt County Virginia, USA  Death:  Sep. 14, 1841 Bartholomew County Indiana, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT James married Nancy Belleau in Lincoln County, Kentucky 27 January 1797.
2 CONT
2 CONT They made their home on Sugar Creek, Garrard County, where most of their children were born. About 1815 they moved to Gallatin County. While there most of their children were married. By 1835 they had moved across the Ohio River i
2 CONC nto Indiana and settled in Bartholomew County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nancy died in July 1839 and was buried on their property. James died in September 1841 and was buried beside her. Later three grandaughters were buried there. One was removed by family. In 1972 the Indiana Department of Highways w
2 CONC anted to widen and improve Road 9 which crossed the property near the graves. On April 13 1972 Judge Leinberger granted permission to the state to disinter and reinter the four bodies. On June 23, 1972 the four bodies were disinte
2 CONC red and moved to Garland Brook Cemetery, where a very nice marker was placed on their grave. 
2 CONT
