1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas was born in Bucks County, Pennsylvania.  The family moved to Virginia in 1782, and then to South Carolina. Thomas moved to Barren County, Kentucky, about 1805, then to Alabama.  His will, filed in 1827 in Ma
2 CONC rengo Conty, Alabama, named his wife and 12 children.  Letters of administration were issued April 21, 1823, indicating that he died prior to that date.  Ref.: Will abstracts of Marengo County, Alabama.  Children listed were:  Rac
2 CONC hel, Moses, Sally, John, Rebecca and Eli, all over 21;  and Nancy, Vista, Hulda, LusseAnn, Green T. and Harriet, minor heirs. It is believed that the first four children were by Thomas' first wife Hannah (Randall) Roberds and the 
2 CONC other 6 children were by 2nd wife, Anna Nix.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE:  Find A Grave.com
