2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT On August 25, 1770 Emanuel Stevens of the Province of South Carolina sold to William Lawson, Planter, of the Province of South Carolina, 150 acres on the south side of Tyger River.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Lawson served as a Patriot during the Revolution by "providing forage for the public use" in 1782. Payment was received November 18, 1786.
2 CONT
2 CONT the will of William Lawson indicates that he was married twice. His will can be found in the Union county Will Book B and it was proven and recorded March 26, 1829. The name of his first wife is not known. The name of his second w
2 CONC ife waas Susannah Bailey, d/o John Harrison and Mary ? Bailey.
2 CONT
