2 CONT From https://piedmonttrailsblog.wordpress.com/2018/05/03/18th-century-pioneers-of-stokes-county-nc-2/
2 CONT
2 CONT >The year of 1760 brought many settlers to Carolina, among them were the Dearings, Vernons, Wards, Vawters, Walls, Lindsays and Jacksons. Samuel Jackson arrived from Chester County, Pennsylvania and settled along Tom’s Creek, Stok
2 CONC es County. Samuel had at least one son, Joseph Jackson(1761-1818) married Sarah Jessup, daughter of Joseph and Priscilla Jessup.
2 CONT
2 CONT ——
2 CONT
2 CONT >Isaac’s grandparents, Samuel Jackson and Catherine, came to Surry County around 1770-72 settling on Tom's Creek, later called Westfield. They were the first Jacksons in the Westfield area. 
