1 NAME Elizabeth /Jackson/
2 GIVN Elizabeth
2 SURN Jackson
2 _MARNM Ross
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE DEC 1790
2 PLAC Salisbury
2 ADDR
3 STAE North Carolina
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 5 MAY 1847
2 ADDR
3 STAE Tennessee
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elizabeth Jackson was born 1792 “of” Nashville, Tennessee, USA, and died 05 May 1847 in Lincoln, Tennessee, USA (n.b. probably born NC.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:  as of Sept 2017 DNA test evidence suggests https://www.geni.com/people/Hannah-Jackson/6000000050133119178?through=6000000000874999049 and https://www.geni.com/people/Samuel-Jackson/6000000000874999049 From Stokes County,
2 CONC  North Carolina, USA as parents. It appears Elizabeth may have accompanied her brother John G. Jackson to Nashville, Davidson, Tennessee, as many of the rest of their siblings emigrated west to Indiana and Missouri.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family tradition states that Elizabeth Jackson was a cousin of President Andrew Jackson.  Andrew Jackson, known as "Old Hickory" 1767 - 1845; Seventh President of the US; of Scotch- Irish descent; had an estate near Nashville; "Le
2 CONC t the people rule" was his motto. He was elected president in 1828 and 1832. Samuel Jackson was a cousin of https://www.geni.com/people/Andrew-Jackson-7th-President-of-the-USA/6000000007059604501
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT # in 1813, Nashville TN to Abijah Ross.
2 CONT
2 CONT children of Abijah Ross and Elizabeth Jackson:
2 CONT # William Ashburn Ross (1814) m. Mahala Mary Cunningham
2 CONT # Abijah C. Ross (1815) m. Nancy A. Elum
2 CONT # Rebecca Louisa Ross (1818) m. David Farrar
2 CONT # Silas Coleman Ross b 14 Nov 1819 d 03 May 1874, Lincoln, TN m. Matilda Ayers
2 CONT # Sarah D. Ross m. __ Jackson
2 CONT # Nancy Emeline Ross m. Peterson P. Johnson [*]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Comments 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/184102104/elizabeth-ross retrieved March 2019
2 CONT
2 CONT >”Her burial in Lincoln County is unknown. Most list her birth as being in Nashville, Davidson, Tennessee. I do not believe that to be the case, and instead believe she was born in Stokes County, North Carolina and immigrated to N
2 CONC ashville, Davidson, Tennessee with a brother, and maybe some other family members in about 1809/1810. There are no Jackson surnames appearing in any US Census in 1790, 1800, or 1810. The first Jackson's to appear on record in Tenn
2 CONC essee were on the 1820 US Census. DNA evidence connects Elizabeth Jackson to both Samuel Jackson and Hannah Gibson.”
2 CONT
