1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Daughter of Robert Taylor and Elizabeth Welch Taylor. First married to John Doss on January 26, 1680 and then married a second time to Thomas Wingo on July 15, 1688 at Christ Church Parish in Middlesex County Virgi
2 CONC nia. Related to President of the United States Zachary Taylor and James Madison.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://news.rootsweb.com/th/read/DOSS/2012-09/1347546877 Christ Church Parish Register, Middlesex Co., Va. (which I'll refer to here as "CCPR") lists marriage: "John Doss and Ann Taylor was Married the 26th of January 1679."  CCPR
2 CONC  lists the marriage of Ann Doss and Thomas Winger on 15 July 1688, and the death of Ann Wingo (sic) on June 15, 1726. [The remarriage of Ann Doss less than two years after the death of "John Dawd" shown above serves to add weight 
2 CONC to our belief that John Dawd was in fact our John Doss. The same researchers believe this is our Ann remarrying, and that this is a record of her death. The parish records tend to strengthen this argument, as Ann Wingo and Isabel 
2 CONC Herrin seemed to be neighbors, or even living in the same house; they may have both been living with John Doss the younger when they died (see his record).]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Daughter of Robert Taylor and Elizabeth Welch Taylor. First married to John Doss on January 26, 1680 and then married a second time to Thomas Wingo on July 15, 1688 at Christ Church Parish in Middlesex County Virginia. Related to 
2 CONC Presidents of the United States James Madison, William Henry Harrison, James K. Polk, Zachary Taylor, and Benjamin Harrison.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT I resolved a duplicate for Ann Wingo as there seems to be some confusion with her mother-in-law, Ann Wingo who seems to also have a maiden name of Taylor.  Ann Doss Wingo (Taylor) was born in Christ Church  circa 1655.  Her mother
2 CONC -in-law Ann Wingo (Taylor) was born in England in 1630 and immigrated to the US, dying Middelsex County, Virginia.  
