1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://boards.rootsweb.com/surnames.doss/1172.2/mb.ashx
2 CONT
2 CONT Author: Libbie Griffin, former genealogist of the Doss Family Association
2 CONT
2 CONT Christ Church Parish Register, Middlesex Co., Va. (referred to here as "CCPR")
2 CONT
2 CONT As for who married Sarah Herring, the CCPR is very clear: "Jno. Doss and Sarah Herring married June 17th (Banns) 1735." ["Jno." is an old abbreviation of John]
2 CONT
2 CONT The birth of their daughter Mary was recorded in CCPR on 3 Jan. 1739/40. The CCPR records the death of "John Dose" on 17 March 1743. [It is my belief that this man was a son of John Doss and Ann Taylor Doss whose birth is not reco
2 CONC rded in the parish register.]
2 CONT
2 CONT CCPR lists the marriage of Ann Doss and Thomas Winger on 15 July 1688, and the death of Ann Wingo (sic) on June 15, 1726. [The remarriage of Ann Doss less than two years after the death of "John Dawd" shown above serves to add wei
2 CONC ght to our belief that John Dawd was in fact our John Doss. The same researchers believe this is our Ann remarrying, and that this is a record of her death. The parish records tend to strengthen this argument, as Ann Wingo and Isa
2 CONC bel Herrin seemed to be neighbors, or even living in the same house; they may have both been living with John Doss the younger when they died (see his record).]
2 CONT
