2 CONT
2 CONT I have worked for years on the early Va. Doss families and have traced most of them south. It is my firm belief that William Doss who m. Mary Blankenship was the son of Jeremiah Doss and his wife Ursula Taylor Doss, although I don
2 CONC 't have proof. In a nutshell: Jeremiah and Ursula married in Goochland Co. VA. (see The Douglas Register, some entries for them under DAWS and DAVIS). They moved to Franklin Co. Va., then to Pendleton Co. So. Car. (Old 96 District
2 CONC ). They met up with the Blankenships in Franklin Co., where Reuben Blankenship was born. These families traveled together after that. Deeds in So. Car. for Ursula Doss are witnessed by Reuben and other Blankenships. Then they went
2 CONC  to Jackson Co. Ga. William had brothers Claiborn, John and Azariah Doss, who appear frequently in the Ga. records, including Jasper Co. at the time of Wm. & Mary's marriage. Libbie Griffin Genealogist for the Doss Family Associat
2 CONC ion
2 CONT
