1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He served as a soldier in Dunmore's War, a 1774 expedition against the Indians on the frontier. He also served in the Revolutionary War in the 5th and 9th Virginia Regiments. He held the rank of corporal and receiv
2 CONC ed a pension. Sold his land in Virginia in 1804 and moved to Kentucky. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Relationship to wives:
2 CONT
2 CONT At least one Ancestry.com public tree lists Mary Edwards as Joel Doss' wife. The sequence of children's birth years is problematic, and it may be that Edwards was an extramarital affair, or parentage incorrectly attributed to him.
2 CONC  It is also possible that Mary Penny and Mary Edwards (who share the same approximate birth date) might be the same person.
2 CONT
