1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/patty/308/
2 CONT
2 CONT James4 PATY (Edward3, Edward2, Theophilus1) was born circa 1705 at Prince George Co, VA. He married Sarah Clanton circa 1741. He died on 10 December 1758 at Halifax Co, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Paty, who I feel is the father of James Patey, died in Berkeley District South Carolina. Is this why James Patey Jr. moved there fro m Virginia? *James settled in Newberry County South Carolina, (taken from Berkele y Distri
2 CONC ct) and raised his family there. James lived here till his de ath. *I need to find out more about Edward, and his other children, as James Jr, may have gone there because he still had family there, Uncles ect. *.
2 CONT Sarah CLANTON. Reference: 321. She Sarah Clanton is listed as wife of James Paty, in the Quakers records , but I have found no other information on her. She is listed only as Sarah i n the will of James Paty. *. She was born circa
2 CONC  1721 at VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT The five known children of James4 Paty and Sarah Clanton were as follows:
2 CONT * 26. i. Jesse5 PATY married Sarah Sallie West, daughter of Joseph West and Jane Owen, at Never married. He was born in 1744/45 at Brunswick Co, VA. He married Delilah Doss, daughter of James Doss and Frances Nix, circa 1763 at VA
2 CONC . He died after 9 November 1795 at Union Co, SC.
2 CONT * 27. ii. James PATY was born between 1747 and 1750 at Lunenburg Co, VA. He married Margaret Mote, daughter of David Mote and Dorcas Nicholds, on 11 March 1769 at Newberry Co, SC. He died on 28 July 1796 at Newberry Co, SC.
2 CONT * 28. iii. Sarah 'Sally' PATY was born circa 1748 at Campbell Co, VA.     She I believe this daughter of James, to be the mother of Nancy Patty wh o married Benjamin Cannifax, and Elijah Paty who married Ava Parrott. 
2 CONT * 29. iv. Charles PATY was born circa 1749 at Campbell Co, VA. He married Mary Jane Jay, daughter of William Jay and Mary Elizabeth Vestal, on 11 March 1773 at Bush River MM, Newberry Co, SC.
2 CONT * 30. v. Nancy PATY.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
