1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Son of Charles Patty 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Adline (Connell) Hulsey, he died in a mental institution and is buried near Tuscaloosa, Alabama.
2 CONT
2 CONT There was land granted to him near Huntsville, AL on 14 Apr 1896, filed in Cleburne Co., AL. Therefore, the previous death date of May 1890 is wrong. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Nancy Caroline (Thomas) Patty in 1839 in South Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles and Nancy Caroline (Thomas) Patty had 12 children.  John and Henry were born in South Carolina.  The others, Terry, Martha, Mary Ann, Elizabeth,  Junious, Ellen, Nancy, Margaret, Joseph and Green were born in Cleburne Coun
2 CONC ty, Alabama.  All the children lived to adulthood except Green Patty who died when he was 15 years old. Margaret's nickname was "Babe". Source:  Two articles in the book "The Heritage Of Cleburne County, Alabama" See:  "Charles Pa
2 CONC tty" and "Ira Patty"
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles and Nancy Patty came to Cleburne County, Alabama from Union District, South Carolina in 1848.  They settled near Piney Woods Methodist Church, north of what is now Fruithurst, Alabama. Source:  Viola (Cheatwood) Laminack's
2 CONC  Family records.
