1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Parents: F: John Daniel Vest, I (1705 - 1765) & M: Charlotte Ann Bakes (1709 - 1734)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT '''James Richard Vest, Sr''' was born in 1745 in Chesterfield, Virginia, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-111510930 John Daniel Vest, I] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-94817292 Charlotte Ann Vest]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT James married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34779963994 Dinah Chastain] circa 1765 in Chesterfield, Chesterfield, Virginia, USA. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-111505063 George Washington Vest, Sr]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT James married [https://www.geni.com/profile-114289871 Dinah Vest]. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34778356927 Priscilla Bingham Bingham]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34686280723 Edward Vest]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-114290076 John Vest]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-114290126 Littleberry Vest]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-114289996 William Vest]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34662288746 Reiney Vest]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34662288752 Archelus Vest]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34662288756 Stephen Vest]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34662288760 Frank Carter Vest]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34662288766 Eleazor Vest]; 
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/profile-34662288801 James Vest]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on January 6, 1795 in Chesterfield, Virginia, United States. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT James signed a petition supporting separation of Church and State.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Dec. 9, 1785, he signed a petition supporting the disposal of Glebes and other Church (of England TL) property with proceeds to be used to pay the public debt.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Nov. 26, 1786, James signed a petition to repeal the incorporation of the Episcopal Church. Signed as witness to the will of David Mosby Davidson of Bedford Co., Virginia, Sept., 1780. The will was proved April 4, 1793 and it w
2 CONC as noted that James Vest Sr. was now dead
2 CONT
2 CONT According to information from website http://rootsweb.com/pub/usgen/web/va/chesterfield/wills/v22300001.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT I found the following Last Will and Testament of James Vest from Chesterfield Co., VA Will Book # 4. - This was transcribed verbatim by Sandra Lake Lassen in February of 1994. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
