2 CONT
2 CONT There are personal letters from Ambrose to his wife at this site: Letters from War:from website: www.19thalabama.org/doss James Ambrose Doss was a 5th Sgt. in CSA. He was killed in a skirmish on a march outside of Mariette, GA.. H
2 CONC is fellow soldiers buried him on the West bank of the Chattahoochee River on the Turner Plantation. Died on the west side of the Chattahoochee River about 10 miles west of Atlanta, Georgia during the Civil War. He was buried on th
2 CONC e Turner Plantation in Atlanta and a memorial stone was placed at Morris Cemetery   
2 CONT Family links:   Parents:   John Doss (1799 - 1849)   Mary Gentle Doss (1800 - ____)  
2 CONT  Spouse:   Sarah Elizabeth Brake Doss (1824 - 1923)  
2 CONT  Children:   William Martin Doss (1848 - 1938)*   Lafayette Ambrose Doss (1854 - 1936)*   Ambrose McMillan Doss (1856 - 1916)*   Martha Lucinda Doss Spradling (1861 - 1953)*   Bennett Milton Doss (1868 - 1947)*  
2 CONT  Siblings:   James Ambose Doss (1823 - 1864)   Joel Doss (1824 - 1884)*   Ezkiel Doss (1836 - 1910)*  
2 CONT *Calculated relationship  
2 CONT Burial: Morris Cemetery  Morris Jefferson County Alabama, USA  
2 CONT Created by: Robin Knowles Miner Record added: Jun 20, 2012  Find A Grave Memorial# 92218034
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Ambrose served in the Civil War and was killed in the Battle of Atlanta in 1864.  A tombstone was erected in October 1995 in the Morris Cemetary in Morris, AL next to his wife, Sarah Brake.  The tombstone reads:  Ambrose Doss Augu
2 CONC st 29, 1823 to July 5, 1864 Sgt Co C 19th Alabama Infantry CSA Killed in the Battle of Atlanta, buried on the West bank of the Chattahoochee River, Cobb County, GA  Several letters Ambrose wrote to his wife during the war exist.  
2 CONC 1850 Chickasaw MS Census #431(DD-D2): Ambeus, 29, b. AL; Sarah, 26, AL; Mary A., 3; William 2; all b. AL [which indicates they've just arrived in Chickasaw] living with Isaac and Elizabeth Spear, also b. AL and their children WIll
2 CONC iam, 3 and Milton, 2, both b. in Miss.    1860 Jefferson County AL Census (BM3-144):  Ambrose, 36, b. AL; Sarah, 36, b. AL; Mary A., 12, Wm. W., 11, John A., 9, James M., 7, Lafayette, 5, Ambrose M., 3, Sarah E., 1; all children e
2 CONC xcept John born in AL, John born in Miss.  1880 Jefferson County Census (p.68, #11[DD-A7]}:  Sarah Doss, age 56, b. KY; Amhert M., son, age 23; Elizabeth, dau, 21; Lucinda, dau, 19; Milton, son, 12; Asbury, grandson, 9; Emma, gran
2 CONC ddaughter, 7; Jolotta, granddaughter, 5; William M., son, 31.  1850 US Census Name: Ambus Doss  Age: 29  Estimated Birth Year: abt 1821  Birth Place: Alabama  Gender: Male  Home in 1850(City,County,State): Eastern Division, Chicka
