1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ID: I386991 Name: Terrisha BAILEY Given Name: Terrisha Surname: Bailey Sex: M Birth: 1779 in Amherst Co,VA Death: 23 NOV 1867 in Nelson Co,VA Note: 1850 Nelson Co., VA Census, pg 224 65 BAILEY Tessisha 71 m Farmer 
2 CONC 4000 VA 1 Aug BAILEY Frances 36 f VA 1 Aug MURRELL Nancy 32 f VA 1 Aug MURRELL Adeline E. 12 f VA 1 Aug School within yr. MURRELL Virginia 10 f VA 1 Aug School within yr. MURRELL Woodrow 8 m VA 1 Aug School within yr. MURRELL G. 6
2 CONC  f
2 CONT
2 CONT 1850 Nelson 231 166 166 BAILEY Constance 23 f VA 8 Aug 231 166 166 BAILEY Terrisha J. 37 m Farmer VA 8 Aug 231 166 166 BAILEY Fayetta 3 f VA 8 Aug 231 166 166 BAILEY Thomas R. 7/12 m
2 CONT
2 CONT 1860 Nelsonco, Va pg 461 461 BAILY Terisha J. 41 M Farmer Nelson 461 461 BAILY Constance 32 F Nelson 461 461 BAILY Thiette 12 F Nelson 461 461 BAILY Thomas W. 10 M Nelson 461 461 BAILY Cornelia 8 F Nelson 461 461 BAILY Millard F. 
2 CONC 6 M Nelson 461 461 BAILY Christopher 2 M Nelson
2 CONT
2 CONT Information recieved from John Luddy Burke Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT Terrisha began to accumulate land along Dutch Creek, Nelson Co., Va. in 1816.
2 CONT
2 CONT Date Deed Bk Page Acres Location Jun 26 1815 2 232 268 Dutch Creek Aug 25 1816 2 485 150 " " 23 1818 3 55 214 " " Apr 22 1822 3 106 13 " " Apr 24 1825 3 278 40 " " Aug 22 1842 10 69 494 " " Nov 25 1855 13 115 70 " " Apr 15 1858 15
2 CONC  207 13 " " Oct 2 1867 17 1 409 " "
2 CONT
2 CONT 1850 Nelson Co., VA Census, pg 224 65 BAILEY Tessisha 71 m Farmer 4000 VA BAILEY Frances 36 f VA MURRELL Nancy 32 f VA MURRELL Adeline E. 12 f VA MURRELL Virginia 10 f VA MURRELL Woodrow 8 m VA MURRELL G. 6 f VA (surname should be
2 CONC  Norvell, not Murrell)
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1860 Census lists Terrisha Bailey as head of a household, age 82. Residing in the same household were Nancy A. Norvill, age 42; William W. Norvill, age 18; Gabrilla Norvill, age 16. ( Correct spelling is Norvell.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Terrisha's will recorded in Will Bk. at Nelson Co., Va. Court House. The will was dated October 1, 1867, and probated November 25, 1867. An Inventory of Property of the estate of Terrisha Bailey was presented to the Court held for
2 CONC  Nelson County on December 23, 1867 and ordered to be recorded.
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Last will and testament of Terrisha Bailey of Nelson County, Virginia"
2 CONT
2 CONT I, Terrisha Bailey, considering the uncertainty of this mortal life, and being of Sound mind and memory, do make and publish this my last will and testament, hereby revoking all former wills or papers purporting to be such--in man
2 CONC ner and form following viz:
2 CONT
2 CONT First, I desire all my just debts and funeral expenses be paid as soon as possible out of my estate, by my executors, herein after mentioned.
2 CONT
2 CONT Second: Having advanced to my sons Thomas R. and William P Bailey the sums of five hundred dollars each, previous to the making of this my last will and testament, it is my desire and intention that all the rest of my children, vi
2 CONC z: Nancy A. Norville, or her heirs, William N Dickson, or his heirs, by my daughter Mary Ann and Terrisha Bailey, Jas- or his heirs shall receive the like sum of five hundred dollars each before my general distribution of my estat
2 CONC e.
2 CONT
2 CONT Third: I give and bequeath to my grandson William W. Norvill, the sum of three hundred dollars, in consideration of his having lost a leg in the Army.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fourth: If any sale of my real estate should take place, my will and desire is that the family burial ground shall be reserved from sale and remain the joint property of my heirs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Fifth: If after the date of this my last will, I shall pay any debts of my heirs, the sums so paid are to be deducted from the portions of those heirs for whose benefit the said debts were paid.
2 CONT
2 CONT sixth: After the foregoing conditions have been complied with, it is my will and desire that all my property of whatever description, be equally divided among all my heirs, Viz: To Nancy A. Novill and her children, one fifth part;
2 CONC  To Terrisha Bailey Jms and his children, on fifth part; To William N. Dickson and his children by my daughter Mary Ann, one fifth part; To the children of Thomas R. Bailey, one fifth part; To the children of William P.Bailey, one
2 CONC  fifth part.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lastly, I do hereby constitute and appoint Terrisha Bailey, Jms and William S Murrill my Executors to carry into effect this my Will and Testament, In Testimony whereof I have here unto set my hand seal this 1st day of October One
2 CONC  Thousand, Eight Hundred and Sixty Seven.
2 CONT
2 CONT his seal Terrisha Baily
2 CONT
2 CONT Apr 1 1870 Terrisha James Bailey, Executor of Terrisha's Estate recorded the estate divided into five tracts. Deed Bk. 19, Pages 346-348. To be divided among the five heirs as stated in the will.
2 CONT
2 CONT ( Taken from the Parish register of Mt. Shiloh Baptist Church, Nelson County, Virginia, as reported in The Virginia Bailey Genealogy, by R. G. Bailey Publishing Company-1946. )
2 CONT
2 CONT " Died at his residence in Nelson County, November 23, 1867, Terrisha Bailey in the 90th year of his age. In this long life he had filled his position so well in society that all acknowledge him to be an honest and good man. He wa
2 CONC s a man of more that ordinary devotion to his family. From my earliest recollection of him, which was more than 35 years ago, he literally lived for his family. He did not wait for their request, but anticipated, it seemed, their 
2 CONC every want. I visited him in the hot days of last July and found him still working hard for his family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bro Bailey was one of those who made a public profession of religion in Mt. Shiloh meeting house. He was baptized by Bro. C. Wingfield and taken into the constitution of the Church. From that time he filled punctually his Place an
2 CONC d was scarcely ever absent from the house of God, when others met. He paid with great punctuality his pastor's salary, and all other obligations to the church. He has been a subscriber to the Religious Herald 25 to 30 years"
2 CONT
2 CONT I hate errors, so please inform me of any so I may correct them, this work is best I could do as of Nov 2006 and is all I have in general. Please use with caution. jhll
