1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Robert Johns that married Mary Gresham is not of Native American Descent, but he is often connected to the Johns line that is a documented Native American Ancestry in Amherst County, Virginia.
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Johns-838
2 CONT https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/6989691/person/1103337447/facts
2 CONT
2 CONT ---Front leaf of Family Bible of John D. Johns (his grandfather). Submitted by Lester P. Johns
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sory for all of thee in our family who will be bent by the way of greed to change the dividing of Robert Johns will of wishes which is being distributed by his wife Mary. It is indeed sorry that these children are imbued by Satan
2 CONC . Judith, wife of William Booth/Mary, wife of John Richardson and Martha their daughter/ Robert Johns/ William Johns/ Jesse Johns/ Elizabeth, wife of Nathanial Booth/ Francis Johns/ Nancy Johns/ Sally Johns/ John Alexander Johns/ 
2 CONC Bartlett Johns." [2]
2 CONT "Descendants of ROBERT JOHNS of Amherst County, VA should be aware that inaccurate information was posted some years ago and can still be found on the internet. ROBERT JOHNS of Amherst County was not the son of the William Johns w
2 CONC ho died in Amherst County, VA about 1775. There is no proof, or evidence, to substantiate this claim. Nor was he the son of a woman by the name of Ann/AnnWilliams/Judith Ann Williams. No one is able to provide information/document
2 CONC ation/proof about this woman. She seems to be a fabrication who never existed. If anyone would like to further discuss the inaccurate information linking ROBERT JOHNS of Amherst County to the William Johns who died in Amherst Coun
2 CONC ty about 1777, please feel free to contact me. Bob Newsom
2 CONT
2 CONT *In Albemarle County, VA in June 1747, 218 acres was surveyed for Robert Johns. 
2 CONT *On Mar. 1, 1752, William Johns of Chesterfield County bought 730 acres from John Bostick, "where James Staples lives." (There are four other land transactions shown for William in the 1750's in the Deeds of Amherst Co. and Albema
2 CONC rle Co..., Bailey Fulton Davis. William could be a brother of Robert Johns.) 
2 CONT *On December 6, 1756, a survey was done for Roberts Johns. "This is a Plat of 92 acres of land lying on both sides of North Branch of Porrage Creek in the County of Albemarle." This was done by John Staples, Agt. Surv. This plat w
2 CONC as found in Albemarle Plats - 1760, on page 34 at the Virginia Archives. (The plat - 92 A. - should be put here.) 
2 CONT *On July 4, 1757, 208 acres were surveyed for William Johns on Holladays River. (See note above.) 
2 CONT *On March 7, 1758, 164 acres were surveyed for David Johns on the North side of Appomattox River. These references are also located in the Albemarle Plats - 1760, at the Virginia Archives. The references to William's survey is on 
2 CONC page 32, and David's is on page 34. Robert and Mary Johns lived in Amherst County, VA. Amherst County was formed in 1761 from Albemarle County. Amherst County records show the following entries. 
2 CONT *December 18, 1778 - Thomas Johns to Ro. Johns - Thomas for love of his brother, Robt., "and to fulfill desire of his late father, Robt. Johns" - 100 acres both sides Porrage Creek. Part of 218 acres granted to my father, Ro., who
2 CONC  died without will. Upper end of tract. Lines: Joshua Fry. Witnesses: James Dillard, Jno. Christian, Jno. Stewart. Mary Johns, mother of Thomas, appeared and relinquished dower. (Davis, pages 2 and 181.) *November Court 1779 - Wil
2 CONC liam Boothe and Judith, his wife, John Richardson and Mary, his wife, Jobert Johns, William Johns, Jesse Johns, Nathaniel Booth and Elizabeth, his wife, Martha Johns an Infant by John Richardson, her next friend, Francis Johns, Jo
2 CONC hn Alexander Johns, Nancy Johns, Salley Johns and Bartlett Johns, Infants by William Booth their next friend, Plfs. Against - Mary Johns, Admx. of Robert Johns, Decd., and Thomas Johns Heir-at-Law of the Deceased, Dfts - In Chance
2 CONC ry - Mary Johns, Adms. ordered to make an Account of the Estate of Robert Johns, Decd. on oath before Drury Christian, Charles Christian, John Christian (Buffaloe) and they will have authority to divide the Estate of her said husb
2 CONC and having regard to her dower. (Amherst County in the Revolution, Sweeny, page 86.) 
2 CONT *References to the Johns' family marriage records are located in the Marriage Records of Amherst County, Virginia, 
2 CONT *1763-1800. (Enter map of Amherst County 1787.)
2 CONT
