1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Mary Gresham
2 CONT * Born about 1725 in Spotsylvania, Colony of Virginia [uncertain]
2 CONT * Died after 1783 in Amherst, Virginia, USA
2 CONT * Daughter of Thomas Gresham and Mary Unknown [uncertain]
2 CONT *Sister of Thomas Gresham Jr., William Gresham and Rachel Gresham
2 CONT * Wife of Robert Johns — married May 1742 in Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Robert Johns (abt. 1718 - bef. 1778), son of Robert Johns and Judith (Gathright) 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Gresham Johns is not of Native American descent. See lengthy research on profile Johns-6702 with sources that proves she enumerated on tax lists as "white".
2 CONT
2 CONT Mentioned in the "Deed of Gift" from her mother.  Mary x Gresham of Spts. Co., to her "loving children". '''Mary Johns''', William Gresham and Rachael Gresham. Deed of Gift. Goods and chattels. This deed is signed "Mary x Grayson"
2 CONC . July 7, 1742.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Gresham-1068
2 CONT *Gresham, Robinson & Allied Families https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/6989691/person/152184873238/facts
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Gresham-84 WikiTree Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Dec 31 2017, 16:05:29 UTC''
2 CONT * Milt's Theories of Early Virginia Greshams-Research Notes (Shared by Private Researcher) Posted 23 Jun 2020.  < [https://www.ancestry.com/mediaui-viewer/collection/1030/tree/6989691/person/-1151370509/media/939337cf-89a8-4eab-8f
2 CONC 15-3726825c9e67?_phsrc=nHW15701&usePUBJs=true&sort=-created AncestryImage] > Deed Of Gift - 9 July 1742- Spotsylvania Co., DB “D”, p. 1. Mary Gresham makes deed of gift of livestock and other personal property to “my loving childr
2 CONC en” '''Mary Johns, William Gresham and Rachael Gresham'''. Wit: John Waller, John Gordon and James Allen. Recorded: 7 July 1742.
2 CONT
