2 CONC x6720\pardirnatural\f0\fs24 \cf0 >From Amherst County, Virginia, in the Revolution, Lenora Higginbotham   \par Sweeny:   \par p. 14, 15. Muster Roll of Captain Samuel Jordan Cabells Comp'y of 6th   \par Virginia Regiment of Foot, 
2 CONC under Command of Lieutenant Col. James   \par Hendricks for the Months of May and June 1777.  William Johns 4th Mch,   \par Thomas Johns 4th Do.   \par    \par P. 17, Payroll of Capt. Samuel Jordan Cabells Comp'y, 6th VA Batt. of 
2 CONC   \par Continental Forces, Commanded by LT. Col. James Hendricks, July 1777   \par Thomas Johns, Private, 6 2/3, amt of pay 2 10   \par William Johns, same   \par    \par P. 19, Pay Roll of Cap't Samuel Jordan Cabell's Company of 
2 CONC the Rifle   \par Detachment Commanded by Col Daniel Morgan for Three Months from the 1st   \par of August to the 1st of November 1777.   \par William Johns, Private, 6 2/3, $20, L6   \par Thomas Johns, same  (They were in Albany a
2 CONC nd Sarratoga at this time)   \par    \par P. 21, Payroll* of Capt Benjamin Taliaferros Compy of detached Riflemen   \par Commanded by Col Dan'l Morgan for the month of December 1777.   \par William Johns, Privt, 1 mo., 6 2/3,   \p
2 CONC ar Thomas Johns, Privt, 2 mo., 13 1/3, Omitted in Novem'r Payroll   \par *  All of the men listed on this payroll, except Sergt. Thomas Burfoot,   \par received the "Extra month's Pay allowed by the Honourable the   \par Continent
2 CONC al Congress."   \par    \par P. 23, A Pay roll of Cap'n Benjamin Taliaferro's Compy of detached   \par Riflemen Commanded by Col Dan'l Morgan, from the first day of February   \par 78, to the expiration of their Service, including
2 CONC  15 days allowed them   \par for going to Virginia.  (They were in upstate New York)   \par Thomas Johns, pri, 1 month, discharged 15th Feb, 6 2/3.   \par William doesn't show on this payroll.   \par    \par Virginia Publick Claim
2 CONC s, p. 84, 6 Jan 1783, Amherst Co., Mary Johns for   \par boarding & attendance on William Johns 90 days L11-5.  (William must   \par have become ill or wounded during the rev war.  That would be the only   \par way that Mary could
2 CONC  have been paid by Publick Claim for his care.  It   \par might also explain why he wasn't on the muster out roll above with his   \par brother Thomas.)   \par    \par The above information is from Karen Salisbury.  \par >From Amh
