2 CONC he place of William Johns. Over age. Hands on Beaver from Isaac Thornsbury's to the head therfo are to assist (May Term: Monday the 22nd day of May 1826. \par  \par Dec. 27, 1817 Indenture from William James Mayo, Rhodes Meade, Jo
2 CONC hn Hackworth, Tandy Stratton, Thomas Johns, Robert Brown and Mial Mayo, Trustees of the Floyd Seminary Lands to Micajah Harrison in the amount of $300.00 for 303 acres in Floyd County on Quick Sand Creek. \par  \par Thomas Johns a
