1 NOTE {geni:about_me} It has been said that Johanna's father, Russell was a Virginia Monacan Indian. In fact, there is documentation for this in the Virginia Monacan Indian Museum. My great grandfather, Albert G. Cook married Russell's 
2 CONC daughter, Johanna Johns in 1832 in Barren County, Kentucky.  There has been some discussion that Albert may have been from a neighboring Virginia Indian tribe and born in Virginia and not Kentucky!
