1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (Edit - Find a Grave states dates as d. 13 Aug 1793. Current profile shows  d. 04 Aug 1791. Find a Grave Bio below:)
2 CONT OK, someone has asked that I add a NOTE that the DATE of DEATH is  not a sure thing.
2 CONT Please see the paragraph below.........However, Joshua DeMoss is pretty sure Ann lived until circa 1795-96, 
2 CONT So IF there were an "circa"   box that is what I would check.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her SIBLINGS: Sarah  B: 1713
2 CONT Elizabeth   B:  1720
2 CONT RACHEL  B: 1730 married Benjamin Son #2-brother to Joseph
2 CONT Mary        B:  1719
2 CONT William     B:  1727
2 CONT John        B:  1728
2 CONT Thomas      B:  1733
2 CONT Samuel      B:  1739
2 CONT
2 CONT She is 1/2 sister to Rachel Lowe.  She & Joseph married 18 August 1750 in St. John's Parish. There is a Registry of it. She is named in her husband Joseph's will.  
2 CONT Her 2nd husband was Thomas DeMoss,  no issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT After Joseph passed away Ann Lowe-Greer married
2 CONT Thomas DeMoss SR. who was married to 
2 CONT Abiah  Beach-DeMoss, after she passed away Thomas SR.
2 CONT REMARRIED--- Ann Lowe-GREER, Widow of Joseph GREER 
2 CONT and with her came some daughters, namely 
2 CONT Jemima  born 1767  VA
2 CONT Priscilla  born circa  1760  VA
2 CONT Ann  born circa 1775 VA
2 CONT Lize born circa 1777 VA
2 CONT AND when the girls became of age 2 of them married their Step-brothers, Ann married Thomas DeMoss-1798 in Wilkes County North Carolina (marriage contract att'd)
2 CONT
2 CONT Priscilla  married  William L. DeMoss 
2 CONT
2 CONT AND  Jemima  married Philemon Saunders (2nd cousin)
2 CONT The Will of her father Joseph GREER proves not only her parents but her husband, Philemon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nancy (Ann) DeMoss signed the marriage contract for 
2 CONT Temperance Greer to marry William Hatcher
2 CONT Aug. 13,1791 so we know for sure she was alive at least 
2 CONT late 1791.  However, Joshua DeMoss is pretty sure Ann lived until circa 1795-96, when in 1796 Thomas DeMoss has signed Lize's marriage contract.
2 CONT
2 CONT AND  Lize  married Caleb Heptinstall, the marriage contract is signed "Thomas DeMoss, Guardian" 
2 CONT As per "Winfield's Marriage Records of Virginia", pg 113 "Caleb Heptinstall married Lize Greer, 
2 CONT on 7 Nov. 1796,
2 CONT signed, by "sur. Thomas DeMoss, g." (Guardian)
2 CONT
2 CONT SO THIS Marriage Contract proves that the 
2 CONT Thomas DeMoss, Guardian of the Ann Lowe-Greer DeMoss children was in deed still alive in 1796.
2 CONT He would be 70 years of age and still living in Virginia.
2 CONT '*****************************************************
2 CONT
2 CONT sources: St. John's Registry- Will of Joseph-
2 CONT rootsweb.com  Several  GREER Family TREES=
2 CONT And there are sources that say she moved with her husband Thomas DeMoss to Wilkes, N. Carolina..
2 CONT But as of the marriage of the daughter, Lize that took place 1796 in Virginia and signed by her Guardian, Thomas DeMoss, husband of Lize' mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their other CHILDREN  not LINKED:
2 CONT Greenberry B:  1764 #67237127∼
