1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1st  son of Joseph/Ann Lowe-GREER
2 CONT
2 CONT SIBLINGs  not LINKED  yet:Greenberry 15 Sep. 1764  #67237127
2 CONT
2 CONT there is no census or marriage record for this Thomas GREER son of Joseph/Ann Lowe-Greer.
2 CONT
2 CONT several familysearch.org trees say,  he married "Ann" in 1772
2 CONT in Bedford Co. Virginia.
2 CONT So he was only married 9 years when he died.
2 CONT
2 CONT '***********************************************************
2 CONT JUST received from Joshua DeMoss  (copy attached) 
2 CONT     Library of Virginia --Bedford County Chancery Court 
2 CONT     Transcribed by Nel Hatcher 
2 CONT     "The Common Wealth of Virginia" To the Sheriff of Bedford County, 
2 CONT     Greeting We Command you that you summon 
2 CONT     Thomas Demoss & Anne his Wife who was Widow & Ex of Joseph Greer, 
2 CONT     George Haynes & Lucy his wife 
2 CONT     Farley Hatcher & Anne his wife 
2 CONT     Nathan Greer 
2 CONT     Greenberry Greer & 
2 CONT     Joseph, 
2 CONT     Jamima, 
2 CONT     Priscilla, 
2 CONT     Temperance, 
2 CONT     Tegury[?] & ( my note:::Lize “Tege”) 
2 CONT     Anne Greers 
2 CONT     to appear Before the Justices of ?ursai- County Court at the Courthouse on the fourth Monday in this month to answer a 
2 CONT     Bill in Chancery Exhibited against them by 
2 CONT     Dicey Greer & Sarah Greer 
2 CONT     'Infant Daughters of Thomas Greer who was Eldest son of Joseph Greer :deceased by John Forguson their next friend and this they shall in No wise Omit :under the Penalty of one Hundred Pounds and have then there this Writ 
2 CONT
2 CONT Witness James Steptoe Clerk of a?said County Court at the Court House aforesaid the Third day of October 1783 in the Eighth Year of the Common Wealth ? James Steptoe"
2 CONT NOTES on SUMMONS
2 CONT
2 CONT     -LUCY Greer?-Haynes, Geo. (not listed anywhere else)
2 CONT     -ANNE Greer?-Hatcher, Farley (not found anywhere else)
2 CONT     -Nathanial mar.:Lucy Arthur
2 CONT     -Greenberry mar.: Charlotte DEMOSS
2 CONT     -Joseph mar.: Fanny Lyon
2 CONT     -Jemima mar.: Philemon SAUNDERS
2 CONT     -Priscilla mar.: Wm.L. DEMOSS
2 CONT     -Temperance mar.:#1 Ward Hatcher/#2-Wm. Burnett
2 CONT     -Tegury ("Tege" aka:Lize) mar.: Caleb Heptinstall
2 CONT     - ANNE GREER MAR: THOMAS DEMOSS JR....... 
2 CONT
2 CONT     10- PROVES THERE WAS a daughter Ann GREER and that Thomas DeMoss Jr. DID NOT marry his Aunt that was 35 years his senior... 
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings
2 CONT AS PER THE COURT SUMMONS
2 CONT Priscilla Greer DeMoss (1760 - 1836 
2 CONT Joseph Greer (1762 - 1840 
2 CONT Nathaniel Greer (1763 - 1833 
2 CONT Greenberry 15 Sep. 1764 #67237127 Mar.: Charlotte DeMoss 
2 CONT Jemima Greer Saunders (1767 - 1844 
2 CONT Temperance Greer Hatcher (1768 - 1810 
2 CONT Ann Greer 1775 Virginia Mar.: Thomas DeMoss JR. (Step-brother) 
2 CONT Lize Greer Heptinstall (1777 - 1853 (aka:  "Tege"
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN
2 CONT     Dicey Greer Marcum (1768 - 1830 
2 CONT     Sarah Greer Maxey (1774 - 1870 
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes--
2 CONT Definition of the word "INFANT" taken from wikipedia.com 
2 CONT
2 CONT "An infant (from the Latin word infans, meaning "unable to speak" or "speechless") is the very young offspring of a human." (So this to me would mean they were born circa 1772-1781, this would be when researchers say Thomas was ma
2 CONC rried to Ann and when Thomas is known to have passed away, we are assuming that the girls mother was also dead because there is a "friend" who filed the Summons for the Infant girls.
2 CONT
