1 NOTE {geni:about_me}      Luvicy (or Lavicy) Bruce Nix was born April 27, 1798, in Georgia.  She died December 21, 1890 in Honey Grove, Fannin County Texas, and is buried in Oakwod Cemetary,.  She married Obediah Nix about 1818 or 1819
2 CONC , probably in Murphreesboro, Tennessee.  They lived in the Madison County Tennessee area where the first 4 children were born.  Mary Arminda Nix born 1820 (my ancenstor); John Edward Nix born 1822; William Anderson Nix born 1824; 
2 CONC and Lucretia Nix born 1826. 
2 CONT      Obediah had problems with a leg, and when the family was forced to leave Madison County Tennessee they left on a pony cart, with a pony pulling it. With Luvicy Nix and the 2 oldest children  walking and Obediah and the 2 youn
2 CONC gest children riding in the pony cart, the family walked to Illinois, where 5 other children were born - Jasper Levi, Newton Thomas, Francis Marion, Harriet, and Manning Lafayette.  They are on the 1830  Schuyler Co. Illinois cens
2 CONC us and are on the 1840 and 1850 census in Brown County  Texas
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~txfannin/nixfamily.html
