2 CONT *Lady Mary Cholmondeley (1563-1625) was a litigant in a forty-year-long dispute over her father's estate. She was the wife of Sir Hugh Cholmondeley, the younger and had eight children with him.
2 CONT *She was born in 1563 to '''Christopher Holford and Elizabeth Mainwaring''' in Holford, Great Budworth, Cheshire, England and christened on January 20, 1563.[1] She married Sir Randall Brereton of Malpas but he soon died. Around 1
2 CONC 581, she married Sir Hugh Cholmondeley.[2] They had eight children, named Robert, Hatton, Hugh, Thomas, Francis, Mary, Lettice, and Frances,[1] before Sir Cholmondeley's death in 1601.[3] Mary Cholmondeley died on August 15, 1625 
2 CONC at the age of sixty-three in Vale Royal, Whitegate, Cheshire, England and was buried the next day in Malpas, Cheshire, England.[1] .....
2 CONT *From: http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary_Cholmondeley_(heiress) __________________________
