1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT It is thought that Benjamin married Elizabeth Ann Belbin sometime betweenlate 1813 and early 1814. A search of St Phillip's records to present donot show such a marriage. It is possible that the chaplain of the 73rdregiment conduc
2 CONC ted the service. Stated to have served with Governor Macquarie's 73 Corps and returned toEngland in 1837. Previously he was a militia man. After his arrival inSydney he was transferred to Hobart. Later (between 1837 and 1839) he r
2 CONC eturned as a free settler to theCambridge District in Van Dieman's Land (Now Tasmania, Australia) withhis family and the ship's passenger list shows "has gone to be with hisbrother-in-law in Hobart Town". Presumably his daughter S
2 CONC arah Ann and sonBenjamin married in that colony. A Mrs Peggy Morgan (nee Hanslow) came from Tasmania and at preset (1983)is employed on the enquiry counter with the Genealogicial Society,Sydney. Presumably she is of this line.
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT It is thought that Benjamin married Elizabeth Ann Belbin sometime betweenlate 1813 and early 1814. A search of St Phillip's records to present donot show such a marriage. It is possible that the chaplain of the 73rdregiment conduc
