2 CONC eturned as a free settler to theCambridge District in Van Dieman's Land (Now Tasmania, Australia) withhis family and the ship's passenger list shows "has gone to be with hisbrother-in-law in Hobart Town". Presumably his daughter S
2 CONC arah Ann and sonBenjamin married in that colony. A Mrs Peggy Morgan (nee Hanslow) came from Tasmania and at preset (1983)is employed on the enquiry counter with the Genealogicial Society,Sydney. Presumably she is of this line.  Ch
2 CONC ristening : Benjamin Haslow 8 Apr 1787 Gnosall Staffordshire. Military Service 1809 - 1817 Australia and Ceylon. Retired on his returnto England in 1817 M arried Elizabeh Belbin while serving in Tasmania abt1810. (no records found
2 CONC ) Returned to Tasmania with his family in 1836 Death : Benjamin Hanslow 1860 Richmond Tasmania
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
