2 NOTE CoL Floyd was killed on the 12th of
3 CONT April 1783. When the news reached Col. Preston such was the feeling
3 CONT produced by it, that Preston was never seen to smile afterwards.
3 CONT
3 CONT There is no portrait of him. CoL Floyd was six feet high,
3 CONT somewhat slender, formed symmetrically, his complexion dark, brilliant
3 CONT black eyes, very black straight hair, fine white teeth. He was remarkable
3 CONT for his great beauty, generosity of temper, kindness of heart, and undaunted
3 CONT courage.
3 CONT A Historical, Biographical and Genealogical Story of the TULEYS and the FLOYD FAMILY Connection in Virginia, Kentucky and Indiana" by William Floyd Tuley, 1906, attributes this sketch to "an old crayon owned by Col. R. T. Durrett 
3 CONC of Louisville, the only picture existant of Floyd." The crayon is now in the Filson Club, Louisville
