2 CONT http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/s/t/e/Pat-M-Stevens-iv/GENE6-0011.html
2 CONT
2 CONT 18. JEMIMA5 FLOYD (WILLIAM4, JOHN3, CHARLES2, JOHN1)[157],[158] 
2 CONT *was born 1753 in Amherst Co., VA [159]. 
2 CONT *She married (1) JOHN LEMASTER [160],[161] 1768 in Amherst Co., VA or Henry Co., KY [162]. 
2 CONT **He was born 1749 in Amherst Co., VA [163], and 
2 CONT **died 16 September 1781 in Floyd's defeat by Indians, near present day Eastwood, KY [164]. 
2 CONT *She married (2) JAMES A. STURGIS [165] 28 May 1784 in Jefferson Co., KY [166],[167], 
2 CONT **son of JAMES A STURGIS and MARGARET. He was born Abt. 1756, and 
2 CONT **died Aft. 1810168. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for JEMIMA FLOYD:
2 CONT
2 CONT From B. Frank Reinauer III: Jemima Floyd appears to be one of Col. John Floyd's younger sisters. Anna M. Cartlidge gives her year of birth as 1753 (in Virginia). She married (1)ca. 1769, John Lemaster (b. ca. 1749; died 16 Sep 178
2 CONC 1 -- during Floyd's defeat); (2) bond posted 28 May 1784, Jefferson County, KY, James A'Sturgus, Jr. (b. ca. 1760; lived 1810 in Bullitt County, KY according to the census) 
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT Jo Lee Brooks Potts, <Jo0608@aol.com>, writes in June 2001: " Dear Pat, Thank you for your website. I am a descendant of Jemima Floyd. Thank you." I asked her for corrections or additions. 
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT From Alex Luken: "Pat-- Jo Nell sent me this from something called the Lemaster book... 'I found them.... see the Lemaster book page 83. Issue 70 Eleazer Lemaster b abt 1749 d Sept 16-22, 1781 near Louisville, Ky., killed by India
2 CONC ns m abt 1768 Jemima Floyd b 1753 Amherst Co. Va. After the death of Eleazer Lemaster she m2 in Jefferson Co., Ky., May 28, 1784 James A' Sturgus Jr. by whom she has issue: Cynthia A'Sturgus who m Jan 23 1800 William Pope. Jemima 
2 CONC Lemaster received land grant of 400 acres on Beech Fork, Jefferson, Co. Ky May 10 1784.' " 
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT This 400 acres might be the same as referenced here (courtesy of Alex Luken): 
2 CONT
2 CONT "At a Court held for Jefferson County, the 3rd of December, 1781. It appearing to the Court that the following Persons, are entitled by virtue of an Act of Assembly passed May last, to four hundred acres of land, each. Orders that
2 CONC  the County Surveyor lay off to them accordingly, viz: (among the many names listed is Jemima Lemaster)" 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for JOHN LEMASTER:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elton L. Powell sent this to Rootsweb in February 2003: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 'THE LEMASTER FAMILY IN THE USA,' Call #- APV [Lemaster], Howard M. Lemaster, in the Book Location: New York Public Library, Genealogy Section, 1st Floor, 42nd and 5th Ave. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "According to the early History as outlined in this Book, the Lemaster name, with it's many variations, started out with one Claude Le Maistre, [or Glaude I], spelled it with a 'G'], who died in 1683, and refers everyone to see 'A
2 CONC  History of Harlem' for more info on the Lemasters. [I have no info on that book]. And, like I said; he quotes from 'the Cabells and Their Kin' by Alex. Cabell. In the 1700's the name became Le Maitre in Europe. The part about the
2 CONC  Lemaster- Floyd connection is also covered in this book. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Most of the families are listed by the Head of the house. That's all I have for now." 
2 CONT
2 CONT -
2 CONT
2 CONT In march 2006 Alex Luken sent this: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Title: LeMaster genealogy, 1644-1962 
2 CONT *Authors: Goen, Sarah Pope LeMaster , 1914- (Main Author) 
2 CONT *Times-dispatch (Richmond, Virginia) (Added Author) 
2 CONT *Also on microfilm. Salt Lake City : Filmed by the Genealogical Society of Utah, 1982. on 1 microfilm reel ; 35 mm. 
2 CONT *FHL US/CAN Film 1035997 Item 2 
2 CONT
2 CONT LeMaster genealogy, 1644-1962 
2 CONT *Stmnt.Resp. 
2 CONT *contributed by Mrs. Rayburne Wyndham Goen 
2 CONT *Authors: Goen, Sarah Pope LeMaster, 1914- (Main Author) 
2 CONT *Times-dispatch (Richmond, Virginia) (Added Author) 
2 CONT *Notes: Typescript. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Photocopy of transcript (some typewritten, some handwritten) by M. Herberger; transcript was of genealogical column published in the 2 May 1909 issue of The Times Dispatch (Richmond, Virginia). Includes Armistead, Asturges (Asturg
2 CONC us, Sturges), Field, Floyd, Goen, Pope and related families. John LeMaster (d.1784) immigrated to Virginia, and married Jemima Floyd, a daughter of Wales immigrant William Floyd (d.1783). John died in an Indian fight near Louisvil
2 CONC le, Virginia (later Kentucky). John Floyd LeMaster (ca.1769-1807) married twice, and moved from Virginia to Bullitt County, Kentucky. Descendants and relatives lived in Virginia, Kentucky, Tennessee, Mississippi, Colorado and else
2 CONC where. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Subjects: LeMaster, Armistead, Asturges, Sturges, Field, Floyd, Goen, Pope 
2 CONT
2 CONT More About JOHN LEMASTER:
2 CONT *Burial: Eastwood, KY on the Louisville- Frankfort Road. There is a monument
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for JAMES A. STURGIS:
2 CONT *Also recorded as James A' Sturgis and A'Sturgus and A' Sturgus and more.... And court records also report Austinguss, Austengus, and Austergess. Good grief.... I think his name is Jim Sturgis..... 
2 CONT
2 CONT ....and this note from a probable descendant: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 16 Dec 2000 From: Jim Sturgis <jim.sturgis@mindspring.com> ...I am researching my Sturgis/Sturgus/Sturges line, and located your information on James A. Sturgis, b. abt 1752, who married Jemima Floyd on 28 May 1784 in Jefferson Co
2 CONC unty, KY.... My gg-grandfather was William Floyd Sturgus, b. abt 1789 in KY, d. 1852 in AL, m. Eliza Williams Gresham. The link between William and his ancestors in KY is not yet known, but with the middle name "Floyd" there may b
2 CONC e some connection to Jemima Floyd. Do you know of any children of James A. Sturgis and Jemima Floyd, or indeed, anything about the family of James? Jemima's family seems well documented. The name "Minor" appears in our family and 
2 CONC was my father's middle name as it is mine. (Editor: there are several Miner or Minor or Minart A'Stugusses, et al....) Any assistance would be greatly appreciated. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jim Atlanta 
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT ...and from Alex Luken: James A'Sturgis was one of the earliest settlers in Jefferson County. Sturgis Station is located near the home the Bullitts, which is still occupied by members of the family. If you follow Beargrass Creek, 
2 CONC moving northeast, you would have Floyd Station, then about a mile away, Low Dutch Station, then about 1.5 miles away, Sturgis Station. I believe the spring house from Sturgis Station is still standing. Most of my reseach and my in
2 CONC terest in the Floyds is through their attachment to the Fontaine family, which also has ties to the Minor Family. There were Minors in Jefferson County at that time as well.... 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alex Luken later writes that the basic Sturgis family appears to be as follows: 
2 CONT *James A'Sturgis Sr. m. Margaret ? received 400 acre land warrant 6/1/1780 on Harrods Trace. I believe he may have come from VA or MD. Functioned as a skilled boatbuilder for George Rogers Clark. There are four known sons: 
2 CONT *1. John A'Sturgus -- moved to Missouri no dates per Early Settlers of Jeffersontown and Southeastern Jefferson Co. Could not find marriage in Jefferson Co. 
2 CONT *2. James A'Sturgus Jr.--speculation: b. 1754 d. 1816 married 1st Mary Ogelby (DAR) This age would be too young to be James Sr. Jemima would be the wrong age to marry James Sr. if Margaret was the mother of Sr.'s sons at the time 
2 CONC of Sr's death. 
2 CONT *3. Peter A'Sturgus married Ann "Nancy" Tyler. Established A'Sturgus Station spring 1780. Springhouse still stands on Oxmoor Farm. Mentioned in Sr.'s will daughter Margaret A'Sturgus, daughter of Peter, deceased. Peter died at Flo
2 CONC yd's Defeat, aka Long Run Massacre. (As did Jemima's husband Eleazar LeMaster.) Peter is credited with being the nephew of John Floyd, but in 1780 John Floyd was too young to have a nephew old enough to do that, unless Margaret wa
2 CONC s his sister, or Margaret was Margaret Buchanan, sister of Jane Buchanan. That's a possibility. She was widowed by the time the family moved to KY so James Sr. could have been her second husband. Anyhow, 8/16/1785 Nancy Tyler A'St
2 CONC urgus married Capt. James Denny. She married 3rd Michael Humble. 
2 CONT **This gets to be an interesting twist: Marriage Book 1 page 29 2/19/1798 John LEMASTER marries Peggy ASTURGUS, bond is posted by William POPE Jr. 
2 CONT *4. Minard (Minert, Miner, Minor) A'Sturgus predeceased his father. Moved to Vincennes IN and is presumed killed by Indians ca. 1786. There is a lot on information on this family with the Vincennes DAR and the Northern CA DAR. Hav
2 CONC e correspondence and will send it. There is a Minard Sturgis who was a professor at Hanover College that I presume is from this family. There are bible records for this family with the Vincennes DAR. There was only one son, Robert
2 CONC . Interestingly, a Robert A'Sturgus pops up in Jefferson Co. early 1800's but is most likely a cousin. Married Ann Mayes, daughter of Robert and Elizabeth Mayes. Miner Sturgis was born 1/26/1759. Descendants of this line dropped t
2 CONC he A' but continued to use A. as a middle initial. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jefferson Co. Marriages of interest-- pay attention to the names-- Book 1 page 25 11/1/1796 John SPEED to Abigail LAMASTER, stepfather James A'STURGUS Jr. bond posted by William POPE Jr. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1/23/1800 William POPE Jr. to Cynthia STURGUS father James A'STURGUS (I have seen reference that this is a different James than our James, but I believe that it is one and the same. I don't think that Jemima Floyd LeMaster is her 
2 CONC mother though.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 x 153 5/5/1824 James STURGUS to Penelope FIELD, daughter of Abner FIELD, bond William H. POPE 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 x 7 8/18/1788 James LEMASTER to Mary IRWIN, daughter of William Irwin, deceased. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 x 38 John LEMASTER to Elizabeth BEELER, daughter of Charles Beeler 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 x 73 8/4/1812 Thomas BEELER to Sarah P. FLOYD daughter of Nathaniel Floyd 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 x 28 2/26/1815 George L. ROGERS to Jane B. FLOYD daughter of Charles Floyd 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 x 9 1/21/1790 Thomas Smith to Abba FLOYD daughter of Will Floyd bond Robert Floyd 
2 CONT
2 CONT The following comes from the ROGERS INDEX at the Filson Club. There are two entries with slightly different information. Source: M. L. Clark's Record 
2 CONT
