2 CONT *8. 51.	viii.	 	COLONEL FOUNTAIN R. FLOYD, 
2 CONT **b. 26 August 1796, VA; 
2 CONT **d. 10 January 1887, Beaumont, TX.
2 CONT *9. 	ix.	 	ABIGAIL DAVIS FLOYD [204], 
2 CONT **b. 30 March 1798, KY [204],[205],[206]; 
2 CONT **m. JOSEPH L. KING; b. 1811 [207].
2 CONT ***Notes for ABIGAIL DAVIS FLOYD: Abigail's dates are a mixture, and Anna Cartlidge explains why in her "These, too, are Our Ancestors," an undated typescript: 
2 CONT ****"She was some thirteen years older than her husband, Joseph King, and she was very anxious to keep the fact a secret. Consequently she informed the census taker in 1850 that she was born in 1803; in 1860 she told him it was 18
2 CONC 05; but by the time 1870 rolled around, she had lowered the date to 1800. Actually the bible says she entered this world on March 30, 1797." Adding to the confusion, Anna elsewhere reports her birth as 20 March 1798. 
2 CONT *10.	x.	 	SARAH P. FLOYD [208], 
2 CONT **b. 04 July 1799 [208],[209],[210]; 
2 CONT **d. Bef. 1850, probably KY; 
2 CONT **m. JOHN LEWIS TUTT [211], 31 October 1825, Todd Co., KY; 
2 CONT ***b. 1805, KY; 
2 CONT ***d. Aft. 1850, probably KY.
2 CONT *11. 	xi.	 	MARY W. FLOYD [211], 
2 CONT **b. 15 November 1800 [212],[213],[214],[215]; 
2 CONT **d. Bef. 03 May 1823 [216]; 
2 CONT **m. WILLIAM PERKINS [217], 08 March 1822, Jefferson Co., KY; 
2 CONT ***b. 1789, MA; 
2 CONT ***d. 30 July 1850, Louisville, KY.
2 CONT ****Notes for MARY W. FLOYD: Probably died in childbirth. 
2 CONT *12. 52.	xii.	 	CYNTHIA STEWART FLOYD, 
2 CONT **b. 26 July 1802, Jefferson Co., KY; 
2 CONT **d. 26 April 1874, Tazewell or Bond Co., IL.
2 CONT *13. 	xiii.	 	THOMAS FLOYD [218], 
2 CONT **b. 26 May 1804, KY [218],[219],[220]; 
2 CONT **d. Tomberlin Branch in Todd Co., KY.
2 CONT ***Notes for THOMAS FLOYD: Alan Pearson, <alpearso37@aol.com>, April 2002 was kind to send this information: 
2 CONT ****"Hi Pat, This note is to correct some info which I sent you last year about Thomas Floyd. 
2 CONT ****"I have recently learned that the "Thomas" Floyd described in our family history written by my g-uncle U.D.Rhodes in the 1940's was really Charles Thomas Floyd and NOT the Thomas who was the son of of Charles Floyd and Mary St
2 CONC ewart. I would appreciate it if you would remove the info I gave you from your Rootsweb site for Thomas Floyd (ID 14034). (ed.: This is removed and I am posting this note where the info was.....) According to my new info, Charles 
2 CONC Thomas Floyd (b. 1806 NC, d. 1829 Todd KY) m. Mary Christian (b. 1802 VA, d. 1836 Todd KY). They had 9 children including William Moten Floyd (my ancester) and Caziah Floyd who married Charles Stuart Floyd (son of Charles Floyd an
2 CONC d Mary Stewart). 
2 CONT ****"Sorry for the mix up......... Al Pearson" 
2 CONT ***Thanks to Al for this correction. 
2 CONT *14. 53.	xiv.	 	JAMES HARVEY FLOYD, 
2 CONT **b. 23 June 1806, Jefferson Co., KY; 
2 CONT **d. 02 April 1889, Tazewell Co., IL.
2 CONT
