1 TITL Capt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''John Peartree Burks II''' was the son of John Peartree Burks and Sarah Isham.  He was born c.1740 in Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Burks, wife Mary, and their children left Virginia and settled briefly in Spartanburg District, South Carolina. By 1773, they settled about sixty miles north of Augusta, Georgia, in the area that became Wilkes County. John an
2 CONC d Mary had five sons and three daughters at the time they settled in Georgia. After arriving in Georgia, they had at least four more children.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1779, John Burks secured a Captain's commission in the Georgia Militia. His son Isham raised a company of men in the same year, and served under his father's command.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the Revolutionary War, John remained in Wilkes County, Georgia for several years. There are many land transactions for him in Wilkes and Taliaferro Counties, Georgia. In the late 1790's, John and Mary return to South Carolin
2 CONC a. By March 19, 1811, he is in Lincoln County, Tennessee. That is the last document for Capt. John Burks. He is believed to have died in Lincoln County, Tennessee between 1811 and 1817.
2 CONT
2 CONT This John Burks is often confused with John Burks (1779-1826) who was also born in Virginia, but who settled in Barren County, Kentucky. Both had wives named Mary who were born in Virginia. The wife of John Burks of Barren County 
2 CONC was Mary Kedrick, daughter of John Kendrick or Kindrick. 
2 CONT
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT *http://files.usgwarchives.net/ga/wilkes/bios/burksfam.txt
2 CONT *http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/w/y/a/Michael-J-Wyatt-OH/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0454.html
