2 CONT Richard (son of the first Robert) married Ann Smith and had sons, Richard, Obadiah and John. Also daughters, Elizabeth, married to Thomas Morton, and, secondly, to Edward Goode; Judith, to Jacob Micheaux; Mary to Richard Truemand,
2 CONC  and Agnes to Joseph Morton.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT '''Richard Woodson'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Woodson, born in 1662 and died 4 Mar 1716 at Longdale in Henrico County, Virginia. The son of Robert Woodson and Elizabeth Ferris, and the husband Ann Smith, who he married 1680 in Henrico County, Virginia; the daughter of
2 CONC  Lt. Colonel John Smith of Turkey Island.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/11295993/richard-woodson Richard Woodson's Find A Grave Memorial ID # 11295993]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT He held 180 acres in Henrico County, 1704. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His brother Robert on 4 March 1716/7 deeded to his "loving cozens (nephews) Capt. Obadiah Woodson, John Woodson and Joseph Woodson, sons of Richard Woodson, deceased," 498 acres in Henrico County, being the third part of a patent 
2 CONC to Robert Woodson dated 23 Dec 1714, and the same day conveyed 80 acres to his "loving Cozen Richard Woodson," son of Richard, deceased.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://archive.org/stream/jstor-1915487/1915487#page/n6/mode/1up Page 6] of "Woodson Family" , an article from The William and Mary Quarterly, Volume 11.
2 CONT
2 CONT Woodson, Richard (son of the first Robert) married Ann Smith and had 3 sons and 4 daughters. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Richard
2 CONT * Obadiah
2 CONT * John 
2 CONT * Elizabeth, married to Thomas Morton, and, secondly to Edward Goode; 
2 CONT * Judith to Jacob Micheaux
2 CONT * Mary to Richard Truemand
2 CONT * Agnes to Joseph Morton. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources/links  
2 CONT * [https://archive.org/stream/jstor-1915487/1915487#page/n6/mode/1up Page 6] of Woodson Family Author Tyler, Lyon G. Collections jstor_willmaryquar, jstor_ejc, additional_collections, journals Contributor JSTOR
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/11295993/richard-woodson
2 CONT * https://archive.org/details/historicalgeneal01wood/page/59/mode/2up?view=theater
2 CONT * https://archive.org/details/jstor-1915487/page/n6/mode/1up?view=theater
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT III * 8 Richard,3 born about 1662, at Curles in Henrico county, married Ann Smith, daughter of Obadiah Smith. In 1729 he made a deed to James Hambleton, for land in Henrico, being part of a tract granted to his father 3 Robert Woo
2 CONC dson2 in October, 1704. As he was about sixty-seven years old at the time of making this deed, he probably died within a few years thereafter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Anne Smith and Richard Woodson are:
2 CONT
2 CONT i. Joseph Woodson.
2 CONT ii. John Woodson was born ABT. 1697. He married Elizabeth Anderson ABT. 1720, daughter of Thomas Anderson.  [NO - that’s a different John Woodson] 
2 CONT iii. Elizabeth Woodson was born ABT. 1699, and died ABT. 1740. She married Thomas Morton ABT. 1718, son of John (James) Morton and Joanna Hughes. He was born ABT. 1690, and died BET. 9 FEB 1730/31 - APR 1731. She married Edmund Go
2 CONC ode AFT. 20 SEP 1740.
2 CONT iv. Richard (Baron) Woodson was born AFT. 1701 in Henrico County, Virginia, and died BET. 21 SEP 1770 - JAN 1775. He married Anne Madeline (Nannie) Michaux BET. 1726 - 1731, daughter of Abraham Michaux and Susanna Rochet. She was 
2 CONC born ABT. 1710 in "Michaux Grant," Prince Edward County, Virginia, and died ABT. 1796.
2 CONT v. Judith Woodson was born 1703 in Henrico County, Virginia. She married Jacob Michaux BEF. 1727, son of Abraham Michaux and Susanna Rochet. He was born ABT. 1695, and died BET. 13 DEC 1744 - 15 JAN 1744/45.
2 CONT vi. Mary Woodson was born ABT. 1707 in Henrico County, Virginia. She married Richard Truman , Jr. BEF. 3 SEP 1739. He died AFT. 3 NOV 1772.
2 CONT vii. Agnes Woodson was born 27 FEB 1710/11 in Henrico County, Virginia, and died 10 MAR 1802 in Charlotte County, Virginia. She married Joseph Morton , Jr. 1736 in Lunenburg County, Virginia, son of Joseph Morton and Elizabeth Dav
2 CONC is. He was born 27 DEC 1709 in Prince Edward County, Virginia, and died 28 JUN 1782 in Charlotte County, Virginia.
2 CONT viii. Obediah Woodson was born ABT. 1712, and died BET. 9 SEP 1766 - 21 NOV 1767. He married Constance Watkins ABT. 1734, daughter of John Watkins and Elizabeth Sullivan. She was born ABT. 1715, and died BET. 17 JUL - 15 NOV 1773.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
