1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://wc.rootsweb.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=:3227371&id=I13931 ID: I13931 
2 CONT Name: John West HUDDLESTON 1 Sex: M Birth: 1802 in Virginia 1 
2 CONT Death: 1850 in Oregon Co., Mo. 1
2 CONT Father: Abraham HUDDLESTON b: 1773 in Pennsylvania  Mother: Mary ALLEN b: ABT 1777 in Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Mary "Polly" BATY b: 1800 in Kentucky
2 CONT Married: 21 JUN 1823 in Pope County, Illinois 
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT # Margaret L. "Peggy" HUDDLESTON b: 1 APR 1824 in Missouri
2 CONT # Abraham H. HUDDLESTON b: 1827
2 CONT # John George HUDDLESTON b: 5 OCT 1828
2 CONT # Mary "Polly" HUDDLESTON b: 1831
2 CONT # Sarah Malinda "Sally" HUDDLESTON b: 10 SEP 1833
2 CONT # Nathan Wesley HUDDLESTON b: 1838
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: Title: 1977824.ged Author: Sharon Scott,  Repository:  Media: Electronic Text: Date of Import: Apr 17, 2002
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/80186325/person/210074062848 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 27 2019, 14:17:37 UTC''
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://familysearch.org/tree/person/details/L6TM-DQT FamilySearch Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 25 2020, 18:02:39 UTC''
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Not sure about his middle name/initial.
2 CONT He was born in Smith Co, TN where his father had moved in 1794.
2 CONT About 1818/19 his father and family moved to Pope Co, IL, leaving some Huddleston relatives in TN.
2 CONT
2 CONT His father and most of his family moved to Oregon County, MO in 1821, but John did not.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Mary Baty in Pope Co, IL in 1823, then moved to Oregon Co, MO about 1828, probably bringing his widowed mother-in-law with them.  (She signed a consent for her daughter Margaret to marry in Pope Co, IL in Apr 1825).  Jo
2 CONC hn's son, Abraham was born in Illinois in 1827 and son John George was born in Missouri in Oct., 1828.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1830 (Wayne Co, MO) he has a boy living with him b 1815-20. He could not have been married before Mary Baty and had a son because he was living with his father in 1820, then married in 1823 (age 21).
2 CONT
2 CONT When they finally came to Missouri, they settled by the rest of his family near Thomasville in Oregon Co. The counties changed (from Wayne to Ripley to Oregon), but he never moved away from the Huddleston settlement near Thomasvil
2 CONC le. His parents and all of his siblings died there.
2 CONT
2 CONT Possibly died before 1850. In 1850 his wife, Mary, was in Oregon Co, Mo. with her 3 children:
2 CONT Mary Huddleston (40 b Ky), John G. (21 b Mo), Sarah M. (17 b Mo), Nathan W. (13 b Mo)
2 CONT
2 CONT Others say his date of death was Feb 4, 1858. There were other Huddleston men who died around that time: his father Abe Sr. died Feb 1, 1858. His brother Abe Jr died Feb 4, 1858. His brother Joseph died Dec 1857. (There was a worl
2 CONC dwide influenza epidemic in 1857-58, perhaps the cause of these deaths.)
2 CONT
2 CONT His burial place is uncertain, but it was probably in the now defunct Thomas/Lashley cemetery near Thomasville, where possibly several of his family was buried.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT # Margaret L. "Peggy" Jolliff - # 15497219
2 CONT # Abraham Marshall - 
2 CONT # John George - # 14923518
2 CONT # Mary "Pop" Dunkin 
2 CONT # Sarah Malinda "Sally" Maulding
2 CONT # Nathan Wesley
