1 NOTE From :   khramsay*juno 
2 CONT To :   ncimino
2 CONT Subject :   Venables  
2 CONT Date :   Tue, 16 Sep 2003 11:23:51 -0400  
2 CONT I saw a post on the internet of yours that had a Jacob M. Venable married
2 CONT to a Lucy Smith Robertson (b. 5 Oct 1814).  Jacob is my husband's gg
2 CONT grandfather. I would be interested in any info you could send me.  I have
2 CONT a lot of info on Jacob after he moved to Missouri, but nothing in
2 CONT Virginia.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Thanks,
2 CONT Stephanie Ramsay
2 CONT Florida
2 CONT
2 CONT My husband's line comes through Jacob M. Venable's second wife,
2 CONT Dosha Harding.  Jacob married Dosha in Missouri, and I am guessing that
2 CONT is where Lucy must have died since Jacob and Lucy's son's birthplace is
2 CONT listed as Missouri on the census.  Any ideas about Lucy's death?  
2 CONT
2 CONT Thanks again for all your help.
2 CONT
2 CONT More from Stephanie Ramsay:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob M VENABLE
2 CONT Born: 1808 in Virginia  Notes: 1,2,3,4
2 CONT Died:  Oct 1882 in Dalton, Chariton, Missouri
2 CONT Buried: Venable Cemetery, Bowling Green Twp, Chariton, Missouri
2 CONT Married 1st to Lucy ROBERTSON on 24 Sep 1833  in Amelia Co., Virginia. Lucy died before Dec 1846 in Missouri.
2 CONT Other Spouse
2 CONT Dosha A HARDING
2 CONT Married: 16 Dec 1846 in Keytesville, Chariton, Missouri
2 CONT Jacob's father: John Holcombe VENABLE
2 CONT Jacob's mother: Dorothy GLENN
2 CONT The only child of Jacob Venable and Lucy Robertson was William VENABLE born about 1835 in Missouri.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob M VENABLE
2 CONT In the 1870 census there is a Jessie Venable, age 45, male, born in Missouri living with Jacob.  Jessie is listed 
2 CONT as being Black.  Living next door in the same census are Venable, Martha (age 46, female, born in Virginia), 
2 CONT Rutha ( age 12, female, born in Missouri), and Fannie (age 65, female, born in Virginia).  All Black.
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT   1. 
2 CONT 1850 Census, Chariton County, Missouri, House #671, Keytesville Twsp., 5 Oct 1850.
2 CONT "Venable, Jacob, age 42, male, farmer, value of estate 1300, born in Virginia."
2 CONT   2. 
2 CONT 1860 Census, Chariton County, Missouri, Page 74, Keytesville, Twsp., 18 Jul 1860.
2 CONT "Venable, Jacob, age 52, male, farmer, value of real estate 5700, value of personal estate 18,225, born in 
2 CONT Virginia."
2 CONT   3. 
2 CONT 1870 Census Chariton County, Missouri, Page 30, #172/178.
2 CONT "Venable, Jacob, age 62, male, born in Virginia."
2 CONT   4. 
2 CONT Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, 1880 United States Census on CD, Bowling Green Twsp., Chariton, 
2 CONT Missouri Page 483B.
2 CONT "Venable, Jacob M., married, white, male, age 71; Relation to head of household: Self; Occupation: Farmer; Born 
2 CONT in  Virginia; Father born in Virginia; Mother born in Virginia."
2 CONT   5. 
2 CONT Couch, Robert, 
2 CONT Chariton County, Missouri Cemeteries 
2 CONT , Family History Library, 35 North West Temple, Salt Lake 
2 CONT City, Utah 84150, 977.825 V38c.
2 CONT "Venable, Jacob M. 1812-1882."
2 CONT   6. 
2 CONT Elizabeth Prather Ellsberry, 
2 CONT Chariton County, Missouri Marriages 
2 CONT , Family History Library, 35 North West Temple, 
2 CONT Salt Lake City, Utah 84150, 6125615.
2 CONT "Jacob Venable to Dosha A. Harding 16 Dec 1846 by B.H. Spencer."
2 CONT   7. 
2 CONT 1850 Census, Chariton County, Missouri, House #671, Keytesville Twsp., 5 Oct 1850.
2 CONT "Venable, William, age 15, male, born in Missouri."
