2 TITL Joseph Bragg (abt 1691-1747)
1 NOTE from the Douglas Register page 100
2 CONT Brags, John & Frances Marks:  26 Dec 1781
2 CONT
2 CONT From Dec. of Joseph Bragg by Damon Floyd:
2 CONT John Bragg was born in 1733.  He married Frances Marks, daughter of John Marks Sr and Hannah at Goochland Co. VA.  He died circa 1812 at Fluvanna Co. VA
2 CONT Note: CENSUS: 1810 census for Fluvanna Co., VA lists Bragg, John Township: Fluvanna County: Fluvanna State: Virginia  Year: 1810 Roll: M252_68 Page: 285 Image: 549. He is listed with 1 male under 10, 1 10-16, 1 over 45; 1 female u
2 CONC nder 10, 2 16-26, 1 over 45. There is also a John Bragg, Jr. listed with 1 male 26-44; 3 females under 10 and 1 26-44.
2 CONT
2 CONT  On 4 August 1752 at Richmond Co., Virginia, the court records showed "John Bragg against Sir Marmaduke Beckwith for being a witness. Court ordered Beckwith to pay 50 pounds of tobacco to John Bragg."44
2 CONT On March 6, 1758 at Richmond Co, VA,  John Bragg was granted a certivicate for obtaining letters of administration on estate of Elizabeth Bragg, dec'd. with John Ford his security.  John Edison, Matthew Kelly, Henry Suttle, and Wi
2 CONC m William (sic0 or any 3 appointed to appraise the slaves (if any) and personal estate of Elizabeth Bragg dec'd. and return an inventory to next court.
2 CONT On Dec 1, 1778 at Fluvanna Co, VA, John bought 99 acres of land on Roundabout Creek adjoining lands of Elias Williams and Wilson Milses-Cary from John Pierce. (signature shows John Pace and wife Nancy)
2 CONT On 5 Oct 1797 at Fluvanna Co, VA. John purchased 67 acres fromWlias Wills, Sr. bounded by John Bragg's land on the  west, James Cole and Absalom Applebery on the west & southwest, William Johnson and Caleb Stone on the south east 
2 CONC and east and by the land bought of Lisle byDavid Ross on the east and which will fully appear on a patent granted to said Elias Wills bearing the date March 1, 1773.
2 CONT Douglas Register includes on page 100 "BRAGS, John & Frances Marks 26 Dec 1781 (under marriages not recorded by Rev. William Douglas)
2 CONT also Shows on page 161 Jo: Brags & Francis Marks a Son Marks born Dec 26, 1781. Baptized May 26, 1782 (p 106) and Jo: Bragg & Francis Marks a son Elias born Sep: 12 1784. Baptized May 14, 1787. (p 118)
2 CONT and on page 162 Jo: Bragg & Francis Marks a daughter Susanna born April 8, 1786. baptized May 14, 1787 (p 118)
2 CONT Name: John Bragg
2 CONT  Given Name: John Surname: Bragg NSFX: Sr. Title: Sr. Sex: M Birth: 1733 Death: ABT 1812 in Fluvanna County,Virginia Note:
2 CONT On 4 August 1752 at Richmond Co., Virginia, the court records showed "John Bragg against Sir Marmaduke Beckwith for being a witness. Court ordered Beckwith to pay 50 pounds of tobacco to John Bragg."44   On 6 March 1758 at Richmon
2 CONC d Co., Virginia, John Bragg was granted a certificate for obtaining letters of administration on estate of Elizabeth Bragg, dec'd, with John Ford his security. John Edison, Matthew Kelly, Henry Suttle & Wim William (sic) or any 3 
2 CONC appointed to appraise the slaves (if any) and personal estate of Elizabeth Bragg dec'd and return an inventory to next court.18   On 1 December 1778 at Fluvanna Co., Virginia, John bought 99 acres of land on Roundabout Creek adjoi
2 CONC ning lands of Elias Williams and Wilson Miles-Cary from John Pierce. (signature shows John Pace and wife Nancy).47   On 5 October 1797 at Fluvanna Co., Virginia, John purchased 67 acres from Elias Wills, Sr bounded by John Bragg's
2 CONC  land on the west, James Cole and Absalom Appleberry on the west & southwest, William Johnson and Caleb Stone on the south east and east and by the land bought of Lisle by David Ross on the east and which will fully appear on a pa
2 CONC tent granted to said Elias Wills bearing the date 1 March 1773
