1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Adams migrated, in 1742, with parents and siblings to the Childrey Creek area of Halifax County, Virginia.  He was a Revolutionary War soldier (probably in the Patrick County Platoon).  In 1793 Captain Char
2 CONC les Foster, of Patrick County called him, "Battalion William Adams, Lieutenant". "Col. Abraham of the Continental Army was commissioned to raise a comapny from the territory which now includes Franklin, Henry and Patrick Counties,
2 CONC   Included in this militia were platoons from the Patrick territory led by Hamon Critz, George Hairston, and John Reutfro.  This company was the only organized militia to leave the territory. (from the internet- Patrick County).  
2 CONC He bought land in Henry County, Virginia on January 10, 1790 with witnesses Henry Sumpter ( son of Absalom Adams's father in law) and 
2 CONT
2 CONT William's son, John Adams.  John Adams, Absalom's brother, (b. 1772 moved to Harrison County, Kentucky in 1805-1807 and died there in 1819.  James Swinford, James Hiks, and John Owings.  William Adams ( Absalom's father) moved to 
2 CONC Harrison County, Kentucky prior to 1789.  In 1819 an indenture of Alexander McNees was witnessed by William Adams and son, Absalom.   William Adams bought land in Harrison County, Kentucky in 1812 adjoining Swinford and McNees fam
2 CONC illies.  William Adams moved to Newell Township, Vermillion county, Illinoise in 1826.
