0 @I6000000000966140851@ INDI
1 NAME Charles /Smith/
2 GIVN Charles
2 SURN Smith
2 _MARNM Smith
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1655
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia Colony
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 10 AUG 1710
2 ADDR
3 STAE Province of Virginia
1 TITL Capt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 1.	Charles Smith was born Abt 1655 in Gloucester County, Virginia, and died Bef 10 Aug 1710 in Gloucester County, Virginia. He was the son of 2. Lawrence Smith and 3. Mary Debnam. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===family===
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 
2 CONT # Dorothy Peyton, daughter of Robert Peyton. She was born Abt 1663 in Gloucester County, Virginia, and must have died before 1700.
2 CONT # on 6 June 1700 in Essex County, Virginia to Dorothy Buckner, daughter of Richard Buckner.  She was born 1673 in Rappahonock County, Virginia, and died 17 Feb 1746 in Port Royal, Caroline County, Virginia.  She married 2nd to Joh
2 CONC n Roy, son of Richard.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by 1st wife 
2 CONT #  Hannah Smith b: 1680 in Caroline County, Virginia
2 CONT #  Elizabeth Smith b: Abt 1693
2 CONT #  Sarah Smith b: Abt 1695
2 CONT #  Charles Smith b: Abt 1697
2 CONT #  Lawrence Smith b: Abt 1699
2 CONT
2 CONT children by 2nd wife 
2 CONT #  Robert Smith b: 1701
2 CONT #  Dorothy Smith b: Abt 1702
2 CONT #  Peyton Smith b: 1709
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy Buckner, daughter of Richard Buckner, was born in 1673 in Rappahannock County, married Charles Smith in 1700, then, after he died in 1710, married John Roy. She was NOT the mother of Hannah Roy. Her children were Robert Sm
2 CONC ith (from the first marriage), Thomas Roy, John Roy, Jr., Reuben Roy, Mungo Roy, Richard M Roy, Mary Roy, and Elizabeth Roy.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived in Essex County and died Abt 1710 when his widow Dorothy Smith, Augustine Smith, and R. Buckner gave bond in Essex court as his Administrators.
2 CONT
2 CONT Following in the footsteps of his father, he also was a surveyor. In Essex County Records dated December 11, 1704, Charles Smith surveyed land of Major Lawrence Smith, a patent dated 26th March 1666 to his father.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also in Essex Co. Court, August 11, 1699, Augustine Smith and Charles Smith - Action brought against Elizabeth Bradley.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
