1 NAME Alexander /Womack/
2 GIVN Alexander
2 SURN Womack
2 _MARNM Womack
2 NICK James Alexander Womack
2 NICK D24
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1715
2 PLAC Dale Parish, Henrico Co, VA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1 MAR 1784
2 PLAC Campbell, Virginia, USA
2 ADDR
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He is sometimes sen as James Alexander Womack, but his will says "I, Alexander  Womack..."
2 CONT https://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/womack/996/
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Wommack and Elizabeth Puckett 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT * Thomas (~1706-~1782)
2 CONT * Matthew Born abt 1708.
2 CONT * Richard (1710-1785)
2 CONT * Sarah[5]. Born abt 1712 in Halifax County, Virginia. Sarah died in Warrenton, Warren County, Georgia in 1795, she was 83. Buried in Cody Cemetery in Warrenton, Georgia.  Notes for Sarah Womack: Sarah attached here as the child o
2 CONC f Richard Jr. although''' no proof of this connection.'''
2 CONT * '''Alexander.''' Born abt 1715 in Henrico County, VA.  Alexander died in Virginia on 1 Mar 1784, he was 69.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Alexander Womack:[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Alexander Womack,Campbell Co., VA. 1784.Campbell County Will Book 1 1782-1800,pages 38-41:
2 CONT
2 CONT " I Alexander Womack of the County of Prince Edward do hereby make this my last Will and Testament.I appoint William Watts and Richard Womack my Executors.I give to my son Richard Womack the Land he lives on in Canel County to him
2 CONC .I give to my son David Womack the Land I had of Benjamin Harrison lying in Campbell County after the decease or Widowhood of my wife Martha Womack also one feather bed and furniture and all my Plantation utensils to him.I give my
2 CONC  Grand Daughter Nancy Womack one feather bed and furniture and one cow to her.I lend to my Wife Martha Womack during her life or Widowhood my Tract of land in Camel County I had of Benjamin Harrison and all My Estate both real and
2 CONC  Personal not before Divided and after her decease or Widowhood my Will and desire is that the same be sold for the best Price that can be got Except the Land and Divided amongst my children 
2 CONT * Alexander Womack
2 CONT * Richard Womack
2 CONT * David Womack
2 CONT * Anne Drisca
2 CONT * lElizabeth Mason
2 CONT * Jean Tomison
2 CONT * Martha Rutlidge and
2 CONT * Juda Richards 
2 CONT * my son David Womack to have Twenty Pounds more than my other children.Given under my hand and seal the 26th day of August 1782.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed Sealed/S/ A. Womack(Seal)
2 CONT in Presence of
2 CONT Wm. WattsDudley McDearmonroe
2 CONT Robert Turner
2 CONT
2 CONT At a Court held for Campbell County April 1st 1784.
2 CONT The within last Will and Testament of Alexander Womack deceased was proved by the Oath of Robert Turner a Witness thereto suscribed.And at a Court held for the said County the Sixth day of May following the same were further Prove
2 CONC d by the Oath of Dudley McDearmonroe another Witness thereto suscribed and Ordered to be Recorded.And on the Motion of Richard Womack one of the Executors therein named who made oath thereto according to Law Certificate in Granted
2 CONC  him for obtaining Probate thereof in due form giving Security Whereupon he together with William Mason and Daniel Mitchell his Securities entered into and acknowledged their Bond in the Penalty of Five Hundred Pounds conditioned 
2 CONC as the Law directs for the said Executors due and faithful Administration of the said Decedants Estate and Performance of his Will, Liberty being reserved the Other Executor in the said Will named to John in the Probate thereof wh
2 CONC en he shall think fit.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Alexander Womack:
2 CONT * Fact 1: 1742, Lived in Dale Parish.
2 CONT * Fact 2: 1759, Lived in Prince Edwars County, VA.
2 CONT * Fact 3: 1782, Purchased 200 acres of land on Felpes Creek.
2 CONT
2 CONT abt 1737 when Alexander was 22, he married Martha ALEXANDER[5], in Dale Parish, Henrico County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
