2 CONT Burial:	 St. Clair, Missouri, United States. Iconium Cemetery. 1847-Founded Liberty Baptist Church Dec. 29. He was the first pastor. 1848-Founded Providence Church Jan 22. He was the first pastor. 1850-Honey Creek Church (third pa
2 CONC stor)  South Fork Church, member only. joining in 1850 Founder of South Wyaconda Church and charter member, along with his wife Isabell. 1851-Founder of Des Moines Baptist Church. First pastor. 1857-Pastor of West Providence Churc
2 CONC h for this year. 1858-Fifth pastor of Zion Church 1863-Pastor of Sand Hill and Gilead Churches 1865-Pastor of Etna Church
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1871 minutes of this association, the committee of Deceased Ministers submitted the following report: We, your Committee on Deceased Ministers, beg leave to make the following report: Dear brethren - Our Association has bee
2 CONC n heavily stricken since our last meeting; one of our venerable and much beloved ministers has fallen a victim to the monster Death - Elder C.V. Maddox is no more; and while we bow in humble submission to the dispensation of a kin
2 CONC d Providence, we can only be sensible of the great loss our body has sustained in our pulpits and deliberative bodies. Not having sufficient data from which to make an obituary we submit this notice by extending our heartfelt symp
2 CONC athy to the family of our departed brother. - Letter to Ms. Pat Meador from Center for Baptist Historical Studies.
