1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary was one of at least seven children born to Thomas Davenport (1711-1809) and Dorothy (Strother) Davenport (1712-1767). Her paternal grandparents were Martin Davenport, Sr. (1682-1735) and Dorothy (Glover) Daven
2 CONC port (1690-1767).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary married William Wiseman abt. 1761/1762 and with him had eleven children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Thomas Wiseman, b. Apr. 30, 1763 2) Dorothy Wiseman, b. Feb. 5, 1765; m. David Baker, Aug. 9, 1793 (his 2nd) 3) William Edward Wiseman, b. Aug. 5, 1767 4) Mary "Polly" Wiseman, b. Apr. 11, 1769; m. John Puett 5) Davenport Wisem
2 CONC an, b. Aug. 25, 1771 6) Martin Wiseman, b. Aug. 24, 1773 7) James Wiseman, b. Aug. 18, 1775 8) John Wiseman, b. Feb. 21, 1777 9) Celestial Wiseman, b. Oct 22, 1779 10) Susannah Wiseman, b. Dec. 16, 1781; m. Thomas Baker, Jul. 15, 
2 CONC 1802 11) Robert Wiseman, b. Jul. 14, 1784
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary and William started their family in Culpeper County, Virginia, with son Thomas. After he was born, they moved south to the Carolinas. It appears two of the children were born in South Carolina. The rest were born in North Car
2 CONC olina. They eventually settled along the North Toe River, next to the stream, Sunny Brook. Some listings show a 12th child, Nancy, but she was a grandchild. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary and three of her younger children (unknown) died from milk poisoning. They were buried on the family's, "Sunny Brook Farm" in a graveyard established at the southern end of the garden. Later, her husband William and either hi
2 CONC s second wife Lydia or son Thomas were also buried there (six graves in all). The graves were covered over when U.S. 19-E was widened. A memorial monument was placed for William in the 1940s on the east side of the highway,  about
2 CONC  36 feet from his actual grave. No mention is made of Mary or the others.  The site is now in Avery County (established in 1911),  about five miles north of Spruce Pine, Mitchell County.
2 CONT * Reference: [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=136318263 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 12 2016, 21:56:31 UTC''
