1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/63397418/william_coleman-glenn
2 CONT
2 CONT William Coleman Glenn was a member of a Continental Regiment from Cumberland County, Virginia in the American Revolution.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Nathan Glenn (1735-1805) Mother: Lucy Coleman Glenn
2 CONT
2 CONT nscription
2 CONT "He was engaged in the Revolutionary Struggles for his Country.
2 CONT The morning sun begins the day,
2 CONT So soon the night passeth away.
2 CONT The weary seek for rest,
2 CONT And in slumbering, sleep and blest.
2 CONT Youth begins the man to rear,
2 CONT Age with trouble and with care.
2 CONT Death doth bring him to rest,
2 CONT And he in Christ are blest."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Glenn-3147
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Nehemiah Glenn (ca 1724 Hanover, VA - ca. 1774 VA) & Anne Coleman (ca. 1730, dau. of Daniel Coleman & Patience Elliott), he became a planter & slave-owner in VA. He m. Frances Harris (ca 1746 - 1814) & had issue:
2 CONT
2 CONT Patience Coleman Glenn m. Samuel Wright
2 CONT
2 CONT Nehemiah Glenn
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathan Glenn
2 CONT
2 CONT Nancy Ann Glenn m. Craddock Wisdom
2 CONT
2 CONT Reuben Glenn m. Elizabeth
2 CONT
2 CONT Frances Harris Glenn m. John M. Brightwell
2 CONT
2 CONT William Glenn m. Sophia
2 CONT
2 CONT He is reported to have been in the American Revolution - Continental, Cumberland, VA, but no DAR records have been found.
2 CONT
2 CONT Will
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.archivesindex.sc.gov/ Search for "Glenn, William C." for images
2 CONT
