1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Daniel-495
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/26634422/chesley-chickeley-daniel
2 CONT ----
2 CONT there are DNA tests for both Chesley and Josiah who are cleanly documented sons of James of Albemarle, thus establishing the baseline for this family. In January of 2006 the results for a descendant of James (subject of this artic
2 CONC le, lived 1747-1820, md. Sally Cocke) were returned, a perfect 37/37 match for Chesley and Josiah, thus confirming the above record evidence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Many old write-ups place Chesley and his siblings as children of an '''Elizabeth Woodson''' and thus of a different Daniel family: it was a faulty leap, an "assignment" based probably on Judith's middle name of Woodson. The Woodso
2 CONC n name is not really a good marker for relationships; the family was such a big player in its time that everybody gave the name to children, related or not. The Woodson assignment has unfortunately become written in stone and turn
2 CONC ed to "fact" over time, but it's time for that assignment to fade away.
2 CONT
