1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Francis Watkins'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A122286 DAR Ancestor #: A122286]
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/110022917/francis_watkins
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis was the son of Thomas Watkins of Chickahominy, Virginia. As a youth and young man he was largely self taught. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On January 1, 1765 he married Agnes Woodson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT During the Revolution he served on the Prince Edward Committee of Safety. After several years as Deputy Clerk for Prince Edward County he was elected Clerk of the Court in 1783. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1776-1792 he served as a Trustee of the Hampden-Sydney College. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children included the following: Richard, Mrs. Joseph (Elizabeth) Venable, Mrs. David (Agnes Woodson) Flournoy, Judge Francis (Jr.), Benjamin, Henry Edward, Dr. Joseph, Mrs. S.L. (Selina) Lockett., & Mrs. James Daniel (Franc
2 CONC es Anderson) Wood.
2 CONT
2 CONT Poplar Hill Plantation was built by Richard Woodson in Farmville, Prince Edward County, Virginia. It was handed down to his daughter Agnes and her husband Francis Watkins. The Poplar Hill Plantation is now home to the Poplar Hill 
2 CONC Golf Club.
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis was the son of Thomas Watkins of Chickahominy, VA.  As a youth and young man he was largely self taught.  On Jan 1, 1765 he married Agnes Woodson.  During the Revolution he served on the Prince Edward Committee of Safety. 
2 CONC  After several years as Deputy Clerk for Prince Edward County he was elected Clerk  of the Court in 1783.  From 1776-1792 he served as a Trustee of the Hampden-Sydney College. Their children included the following:  Richard, Mrs. 
2 CONC Joseph (Elizabeth) Venable, Mrs. David (Agnes Woodson) Flournoy, Judge Francis (Jr), Benjamin, Henry Edward, Dr. Joseph, Mrs. S.L.(Selina) Lockett., & Mrs. James Daniel (Frances Anderson) Wood.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.
2 CONC com/memorial/110022917/francis-watkins Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 30 2026, 6:09:21 UTC''
