1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Henry Edward Watkins'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/108658067/henry_edward_watkins
2 CONT * https://reynoldspatova.org/getperson.php?personID=I17156&tree=reynolds1
2 CONT * https://www.oocities.org/heartland/ranch/8428/watkins_marriages_va.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Francis (Sr.) & Agnes Woodson Watkins. He attended Hampden-Sydney, Washington College, Princeton A.B. and William & Mary for law. He was married to Agnes Venable daughter of Samuel Woodson and Mary (Carrington) Venable. The
2 CONC y lived in a house called the "The Home" which lay about a mile from his birth place, "Poplar Hill." At "The Home" he conducted a law school.
2 CONT
2 CONT His political activities included the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT Commonwealth Attorney 1810-1813; Member of the House of Delegates 1812-1833; Member Virginia Senate 1833-34. In 1818 he was on the commission to choose the site location for the University of Virginia. He served as a Captain in th
2 CONC e War of 1812 and was involved with his company at the Battle of Bottom's Bridge.
