1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=106279386&ref=wvr
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Francis Watkins, Sr. 1745-1826 and Agnes Anne Woodson 1748-1820 both of Henrico County, Virginia. They were married June 11, 1765 in Prince Edward County Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Selina married Col. Samuel Locke Lockett 1782-aft 1850 on January 10, 1811 in Prince Edward County Virginia. He died sometime after 1850 in Mecklenburg County Virginia and she moved to Perry, Marion County, Alabama near her daught
2 CONC er Mary Clay Lockett, who married her cousin Col. Napoleon Bonaparte Lockett. Both her father and her husband were attorneys.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had three sons and five daughters. Two, and possibly all three, sons served the CSA in the Civil War. Capt. Lucius Janius Lockett, Sr. died in 1864 of disease during his service in the war. Sons Col. Henry Edmund Lockett and 
2 CONC Thomas J. Lockett moved to Brenham, Washington County Texas. Both were attorneys.
2 CONT
