2 CONT From "The Reads and Their Relatives," by Alice Read, at page 119: 
2 CONT
2 CONT       "Margaret Read, called 'Peggy,' died young, 'leaving a memory of great virtues.' Mr. Grigsby says that her loss saddened and clouded her husband's mind until he was an elderly man. He could not forget her loveliness, and rec
2 CONC ords that she was 'the best of wives and a woman of innumerable virtues.' She lived nearly eleven years after her marriage and died leaving five babies, all of whom grew to to be noble men and women."
2 CONT
