1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/221141259/mary-morton
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth 	1710 Virginia, USA
2 CONT Death 	1733 (aged 22–23) Prince Edward County, Virginia, USA
2 CONT Burial 	Goode Family Graveyard Prince Edward County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT JOSEPH MORTON OF LITTLE ROANOKE BRIDGE. Joseph Morton, b. 1709, d. June 28, 1772; m. (I) Miss-- Goode, m. (2) Agnes Woodson, b. February 27, I711, d. March 10, 1802, dau. Richard Woodson and wife Agnes Micheaux, grand-daughter Abr
2 CONC aham Micheaux and wife Susannah Rochette. Joseph Morton settled at Little Roanoke Bridge. By profession he was a surveyor. At first a staunch Episcopalian, subsequently became a staunch Presbyterian and remained so the rest of his
2 CONC  life. He became an Elder in the Briery Church. Was gentleman Justice of Prince Edward county, Va., when county was organized January 8, I754. Said to have come from Orange county, Va., and to have been employed by the Randolph fa
2 CONC mily to survey their lands. A man named John Morton is said to have been asso- ciated with Joseph Morton in surveying. What relation existed between the two men is not known. John Morton m. Elizabeth Woodson, dau. Sanborne Woodson
2 CONC . Children Ist marriage: Morton: i i. Mary, b. November, I 733. Children 2nd marriage: Morton: 12. Josiah, b. November 14, 1737, d. November 27, 1785. 13. Judith, b. December 27, I739. 14. William, b. November 27, 1743, d. Novembe
2 CONC r 29, 1820, m. October 29, 1764, Susannah Watkins. I5. Jane, b. February 14, 1745. I6. Agnes, b. February 26, 1747. p. 315
2 CONT
2 CONT 17. Little Joe, b. November 15, 1749. 18. Jacob, b. January 29, 1751, d. May 22, 1829, m. September 3, 1774, Jane D. Booker. I9. Elizabeth, b. May 14, 1754. NOTE.-This lineage I have not verified by documentary proof. D. M. p. 316
2 CONT
2 CONT The Morton Patriarchs of Virginia by Daniel Morton, The Virginia Magazine of History and Biography, Vol. 17, No. 3 (Jul., 1909), pp. 311-316, Virginia Historical Society
2 CONT ----
