1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joel Joseph Watkins married Agnes Woodson ''Morton'' b. 26 Feb 1747.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joel Watkins is the son of Thomas Watkins of Chickahomony, and Frances Ann Anderson. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas is the son of Thomas Watkins of Swift Creek, 1678 - 1760 Powhatan Co., Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT Agnes Morton who married Joel Watkins, was d/o Joseph Morton, of Little Roanoke Bridge. Charlotte Co., VA and was born 1709; d. 28 Jun 1782. 
2 CONT
2 CONT By profession he was a surveyor, Justice of the Peace of Prince Edward Co., Va when that county was formed, 8 Jan 1754. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Morton first married 
2 CONT Miss Goode; Issue: 
2 CONT 1.) Mary Morton, b. Nov 1733. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Joel married Agnes Woodson; issue: 
2 CONT 2-Josiah Morton, b 14 Nov 1737; d 27 Nov 1785; m. Elizabeth Venable
2 CONT 3) Judith Morton b. 27 Dec 1739; d. 1825 m. James Venable
2 CONT 4) Col. William Morton, b. 27 Nov 1743; d Nov 29 1820 m. Susannah Watkins
2 CONT 5) Jane Morton [m. John Carter of Charlotte Co.]
2 CONT 6) Agnes Morton, b 26 Feb 1848, m. Joel Watkins
2 CONT 7) Little Joe Morton b 15 Nov 1749
2 CONT 8) Jacob Morton, b 29 Jan 1751; d. 22 May 1829 m. 3 Sep 1774 Jane D. Booker
2 CONT Agnes Woodson, (d/o Richard and Ann Smith) was b. 1711; d. 1802; Richard Woodson was s/o Robert Woodson and Elizabeth Ferris; Robert is s/o Dr. John Woodson and wife Sara. (Genealogy of the Woodsons and their connections, compiled
2 CONC  by Henry Morton Woodson of Memphis, Tenn. Pub. 1915
2 CONT
2 CONT [S93] Sons of the American Revolution, https://www.ancestry.com/interactive/2204/32596_242044-00262?pid=42092&backurl=https://search.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/sse.dll?db%3DSARMemberApps%26h%3D42092%26indiv%3Dtry%26o_vc%3DRecord:OtherRe
2 CONC cord%26rhSource%3D7836&treeid=&personid=&hintid=&usePUB=true&usePUBJs=true.
