1 NAME Uriah /Edwards/ Sr
2 GIVN Uriah
2 SURN Edwards
2 NSFX Sr
2 _MARNM Edwards
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1714
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1781
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Shipbuilder.
2 CONT
2 CONT His parents are unknown. He may have been the son of John Edwards of King George County (d.1743) or James Edwards of King William County (d. aft.1756) both of whom owned land in Spotsylvania County in the early 18th century. He be
2 CONC gins appearing in the records of Spotsylvania County, Virginia in 1760. A 1974 reference to a family bible claims he was age 67 at his death, though this information was tangled up with "Edwards Heirs" fabrications, so the authent
2 CONC icity is not known. There is currently no evidence he was an immigrant from Wales, though that remains a possibility.
2 CONT
2 CONT His will/probate:
2 CONT
2 CONT "EDWARDS, URIAH, Berkeley Parish, Spotsylvania Co., d. Apr. 16, 1781, Executors Bond dated Aug. 17, 1781. Wit. Charles Pemberton, Edward Brasfield, Bennet Pemberton. Ex. Edward Herndon, Joseph Herndon and my son John Edwards. Leg.
2 CONC  wife Milley Edwards; son John Edwards; my four youngest children, Benjamin, Moses, Milley and Mary Edwards; my seven children, Uriah, Benjamin, Moses, Milley and Mary Edwards, Rebecca, the wife of Reuben Hawkins, and Elizabeth, t
2 CONC he wife of Elisha Hawkins. (Page 404)"[1] 
