1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Claimed 400 acres Salt River on 11/3/1779 Birth: 	Oct. 9, 1748 Lancaster County Pennsylvania, USA Death: 	Jun. 8, 1801 Mercer County Kentucky, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of James and Jane (McMichael) McAfee, married Hannah McCormick, about 1774, Botetourt County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Born on Octoraro Creek, Lancaster County, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT First magistrate of Mercer County, Kentucky.
2 CONT
2 CONT One of the founders of New Providence Presbyterian Church in Mercer County, Kentucky.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel McAfee.[31] Born in Oct 1748 in Lancaster Co., Pennsylvania. Samuel died on 7 Jun 1801 in Mercer Co., Kentucky.[32] Buried on 8 Jun 1801 in New Providence Presbyterian Cemetery, Mercer Co., Kentucky.[17] Occupation: Justice
2 CONC  of Mercer Co., KY (appointed June 28, 1792). [View a transcription of Samuel McAfee's Last Will and Testament.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Abt 1774 Samuel married Hannah McCormick, in Botetourt Co., Virginia. Born on 24 Oct 1750 in Rockbridge Co., Virginia. Was on the census for Mercer Co., Kentucky, in 1810.[33] Was on the census for Harrodsburg, Mercer Co., Kentuck
2 CONC y, in 1830.[34] Hannah died in Harrodsburg, Mercer Co., Kentucky, on 28 Jun 1833; she was 82.[35] Buried aft 28 Jun 1833 in New Providence Presbyterian Cemetery, Mercer Co., Kentucky.[36]
