1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.momslookups.com/generations/clark.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis Clark married Cordelia Langford or Lankford, daughter of Thomas Lankford, in Quaker meeting in New Kent Co. VA in 1704.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Francis Clark and Cordelia Lankford.  Birth order is uncertain.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Elizabeth Clark (d. before 1769) m. William (?) Haley
2 CONT *Sarah Clark m. Andrew Moorman [error corrected 7/6/05]
2 CONT *Thomas Clark m. Elizabeth; was her maiden name Rush?
2 CONT *John Clark, wife's name uncertain (see below)
2 CONT *Joseph Clark (d. 1774) m. Mary, maiden name unknown
2 CONT *Francis Clark m. Christian [not Christina!] Stone
2 CONT *Agnes Clark m. John(?) Haley
2 CONT *Isaac Clark (d. 1787) m. Rebecca ??
2 CONT *Ursula Clark m. Benjamin Mosby
2 CONT *Christopher Clark m. Elizabeth Stone, Christian Stone's sister
2 CONT *Benjamin Clark (d. 1766) m. Elizabeth Price
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT > NOTE FROM ORIGINAL - "The reason that I believe that Thomas Lankford was the father of John and among his children was Cordelia Lankford who married Francis Clark, is that Thomas Lankford (Sr.) was likely born at least by 1631, 
2 CONC maybe much earlier. Thomas Lankford [Jr.] appears later, after 1700 when he was married. He was likely the brother of Cordelia."
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sites.rootsweb.com/~lksstarr/reports/fraclarksr.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT > Francis Clark signed a marriage certificate in the Henrico Quaker Monthly Meeting at William Porters house when he was about 19 yrs old. (1703) On Oct. 10, 1704 he was advised by the Henrico Monthly Meeting that he must declare 
2 CONC marriage intentions with Cordelia Landford, daughter of Thomas Langford, in the New Kent particular Meeting since they were both members there.  In November, 1704, he was liberated by the Henrico Monthly Meeting to marry Cordelia 
2 CONC Langford and they were married Dec. 12, recorded by New Kent Monthly Meeting. He was born about 1683 based on the marriage date.  He would have to have been 21 to purchase land in 1704.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Langford-141
2 CONT
2 CONT > Cordelia Lankford (sometimes seen Langford) is estimated to have born about 1682 in Virginia Colony [now United States], based on her marriage. The only spelling of the name found to date in Quaker meeting minutes is Lankford. D
2 CONC ocumentation that she is the daughter of John Langford (1662 - 1741) is currently lacking.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
