1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Francis owned land in Louisa County, St. Peter's Parrish, New Kent County, St. Paul's Parrish, Hanover County, and perhaps Orange County. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1744, it is recorded that Francis Clark was overseer of the Fork Creek Meeting (Quaker), which was a satellite meeting of the Cedar Creek Meeting in Hanover County. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On the 23 of March 1756, Francis Clark made deeds of gifts to his three sons, to John Clark-365 acres of land on which John then lived, to Thomas Clark-420 acres where resided, to Francis Clark-734 acres whereon he then lived and 
2 CONC another tract of 534 acres. These deeds established the sites of the plantations of the several Clarks, who resided in the Fork Creek section of Louisa County.
2 CONT
