2 CONT Original data: Find a Grave. Find a Grave®. http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi; URL: Find A Grave: Memorial #148764502
2 CONT Ancestry Record 60541 #5048331 (accessed 7 February 2024)
2 CONT Sarah Ann Moorman's husband Andrew Moorman burial.
2 CONT Also see: Family History: "Geneanet Community Trees Index"
2 CONT Original data: Geneanet Community Trees Index. Paris, France: Geneanet
2 CONT Ancestry Record 62476 #6518908658 (accessed 7 February 2024)
2 CONT Name: Sarah Ann Clark; Gender: F (Female); Birth Date: 1713; Birth Place: Louisa, Louisa, British Colonial America (Louisa), Virginia, USA; Marriage Date: 1727; Marriage Place: New Kent, British Colony (New Kent), Virginia, USA; D
2 CONC eath Date: 1776; Death Place: Richmond, North Carolina, USA; Father: Francis Isaac Clark; Mother: Cordelia Langford; Spouse: Andrew Moorman; View on Geneanet: https://gw.geneanet.org/sssarawolf?n=clark&oc=&p=sarah+ann
2 CONT
2 CONT ————————
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Moorman, son of Thomas Moorman (2) and Elizabeth (?Simpson?), was baptized 4 November 1689, St Peter’s Parish, New Kent County, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1716, he occupied brother Charles’ property on Whyting Swamp. In 1725 he bought 400 acres in Henrico County (Virginia?) In November 1729 he purchased 280 acres of land in Hanover County, Virginia. In 1740 he sold some of Goochl
2 CONC and County, property, moving to Brunswick County, Virginia. He went to Anson County, North Carolina about 1749.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had at least two wives: Ann Diggs, whom he may have married about 1710 and Sally Clark married about 1737 in either Virginia or North Carolina; there is also a source which names a wife named Susan or Susanna, named on property
2 CONC  sold by Andrew in 1726, 1728, & 1729. Her surname may have been Reynolds.
2 CONT
