1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Lucy Adams===
2 CONT * Birth:	abt 1722 - Goochland, Virginia
2 CONT * Death:	Jan 1 1780 - Albemarle, Virginia, USA
2 CONT * Parents:	Robert Adams, Mourning Lewis
2 CONT * Husband:	John Graves, Jr.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Possibly due to failing health, Robert Addams wrote his Will in Feb 1738. His estate was left to his wife Mourning, sons James and Robert and daughters Judith Clark, Mary Moreman [Moorman], Eliza Moreman [Moorman], Agnes Farguson 
2 CONC [Ferguson], Susanna, Lucy, Anna the younger and Sally.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: before 1743 to John Graves, Jr., who was born about 1712 in VA.   He was the son of John Graves (b about 1677) & Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her sister Susannah married Matthew Graves, her husband's brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT They lived in Goochland Co., VA.  (R‑45, R‑230). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children - Graves
2 CONT #  Adam Graves, b.c. 1745, m. Mary Holland, 4 May 1769 (Goochland Co., VA).
2 CONT #  William Graves, b.c. 1748.
2 CONT #  John Graves, b.c. 1750, m(1) Elizabeth Davidson, 1772, m(2) Edith June, c. 1798, d. 1830.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources 
2 CONT * [http://www.gravesfa.org/gen169.htm Graves Family Association - Capt. Thomas Graves of VA]
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=45124477 Find A Grave Memorial# 45124477]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT John Graves, Jr. who married 1743 - Lucinda Adams, Goochland Co. VA, daughter of Robert and Mourning (Lewis) Adams, also, same on 
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthew Graves who married 1738 - Susannah Adams, Goochland Co. VA, daughter of Robert and Mourning (Lewis) Adams
2 CONT
2 CONT John Graves, Jr. was indeed married to Lucy Adams, and Matthew Graves to Susannah Adams. John and Matthew appear in early Albemarle deeds (Albemarle formed from Goochland 1745). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Proof: There are two Oct 1743, Goochland deeds (DB 4-248 & 252), "John Graves Jr. & Lucy his wife of Goochland" selling "land left by Robert Adams deceased to his daughter Lucy by his will." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Also, Mourning Adams 1765 Albemarle Deed "I Mourning Adams in pursuance of the Last Will and Testament of my well beloved husband Robert Adams Deced" names daus Lucy & Susanah Graves. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family tradition says my Martha (Graves) McClain was dau of John & Edith June Graves. Edith June said to be 2nd cousin of John Q. Adams. Probably a flawed tradition. Yet, these Adams-Graves marriages open the possibility of this b
2 CONC eing her line. Edith June is nowhere to be found.
