1 NAME Elizabeth /Reynolds/
2 GIVN Elizabeth
2 SURN Reynolds
2 _MARNM Moorman
2 NICK Renalls
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE BET 29 AUG 1674 AND 1686
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
1 BAPM
2 DATE 15 MAR 1690
2 ADDR
3 CITY Louisa
3 STAE VA
1 DEAT
2 DATE 11 MAY 1765
2 ADDR
3 CITY Green Springs
3 STAE Virginia
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Parentage disputed; Either-
2 CONT *(1) Christopher Reynolds and Elizabeth [NO]
2 CONT *(2) Thomas 'Renalls'
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles Moorman married Elizabeth Reynolds. There is some dispute as to whether she was the daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Christopher-Reynolds-II/6000000020446198787?through=6000000002906457633 Christopher Reynolds] and
2 CONC  Elizabeth, or the daughter of [https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Reynolds-II/6000000002741972229?through=6000000002906457633 Thomas “Renalls”], the recorded baptism dated 15 of March 1690-1691. The Louisa County court records si
2 CONC mply identify Charles’ wife as Elizabeth. She died in 1763.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN OF CHARLES MOORMAN & ELIZABETH (REYNOLDS):
2 CONT # Thomas Moorman - born 04 Sep 1705; married Rachel (Clark), daughter of Christopher; died 10 Nov 1767.
2 CONT # Anne Moorman - born in 1708 in Hanover Co., Virginia.
2 CONT # Achilles Moorman - born 26 Oct 1713; married Elizabeth (Adams), daughter of Robert; died in Nov 1785.
2 CONT # Judith Moorman - born in 1714; married John Douglas.
2 CONT # Charles Moorman - born in 1715; married Mary (Adams), daughter of Robert; died in 1778.
2 CONT # Mary Moorman - born 1716 in Green Springs, Virginia. (Anthony Roots & Branches list Mary as having married William Ballard whose 2nd wife was Rachel (Clark) Moorman, widow of Thomas. She lists their children as Thomas, Frances, 
2 CONC Byrum, Delphia, Moorman, and David. Other researchers insist that William Ballard's first was Mary Byrum or Byrom, therefore I have not included this information.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Probate 
2 CONT
2 CONT Probate Date: 11 MAY 1765 Place: Louisa County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT *Be it known to all men that I Elizabeth Moorman of Louisa County being of sound Mind and memory for which I desire to be made truly thankfull to the Lord calling to mind the uncertainty of this Life do make and ordaine this my la
2 CONC st Will and Testament in manner and form following.
2 CONT *Item I give and bequeath to my '''three Sons Thomas Moorman Charles Moorman and Archilles Moorman''' all my Money or Negroes if I should gain any whatsoever Estate else I should have gained since the death of my Husband to be equ
2 CONC ally divided Between the three fore mentioned Sons Except my marring Afterwards which I give to '''my two Daughters Judith Douglas and Anne Martin''' to be equally divided between them. 
2 CONT *In witness whereof I have hereunto set my hand and affixed my Seal this twenty ninth Day of January one thousand seven hundred and sixty one.
2 CONT *her Elizabeth X Moorman mark Sign'd seald published and declar'd by the Testator as and for her last Will and Testament in the presence of us George Thompson Lucy English Mary Thompson At a Court held for Louisa County of the 11t
2 CONC h day of May 1765. This will was this day proved in open Court by the Oaths of George Thompson Lucy English Mary Thompson witnesses thereto and by the Court admitted to record and is recorded. Teste James Littlepage clerk[2] Inven
2 CONC tory
2 CONT
2 CONT Date: 12 AUG 1765 Place: Louisa County, Virginia[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Research Notes==
2 CONT from:  [http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~lksstarr/reports/bldfntes.txt Dick Baldauf's OBSERVATIONS edited by Linda Sparks Starr MAY 1996]
2 CONT
2 CONT >First generation is  Samuel  SNEAD  and  Alice;  they  had  three children (second generation) -- (1) Samuel  who  appears  on  the Pamunkey River 1664 as a neighbor of Wm. BASSETT;  (2)    William b. 1630; and (3) Susan who marr
2 CONC ied by 1652 Thomas REYNOLDS.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >Susan proposes that this Thomas and Susan (Snead) REYNOLDS had  a son Thomas who was  father  of  Elizabeth  Reynolds  who married Charles "M" MOORMAN (himself father of Thomas MOORMAN who married Rachel CLARK.)  [Dick apparently
2 CONC  found the Susan  Snead  marriage to Thomas Renalls by 1652 in _The  Sneads  in  Fluvanna  County_. I've  asked  for  specifics  <grin>   Thus,  without  reading  my REYNOLDS update, Susan came up with the same _probable_ father o
2 CONC f  Elizabeth that I did AND added yet another  generation!  Needless to say, this differs from Tillman's REYNOLDS  genealogy  and  the general MOORMAN legend.    LSS]
2 CONT
2 CONT >Susan, writing about earlier family connections with "our" bunch:  "Susan Sneed who wed Thomas  Renalls  also  becomes  an  integral figure.  Note that the daughter of Capt.  Christopher  Clark  and Penelope Johnson -- Rachel "M"
2 CONC  born in 1714 married as her  first husband Thomas Moorman in 1729/30.  Thomas Moorman was the son of Charles and Elizabeth (Reynolds)  Moorman.   Bet  this  Elizabeth Reynolds is a descendant of Susan (Sneed) Renalls and her son 
2 CONC is named after Susan's husband, Thomas Renalls... 
2 CONT
