1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alanson (D Alanson) "Alan" Moremen MOORMAN b: November 18, 1803 in Campbell Co, VA - was a Farmer in Meade Co, KY 1850 d: Bet. January 27 - 29, 1890 in Switzerland, Clay Co, FL b: "Glenn Fount" farm, Brandenburg, M
2 CONC eade Co, KY - ( in Meade Co in 1850 Census) 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=18009173&ref=wvr
2 CONT
2 CONT on of Jesse Adams Moorman (1759-1843) and Elizabeth Buckner Stith (1762-1823). Married Rachel Watkins Stith, had 11 children. They built the grand "Glen Fount" plantation house on the Ohio River just east of downtown Brandenburg, 
2 CONC near Buttermilk Falls. They sold that house to their son Alonzo in 1862 and then moved up river to Riverside The Farnsley-Moreman landing in Jeffersonville.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/18009173/alanson-moremen
