1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for Virginia with the rank of CAPTAIN.  [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A048967  DAR Ancestor #  A048967]
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt. Anthony HADEN1 was born on 26 Mar 1746 in Virginia. He died on 28 Apr 1828 in Christian Co., KY. HADN VA02-"The Douglas Register", birth of daughter, Jeannie. 
2 CONT
2 CONT HADN VA12-Marriage papers for Charles Gilbert and Jeannie Haden. 
2 CONT
2 CONT HADN VA09-Copy of marriage papers for Anthony Haden and Anna Dabney. 
2 CONT
2 CONT HADN KY01-Will, Christian County, Kentucky Will Book E, pp. 330-332,19 December 1827. 
2 CONT
2 CONT HADN VA11-Military, Fluvanna County, Virginia Militia 1779. 
2 CONT
2 CONT HADN VA15-Book, lists father, mother, wife and several residences. 
2 CONT
2 CONT HADN VA18-Family Bible of Capt. Jack Jouett. 
2 CONT
2 CONT HADN VA19-"The Douglas Register", birth and baptismal records for sonJohn and daughter Jane/Jean. 
2 CONT
2 CONT HADN KY02-Bible Record from Nathan Haden Bible, Callie E. Haden,Frankfort, MO. 
2 CONT
2 CONT HADN VA31-"Haden Of Virginia and Kentucky" by Chas. H. Hamlin in"Kentucky Ancestors", July 1969, copy from J. Thacker, 557 Dorado Dr,Fairborn, OH 45324-Jouett Bible Record and agreement in CampbellCounty, Virginia, 20 October 1795
2 CONC , between the sons and sons-in-law ofJohn Haden. 
2 CONT
2 CONT HADN MO04-"John Haden Of Virginia" by Dorothy K. Haden, p. 32; Datafrom Revolutionary War Pension Records, The National Archives,Washington, DC, Revolutionary War Claim, R-4418; Howard County,Missouri, 19 April 1853, child and hei
2 CONC r at law of Anthony Haden,deceased; Joel H. Haden, a resident of Howard County, Missouri;Anthony was a Captain and a Private in the Virginia Militia of the U.S.; Anthony died 28 April 1828, Christian County, Kentucky;Deposition, 4
2 CONC  July 1853, by Joshua C. Prewitt, age 54, living inChristian County, Kentucky, said he was acquainted with Anthony Haden,deceased, his wife and his family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain in the Revolutionary War; In will Elizabeth is called"Elizabeth Gosney, my second daughter"; Proof of marriage is in"Douglas Register", p. 24; "Hayden Magazine", Vol. 2, p. 40; AlbemarleCounty, Virginia Marriage Records. 
2 CONT
2 CONT JOUT KY02-Family Bible of Captain Jack Jouett; "Haden of Virginia andKentucky", contributed by Charles Hughes Hamlin, P. O. Box 3525,Richmond, VA 23234. Anthony Haden, a Captain in Virginia service inthe Revolutionary War, was sta
2 CONC ted in the Jouett Bible to have been ason of John Haden and grandson of Anthony Haden "The Elder" and thathe was born 28 March 1746 (or 1747?). The Bible continues with themarriage dates and names of his three wives and the names 
2 CONC of the issueof each wife. To further substantiate the Bible record there isexhibited herewith a very interesting "Agreement" dated in CampbellCounty, Virginia, 20 October 1795, (Abstracted) - "Know ye that we,the sons and sons-in-
2 CONC law of John Haden, of Campbell County, have bymutual consent and with the consent of the said John Haden, haveagreed to divide among us, all and every part of the said John Haden'sestate that he chooses to give up to us," etc., re
2 CONC nouncing all furtherclaims or right to any (of his) property, etc. Signed By: AnthonyHaden, John M. Haden, J. Haden (Joseph), Benjamin Haden, WilliamHopkins, John Dabney, John Moorman. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Angie Brennan refers to a son, James, born 6 January 1771, baptised,10 April 1771, as the second child of Anthony Haden and DrusillaRountree. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Flags: Military=Y Parents: John HADEN Sr. and Jean (Jenny) MOSELEY.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Drusilla ROUNTREE. Capt. Anthony HADEN and Drusilla ROUNTREE were married on 4 Jul 1765 in Dover Church, Goochland County, VA. Children were: John HADEN.
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Ann HARRIS. Capt. Anthony HADEN and Ann HARRIS were married on 21 Dec 1787 in Albemarle County, Virginia. Children were: Rev. Joel Harris HADEN, William Dabney HADEN, Nathan O. HADEN.
2 CONT
