1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA.  [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A079193  DAR Ancestor # A079193]
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Moon 
2 CONT Birth:	Aug 3 1717 - St Peters Parish, New Kent, Virginia 
2 CONT Death:	Nov 15 1793 - Greene, Georgia
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:	Stephen Moon
2 CONT Wife:	Mildred Cobb
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob MOON b. 3 Aug 1717 [SPPR], d. 1793 Green Co., GA, m. unknown  All of his land sales in Albemarle Co. and Bedford Co. in 1777 and after, have no wife signing, indicating that she was dead before this.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT the St. Peter's Parish Register of New Kent Co., VA [SPPR]
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob was not a soldier, because he was past fifty years old. 
2 CONT He was found the" Public Service Claims" of 1782, the original records of the Virginia State Library of Richmond.  
2 CONT Jacob's claim was allowed in 1782 for furnishing "supplys and services".  
2 CONT He furnished horses and beef for the troupes. This making him a Patriot. 
2 CONT In 1786 The Moon families moved to Greene, Hancock, Elbert, and Madison counties of Georgia.  
2 CONT Jacob Moone became a resident of Greene County, Georgia. 
2 CONT He died there in 1793, he was 76 years old.
2 CONT --------------------
