2 CONT
2 CONT CPT William Henry Moon - father 1740-1810 and Mothert Sarah "Sally" Moon (Richardson) 1741-1814
2 CONT
2 CONT THE WILL OF WILLIAM MOON
2 CONT County Court of Ordinary, in elbert County, Georgia
2 CONT Subscribed and Sworn 7 January 1811, recorded February 2, 1811 by A, Pope, CCO
2 CONT
2 CONT Family members named:
2 CONT Item 1,  My wife, Sarah, the plantation where I now live, one negro man named Edmond, one negro woman 
2 CONT
2 CONT Item 2,  My son Jacob Moon's orphans shall have his equal part exept fifty dollars.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item 3,  My son robert have his equal share except fifty dollars.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item  4,  My son William H. Moon have his equal share except fifty dollars.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item 5, I lend to my daughter, Martha Blake, a child's part.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item 6,  My will and desire that my son Boler Moon, my son Pleasant Moon, my son Archelaus Moon, my Daughter, Sally Green Power, my son John Moon and my daughter Susannah Power, individually to have their equal parts and share of 
2 CONC my estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Executrix: My beloved wife Sarah Moon and my son robert Moon and my son William H. Moon executors.
2 CONT
2 CONT ______________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Military records show his name as: William Henry Moon, born 1740-1810, married Sept. 26, 1761 to Sarah Moone (Richardson)
2 CONT
2 CONT William Henry. Moon was born 11/26/1740 Albemarle Co., VA and Died 5/15/1810 Elbert Co., GA. {FAG #147098762)
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Jacob Moon & Mildred Cobb.
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Sarah "Sally" Richardson (1741-1814).  Children listed:
