1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography: Martha "Patsy" (Moon) Martin ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha, commonly known by the nickname "Patsy," was born in 1749 in Albemarle County, Colonial Virginia. She was a key figure in the Martin family's migration along the Baptist Pipeline from Virginia into the Ninety-Six District o
2 CONC f South Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT She died in 1802 at approximately 53 years of age. While some records suggest a death in Pendleton (Anderson County), she is believed to be buried in Abbeville County, South Carolina, where her husband’s estate was later settled.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Lineage and Family ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha was the daughter of '''Jacob Moon, Sr.''' (a recognized Patriot, DAR Ancestor #: A079193) and '''Mildred (Cobb) Moon'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married '''Charles Martin''' (c. 1741 - 1808), a veteran of the Revolutionary War. Together, they were the progenitors of a large family documented in the 1808 probate records of Abbeville District.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the 1808 Will of Charles Martin and associated family records, Martha was the mother of:
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Elizabeth "Betsy" (Martin) Cobb:''' Married Thomas Cobb in 1783; she predeceased her father.
2 CONT * '''Susan "Sukey" (Martin) Moore:''' Named as an heir in the 1808 Will.
2 CONT * '''Sarah "Sally" (Martin) Nichols:''' Named as an heir in the 1808 Will.
2 CONT * '''George Washington Martin:''' Served as an executor of his father's estate.
2 CONT * '''William Martin:''' Named as an heir in the 1808 Will.
2 CONT * '''Jacob Moon Martin:''' Named as an heir in the 1808 Will; served as an executor.
2 CONT * '''Mildred "Milley" (Martin) Middleton Savage:''' Though not named in the 1808 Will, her relationship is supported by circumstantial evidence and inter-family property contracts.
2 CONT * '''Thomas Pleasant Martin:''' Associated with the family in secondary lineages, though his primary proof remains under curatorial review.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT == Curatorial Notes and Identity Firewalls ==
2 CONT
2 CONT Curators should be careful to distinguish Martha "Patsy" Moon from her daughter Elizabeth "Betsy" Martin.
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Avoid Name Conflation:''' Do not confuse the "Patsy" (Martha) and "Betsy" (Elizabeth) nicknames. Some secondary sources, including older DAR applications, have mistakenly switched their roles or spouses.
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Disproven Relations:''' Martha "Patsy" Moon is '''NOT''' the mother of the "Nancy Elizabeth Martin Savage" (1780-1856) buried in Tennessee. As established in the 1808 Will of Charles Martin, the only daughter Elizabeth in thi
2 CONC s household was the one who married Thomas Cobb and died before 1808.
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Identity Firewall:''' Maintain the separation of this Martin-Moon family from other contemporary Martin groups in the Ninety-Six District to prevent "identity smash-ups" in the Master Profile.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
