1 NAME Margaret /Quinton/
2 GIVN Margaret
2 SURN Quinton
2 _MARNM Nicks
2 NICK Margaret Nicks
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 29 SEP 1717
2 ADDR
3 CITY Dorchester
3 STAE Province of Massachusetts
1 BURI
2 DATE 3 AUG 1760
2 ADDR
3 CITY Greensboro
3 STAE North Carolina
3 CTRY United States of America
1 DEAT
2 DATE ABT 1775
2 ADDR
3 STAE Province of North Carolina
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Some researchers have felt her last name was 'Quinton.' This was due to a man, named Walter Quinton, Jr., who was her godfather & had left her land in 1728 called 'Horsepond Ridge' & 'Hambleton's Marsh' in Dorchest
2 CONC er Co., MD. She may have also been a niece to Walter Quinton. She was Of, Maryland.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret's maiden name was NOT Quinton, as some researchershave thought. In his Will, in 1728, Walter Quinton, Jr. left land called"Horsepond Ridge" and "Hambleton's Marsh" in Dorchester Co,MD to his God daughter, Margaret Edwards
2 CONC , who appears to be a niece;in 1753, John Nicks and his wife, Margaret, sold that same landto Peter Davis of Talbot Co, MD, via their power of attorney toGeorge Nicks and Isaac Nicks, brothers of John Nicks [IV]. (Refs. Wills, Dor
2 CONC chester Co, MD; Accession #HR1297-1; will dated 25 Mar 1727/8; Abstracts of Land Records of DorchesterCo. MD, by James McAllister, v 10, p 654; and Maryland Archives, X:654.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/quinton/289/
2 CONT --------------------
