1 NAME Terrell /White/
2 GIVN Terrell
2 SURN White
2 _MARNM White
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Poplar Springs Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 ADR1 Plot 11-A-10
3 STAE Georgia
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 21 FEB 1813
2 ADDR
3 STAE Georgia
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1 DEC 1902
2 ADDR
3 CITY Poplar Springs
3 STAE Georgia
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Sheriff, post master, applied for liquor license  haralson co with G. W. Gentry in May 1871, 7th Sheriff of Haralson Co., GA and Postmaster of Poplar Springs in 1876
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} HE WAS THE YOUNGEST CHILD OF ANDERSON WHITE BORN ABOUT 1761 IN CAMPBELL CO. VA. AND DIED SEPT. 3, 1826 IN HENRY CO. GA. ANDERSON WAS THE S/O NICHOLAS AND MARTHA REESE WHITE. TERRELL'S MOTHER WAS MARGERY PULLIAM BOR
2 CONC N ABOUT 1768 IN LOUISA CO. VA.  AND DIED IN HENRY CO. GA.DEC. 27, 1847. HER PARENTS WERE ISHAM PULLIAM AND AGATHA TERRELL.
2 CONT
2 CONT TERRELL WHITE MARRIED MARY POLLY BABB DEC.11, 1834 IN HENRY CO. GA. DAUGHTER OF KELLETT BABB AND REBECCA ABERCROMBIE. SHE WAS BORN JUNE 16, 1813 IN LAURENS CO. S.C. AND DIED DEC. 30, 1888 IN HARALSON CO. GA..
2 CONT
2 CONT THEIR CHILDREN WERE ARINDA DIED AS AN INFANT, MARGERY J., REBECCA A. C., JOHN J., MARTHA ELIZABETH (BURIED HERE), MARY ANN (DIED AGE ABOUT 13)IN 1856.SHE MAY BE BURIED HERE. WILLIAM W., JOSEPH TERRELL, LOIS JOSEPHINE WHO MARRIED W
2 CONC YATT MARION (TOBE) ALDRIDGE. THEY ARE BOTH BURIED HERE. AGNES M., AND JAMES A. C. BORN IN 1854. HE WAS THE YOUNGEST CHILD.
2 CONT
2 CONT TERRELL WAS THE 7TH SHERIFF OF HARALSON CO. GA. IN 1871 TERRELL BUILT A LOG CABIN THAT IS NOW THE OLDEST INHABITED HOUSE IN HARALSON CO. GA. IT IS LOCATED NORTH OF TALLAPOOSA ON HIGHWAY 100.
2 CONT
2 CONT TERRELL WHITE AND GEORGE W. GENTRY WHO WAS ALSO A SHERIFF OF HARALSON CO. APPLIED FOR A LICENSE TO SELL LIQUOR IN MAY 1871. HE WAS ALSO POSTMASTER AT POPLAR SPRINGS IN 1876.
2 CONT
2 CONT HIS 2ND WIFE WAS DELILY HANCOCK. THEY HAD NO CHILDREN
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=64176902
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Son of Anderson White & Margery Pulliam White.  Born 2/21/1823 at Elbert County, GA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Temperence Mary "Polly" Babb on 12/11/1834 at Henry County, GA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Terrell White was the 7th Sheriff of Haralson County, GA.  He was also the Postmaster of Poplar Springs in 1876.
2 CONT
2 CONT Terrell White died on 12/1/1902 and is buried in the Poplar Springs Cemetery, Haralson County, GA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/64176902/terrell-white
