1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was a constable in Elbert County in January of 1814. In the first land lottery held in 1805, James Webb drew two "blanks". In the third lottery (1820), He won lot 219, section 4, Walton County even though he liv
2 CONC ed in Elbert County at that time.
2 CONT  He lived in Georgia until 1832/33 when he moved to an area now known as Milltown, Chambers County, Alabama. With nine other men, he help to established a town on land purchased from the Creek Indians.
