1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Regrettably, Clarke Sanders appeared never to have married.  As per Nathaniel Sanders' will, written 1836, Clarke's inheritance was to be managed by the executor,  his brother Hugh Lewis, indicating Clarke had a me
2 CONC ntal impairment and was not capable of managing his own affairs.  To date, no other information has been uncovered about him.   No mention was made of him when  Hugh Louis and entire family moved to Louisiana/Texas about 1842.  We
2 CONC  can only assume that Clarke was deceased by that date.  This same scenario may be indicated by the condition of his nephew, Alfred Holley, son of John and Rachel Sanders Holley.  The will of John Holley, Sr. refers to Alfred as h
2 CONC is "unfortunate son Alfred" and dictates Alfred's inheritance be managed by brother John, Jr.
