1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Constance Ironmonger''', daughter of Francis Ironmonger (b. Abt 1632 in England), was born about 1694 in Gloucester County, Virginia, and died before 18 April 1765, when her estate was probated in Culpeper County.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married John Major (1690-1757), son of George Major and Anne Campbell, in 1682 in New Kent County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Major and Constance Ironmonger, born at King & Queen County:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 	1. Samuel Major,   b. Aft 1710, King & Queen County, Virginia c d. Bef 1764 (Age < 52 years) ] 
2 CONT *  	2. John Major,   b. Aft 1712, King & Queen County, Virginia  
2 CONT *  	3. Jane Major,   b. Aft 1714, King & Queen County, Virginia    Married (unknown) Loggins.
2 CONT *  	4. Priscilla Major,   b. Bef 1720, King & Queen County, Virginia  d. St. Mark's Parish, Culpeper County, Virginia.  Married George Dillard.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Will
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1749-1770 Culpeper County, Virginia Will Book A; [Sparacio]; Page 396-397
2 CONT * In the name of God Amen. I CONSTANCE MAJOR of the County or Culpeper being weak of body but of perfect and sound mind and memory blessed be God do this Twenty sixth day of November in the year of our Lord one Thousand seven hund
2 CONC red and sixty four make and publish this my last Will and Testament in manner and form following, that is to say,
2 CONT * Imprimis I give to my Grandson PHILIP MAJOR the son of SAMUEL MAJOR deced one Heifer of three years old to be paid by my Excers. hereinafter named when he shall arrive to age.
2 CONT * Item I give to my son JOHN MAJOR one shilling Sterling.
2 CONT * Item I give to my Daughter JANE LOGGINS one shilling Sterling.
2 CONT * Item I give to my Daughter PRECILLA DILLARD one feather bed and furniture and after my just debts and funeral charges are paid and satisfied I further give to my said daughter Precilla all the rest and residue of my Estate of wh
2 CONC atsoever kind 
2 CONT *and I do nominate and appoint my Son in Law GEORGE DILLARD and JOHN DILLARD my Grandson Executors of this my last Will and Testament .. to which I have set my hand and affixed my seal.
2 CONT * Presence: ROBT. EASTHAM , Constance Major
2 CONT * THOMAS HUTCHINGS, JNO. LATHAM
2 CONT * MARGET HAM
2 CONT * At a Court held for County of Culpeper on Thursday the 18th day of April 1765
2 CONT * This last Will & Testament of Constance Major decd was exhibited to the Court by GEORGE DILLARD and was proved by the Oaths of THOMAS HUTCHINS one of the witnesses thereto
2 CONT * And at a Court held for the said County on Thursday the 20th day of June 1765
2 CONT * The said Will was further proved by the oath of John Latham another witness thereto & ordered to be recorded and on the motion of the sd George Dillard Certificate is granted him for obtaining a Probat thereof in due form he hav
2 CONC ing sworn to the same & given bond & security as the Law directs, Liberty being reserved for John Dillard Grandson to the said Decedent to joyn in the Probat when he shall think fit.
2 CONT ===
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 1749-1770 Culpeper County, Virginia Will Book A; [Sparacio]; Page 401
2 CONT
2 CONT >Pursuant to an Order of Court of the County of Culpeper bearing date the 29th day of April 1765 by we the subscribers being first sworn to appraise the Estate of CONSTANCE MAJOR Decd .. items listed and valued to total £209..4..6
2 CONC  ( Includes two negro women, a negro man, a negro girl and two negro boys appraised to £195.0.0) .. her wearing apparell not appraised. Given under our hands per CHRISTOPHER HUTCHINGS, JNO. LATHAM , W. ROBERTSON. Culpeper Sct, May
2 CONC  16th 1765. Return into Court & ordered to be recorded.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
