0 @I6000000052073830219@ INDI
1 NAME William /Smeathers/
2 GIVN William
2 SURN Smeathers
2 _MARNM Smeathers
2 NICK Pop
2 NICK Pappy
2 NICK Smothers
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Berry Springs Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Georgetown
3 STAE Texas
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1766
2 ADDR
3 STAE Pennsylvania
1 DEAT
2 DATE 13 AUG 1837
2 ADDR
3 CITY Brazoria
3 STAE Republic of Texas
1 OCCU Scout, hunter
1 TITL Capt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	1766 Berks County Pennsylvania, USA Death: 	Aug. 13, 1837 Brazoria Brazoria County Texas, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Such men in that time as Pappy were known as scouts and hunters and called "Leatherstockings and Deerslayers." They were known by European settlers as "Leatherstocking," 'The Pathfinder", and "the trapper" and by the Native Americ
2 CONC ans as "Deerslayer," "La Longue Carabine" and "Hawkeye".
2 CONT
2 CONT DNA testing has now proven William Smeathers is from the family of William Smither immigrated from Europe sometime around 1700 to Pennsylvania. He married Maria Catherina Jeakel 1734 NJ due to their differences in religious prefer
2 CONC ences. They then settled in Berks Co Pa where he  died 1760 leaving a will naming all his 10 children,  7 sons and 3 daus. More likely Pappy's parents are  Jacob Smethers and lst wife Anna Margaretha, bur Laurel Cem Pennsylvania u
2 CONC nder auspics of being RW Patriot. Jacob Smethers and lst wife Anna Margaretha had at lest 11 children before she died after 1782. Pappy was probably their 2nd child born. [[this old story folks KEEP circulating has NO truth to it 
2 CONC whatsoever so is debunked!>Smithers was born on the border of Virginia near the Holston River, His father was killed by Indians when "Bill " was only twelve years old, and his mother died shortly afterwards. Before dawn on the day
2 CONC  following his mother's burial he went and stood by the graves of his parents and lifting his hand to heaven he made a vow to devote his life to killing Indians. He fullfilled his vow at every opportunity. He was with Issac Shelby
2 CONC  in the battle of King's Mountain.]]
2 CONT
2 CONT HE NEVER USED THE SPELLING SMOTHERS OR CALLED HIMSELF BILL EITHER, that got misused by previous researchers. He could read and write and he always wrote his name as William Smeathers.
2 CONT
2 CONT William never married a Nancy Fitzpatrick![Nancy was the wife of a William Smothers (a man of color) lived in Virginia ALL his life, was illiterate, a laborer and never left VA. Folks used his info for OUR SMEATHERS, wrong! Rev Wa
2 CONC r Record for this black man named William Smothers, wife Nancy requested a pension [S38375] -desc have copy of warrant awarding him 200ac, married Nancy 17 Sep 1795 Powatan Co Va]
2 CONT
2 CONT Another error-our Smeathers did NOT marry a Chrisman/Dubois [The controversy over whether Jost Hite's wife was a Dubois or otherwise was settled once and for all by the article "German Origins of Jost Hite, Virginia Pioneer", by H
2 CONC enry Z Jones Jr, Ralph Conner, and Klaus Wust Edinburg Va 1979. consult Bergert, Vol 1 p.255 for the information. Records have proven that Jost Hite's wife (Magdalena (Hite) Chrismans' mother) was born Anna Maria Merkle 16 Jan 168
2 CONC 7 Bonfeld Germany,dau of Abraham Merkle b 1 Mar 1661 and Anna Veronika. Abraham was son of Jorg Merklin 1603-16 Dec 1686 and Eva 1617-13 Mar 1690. They were not Dubois.Jacob and Magdalena did have dau Ann Maria Chrisman b 29 Sep 1
2 CONC 735 Opequon Va married 1753 to Peter Stephens, had several children thr 1770,Peter lived to 1810. One of many sources is "Chrismans - Virginia to Oregon".]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1782-83 - William moves to Rough River w/his family.  Builds Smeathers Station [Ft Hartford].  Rough River is on the North edge of Hartford Ky,now just plain old Hartford Ky.  Other data mentions Daniel Grass & Jane Smeathers aft 
2 CONC they md, lived at Vienna. "SMEATHERS CABIN ON OHIO RIVER 25mi from FT HARTFORD on ROUGH CREEK."  "It was 15mi to BLACKFORD CREEK from the YELLOWBANKS." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Both Grass & Berry are found in Severns Settlement Tax list. Some saying Wm Berry was father to John Berry md Betsy Smeathers. It is interesting as Wm Berry lived all his life 13mi fr Owensboro & 2 mi fr Rockport on a bluff overlo
2 CONC oking the Ohio River. He also had a good friend name Daniel Bates that give rise to Bate [s] being the middle name of William Smeathers son and grandson. Wm Berry d 1819. He had 3 other bro's, Joel, Enoch & George and Wm was the s
2 CONC on/o Enoch Berry, son/o Henry Berry of the Berry Plain Berry's of King George Co Va near Dogue. AND now we DO know from DNA testing this was our John Berry's family!! This John Berry a bro to Wm Berry md Clara Feagan 1777 Va. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1784-Wm moves Long Falls of Green River or ole Rhodesville. Wm helps build Ft Vienna, now Calhoun McLean Co Ky. Acc/to Dorothy Gentry's book, Law of the Heart. A Margaret Smeathers is born, John Smeathers signs the bond. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1785-1786 - James Gentry was in Va-he was also a friend of William Smeathers in KY Documented [remembering parts of KY once being VA]  Gentry B 15 JUN 1778 Surrey Co NC  Prob abt this time Smeathers family go to Tenn Co NC
2 CONT
2 CONT 1787-Moses Winters on Davidson Co TN [NC] tax roll  1788-Tennessee Co NC formed  [became Davidson Robertson and Montgomery Co Tn after 1796]
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1788 Pappy is found in Tennessee Co NC and soon marries Mary Winters of Robertson Co daughter of Moses Winters and his 2nd wife, widow Elizabeth Head [Crain]. On Moses Winters gravestone in Head Cemetery Robertson Co TN lists W
2 CONC illiam Smeathers as husband of Moses dau Mary Winters, with first child John Sr born 1789 there. Likely one of Moses wife's son from her Crain marriage, whom two were traveling minister's could married them as he did marry several
2 CONC  of the Winters children of Moses and Elizabeth. Since Moses first son by his previous marriage, Caleb Winters, was later in Capt Smeathers Mounted Spy TN Troop also likely due to his previous acquaintance with the Winters family,
2 CONC  and could have likely introduced William and Mary, even married them as he also was a traveling minister.
2 CONT
2 CONT WINTERS Moses (There is huge stone for the Moses Winters family,following is transcription of monument shows Mary's dob and she married William Smeathers on the stone http://www.sandhollow.net/davidmorgan/genealogy/notes.html#NI40
2 CONC 13 
2 CONT
2 CONT Records in 1790 list Constable: William Smeathers Montgomery Co Tenn (Montgomery was formed 1796 prior to that was Tennessee County).  1790 North Carolina turned the area over to United States and became known as The Territory of 
2 CONC United States of America South of the River Ohio. 1796 when Tennessee entered the union, became State of Tennessee. 
2 CONT
