1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mormon Pioneer Overland Travel 1847–1868 [https://history.lds.org/overlandtravels/pioneerDetail?lang=eng&pioneerId=59367 Mississippi Company (1846)]     Approximate age at departure: 45
2 CONT
2 CONT The Roberds family began their journey with the Mississippi Company, which wintered at Fort Pueblo, Colorado. However, according Richard Thomas Roberd's autobiographical sketch, his family did not leave for the Salt Lake Valley wi
2 CONC th the rest of the group in the spring of 1847. Rather they remained in Colorado for another year before continuing on to Utah with a group of "mountaineers" headed for California, arriving in Salt Lake City the summer of 1848.
