1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sarah Williamson was the daughter of Peter Williamson of Bensalem, Bucks County, Pennsylvania.  She married John Roberds at Goshen December 14, 1764.  They had at least 4 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE:  Find A Grave.com
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Williamson was the daughter of Peter Williamson of Bensalem, in the County of Bucks, married John Roberds at Goshen 14th of 12th month, 1764.
2 CONT
2 CONT 11 NOV 1768 - John Roberds & wife Sarah & children granted certificate to Chester M.M., (from Goshen M.M., PA)
2 CONT
2 CONT 26 NOV 1768 - John Roberds and wife Sarah and children Esther, Rebecca & Lydia received on certificate from Goshen M.M., PA (to Chester M.M., PA)
2 CONT
2 CONT 29 Jul 1771 - John Roberds and wife Sarah and children Esther, Rebecca & Lydia granted certificate to Goshen M.M., PA (from Chester M.M., PA)
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 Jan 1772 - John Roberds and wife Sarah and children Esther, Rebecca & Lydia received on certificate from Chester M.M., PA (to Goshen M.M., PA)
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 Mar 1782 - John Roberds and wife Sarah and children granted certificate to Fairfax M.M., Loudoun Co., VA from Goshen M.M. Bucks Co., PA.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Jul 1782 - Got certificate to Hopewell Monthly Meeting, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Mar 1788 - Thomas, John, Asenath and Sarah granted certificate to Bush River M.M., SC (removed with their parents) from Hopewell M.M., VA
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Mar 1788 - Rebeccah, Lydia, Thomas, John, Asenath and Sarah, children of John & Sarah Roberds, granted certificate to Bush River M.M., Newberry Co., SC (from Hopewell M.M. Frederick Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death of husband - bet 1807 Jul 30 - Sep 23 1808 • Hungry Creek, Barren County, Kentucky (now Allen County, Kentucky)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1810 - Barren, Kentucky, "Sary Robaros" [Sarah Roberds]
2 CONT Females - 45 and over = 2 / Females - 26 thru 44 / Females - 16 thru 25 = 1 / Males - 26 thru 44 = 1 / Males - 10 thru 15 = 2
2 CONT
