1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Roberds married Sarah Williamson, December 14, 1764, in Goshen MM, Bucks County, Pennsylvania, daughter of Peter Williamson and Leah Lenisor.  In 1782, John and Sarah moved their family from Bucks County to Vi
2 CONC rginia (Hopewell MM., Frederick County, Virginia), where they stayed for 6 years before moving to South Carolina. (Bush River Monthly Meeting, District 96, South Carolina).
2 CONT
2 CONT 11 Nov 1768 - John Roberds and wife Sarah and children granted certificate to Chester MM (from Goshen Monthly Meeting, Bucks County, Pennsylvania 
2 CONT
2 CONT 26 Nov 1768 - John Roberds and wife Sarah and children Esther, Rebecca & Lydia received on certificate from Goshen Monthly Meeting, Bucks County, Pennsylvania 
2 CONT
2 CONT 29 Jul 1771 - John Roberds and wife Sarah and children Esther, Rebecca & Lydia granted certificate from Goshen Monthly Meeting, Bucks County, Pennsylvania
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 Jan 1772 - John Roberds and wife Sarah and children Esther, Rebecca & Lydia received on certificate from Chester MM from Goshen Monthly Meeting, Bucks County, Pennsylvania
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 Mar 1782 -  John Roberds and wife Sarah and children granted certificate to Fairfax MM, Loudoun County, Virginia  from Goshen Monthly Meeting, Bucks County, Pennsylvania
2 CONT
2 CONT 11 Jul 1783 - John Roberds disowned for disunity at Hopewell MM, Frederick County, Virginia. This is also recorded at Goshen MM records in Bucks County, Pennsylvania
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Mar 1788 - Thomas, John, Asenath & Sarah granted certificate to Bush River MM, SC (removed with their parents) from Hopewell MM, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 Mar 1788 - Rebeccah, Lydia, Thomas, John, Asenath & Sarah, children of John and Sarah Roberds, granted certificate to Bush River MM, Newberry County, SC (from Hopewell MM, Frederick County, Virginia)  
2 CONT
2 CONT 1800 • Union District, South Carolina - Males - 45 and over = 1 / Females - 45 and over = 1 / Males - Under 10 = 3 / Females - 26 thru 44 = 2 / Females - 16 thru 25 = 1 / Females - 10 thru 15 = 1
2 CONT
2 CONT Property
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 Jun 1807 - Hungry Creek, Barren County, Kentucky - John Roberds was granted 108 acres of land on Hungry Creek in Barren County, Kentucky
2 CONT
2 CONT 12 Jan 1814 • Hungry Creek, Barren County, Kentucky - Sarah Roberds, Esther Roberds, Lydia Roberds, John Roberds and Silas Morgan of Barren County, Kentucky Deeded the 108 acres on Hungry Creek, Entered by John Roberds, to John Bl
2 CONC ankinship. Michael Tracy & Andrew Buckhannon were the adjoiners.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: John Roberds who died 1797 Union County, SC born abt 1760 PA was the son of Walter Roberds. 4 Feb 1765 - Admittance of Walter Roberds, wife Rebekah and three children, Thomas, JOHN and Sarah.
2 CONT
2 CONT above posted by David Roberds 
