1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Thomas Sparks was the son of George Washington Sparkes and Luana Roberds Sparkes, and worked as a farmer.  He married Sallie E. Mathews the daughter of Benjamin Mathews and Temperance Weeks.  They had the f
2 CONC ollowing children:  Temperance in 1863, George F., in 1867, William Thomas, in 1870, Sarah Ellen, in 1872, Cyrus, in 1874, John Albert in 1875, Mary M., in 1877, and Bethsaida in 1879.  Sallie died December 21, 1887, at the age of
2 CONC  just 42 years old and was buried in the Pioneer Memorial Cemetery in San Bernardino, California.  William died at the age of 62 years, 5 months and 21 days due to valvular heart disease.  He was buried in the Anaheim Cemetery in 
2 CONC Anaheim, Orange County, California.  It appears the border fence of the cemetery is right over William Sparks grave site.
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE:  Find A Grave.com
