1 NAME John Henry /Turner/
2 GIVN John Henry
2 SURN Turner
2 _MARNM Turner
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE JAN 1822
2 ADDR
3 STAE Georgia
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 24 DEC 1891
2 ADDR
3 CITY Cleveland
3 STAE Georgia
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Henry and Polly Ann (aka Mary A.) were in Lumpkin Co., GA, on the 1880 Census. Many sources say he died in 1893, but his obituary says 1891. Either his gravestone is wrong, or the obituary is. Probably the gravesto
2 CONC ne is wrong, since it appears fairly modern, and was probably erected many years after his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Killed by Falling Limb, 1-23-1891. We are informed that Henry Turner, an old and respected citizen who resided in Chestatee District, was killed last Saturday while out chopping wood. A limb which had lodged from a tree, which he
2 CONC  had felled to the ground, struck him on the head, killing him instantly. The last and only words he uttered were: "Lift me easy," spoken to friends and relatives who had come to his assistance. When the soul took flight, Chestate
2 CONC e District lost one of her best citizens.
2 CONT
2 CONT He has been a strict member of Macedonia Church for many years, and it will be a long time before the kind deeds of this good man are forgotten by the members of his church."
