2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p10/6749/3403/534448380714f714/Seneca_Martin_family__F_-_rosie_and_posie_Seneca_Martin__Great_Aunt__Granddaddy_Henry_martin_Back_Row_-_Aunt_doll__Aunt_Ann__Uncle_Frank__Aunt_Kit_and_Grandma_Appie_Flowers_Lee_large.jpg?hash=b455f7c918093f7f251aac3aaecc45c5dc40af6231df3a746a8d204b8d6b77a2.1794988799
2 FORM jpg
2 NOTE Also, Appalonia died fairly young, as did 3od her kids. he remmarried a woman named Icie...I was told the grandkids never called Icie Grandma, they called her Aunt Icie. They had two sets of twins, and the only one to survive pass
3 CONC ed 26 was your great grandfather Bob (Robert 
2 NOTE Did you get the picture I emailed you? After doing that I found it on Geni.com...
2 NOTE Also, I love the smirk/smile on Appalonia's face! She looks like she was quite the character and had a great personality!
2 NOTE She is a little bit, but not much. I try to tell her interesting things about her side of the family as I find them out to peak interest. She's good about sharing the info she knows when I ask, though! =)
2 NOTE your guess is as good as mine. I will have to look at more info. I will ask my mom.  Is your mom into it?
2 NOTE I love genealogy! I'm so glad you do too! =D Ok, so if it's not Senaca's wife next to him, I know he had at least three sisters - Lucinda, Rebecca and Emily. 
3 CONT
3 CONT As for Senaca's children, I know there's Z. Henry and Frank, as well as Anne and Dollie, and I think (if the census records I have are correct), they had another sister named Mary. Maybe that's who the other woman is?
2 NOTE Emily I am so glad you are so interested. it is an obsession of mine and I, too am hungry for info. 
2 NOTE No not his wife. I was told she was an Aunt, so maybe his sister. Appie Flowers is standing behind her husband Henry. The other three women are aunts, so probably franks siblings Doll and Ann and someone else.
2 NOTE So, is it Senaca holding Posey, his wife Milisa holding Rosie, Zechariah Henry seated next to her in the bottom row?
3 CONT I know Frank Marion is in the middle of the top row, but which one is Appalonia? And who are the other women? This is such a wonderful photo!
