1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ID: I608702134 
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Harrison BAILEY 
2 CONT
2 CONT Given Name: Harrison 
2 CONT
2 CONT Surname: Bailey 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sex: M 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 1 Apr 1852 
2 CONT
2 CONT Change Date: 4 Jun 2005 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: 
2 CONT
2 CONT ? certain this is the right Harrison Bailey
2 CONT
2 CONT Owned land on Tyger River and on Enoree River. He and his wife and fifteen other members were granted letters of dismission from Lower Fairforest Baptist Church to organize New Prospect Baptist Church July 21, 1849. He deeded 3.4 
2 CONC acres of land "For the benefit of the church" May 4, 1850.
2 CONT
2 CONT On November 1, 1851 the church "agreed to pay Brother H. Bailey $14.00 towards the land where upon the meeting house stands" December 6, 1851 he was paid $11.20 ond on January 31, 1852 a balance of $2.80 was paid. Harrison Bailey 
2 CONC died April 1, 1852. His will was dated January 6, 1852 and probated April 17, 1852. They lived in the Sedalia-Cross Keys section of Union County.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---Betty B. Greer.
2 CONT
