1 NAME Benjamin /White/
2 GIVN Benjamin
2 SURN White
2 _MARNM White
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Center Ridge Cemetery, Maud, Bowie County, Texas, USA
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1820
2 PLAC Union County, South Carolina, USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1858
2 PLAC Bowie County, Texas, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ben and wife Polly [Nix] White, were actually buried at the Tapp / Watson Cemetery, until about 1956, when 8 of the grave stones at Tapp / Watson were moved to the Center Ridge Cemetery in Maud.  A Dam had broken, 
2 CONC and flooded the Tapp property, which was Lake Texarkana, now called, Wright Patman Lake.  Thus, there is a Marker that Says Tapp / Watson, where their headstones are today. So, it is a Cemetery within a Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin White was the son of Elias, and Anne B [Gibbs] White, originally of Union County South Carolina, and may have migrated with Ben and Polly, in 1845/46, though there is evidence that Ben and Polly arrived earlier.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben was a Farmer and probably was handy as a blacksmith, as this trade was passed down through the generations, from Robert White Sr, Ben's grandfather.
2 CONT
2 CONT Polly [Nix] White was the daughter of John C Nix, and Sarah (Sally) [Howard] Nix, John died in SC, Sarah came on the wagon train to Bowie Co TX, with Ben and Polly White.
2 CONT
2 CONT These are NOT THE ORIGINAL GRAVE STONES of Ben & Polly, note, the DEATH YEAR ON STONES ARE CORRECT, the AGE on both Stones is not Correct, Ben was 38, not 55, Polly was 37 not 48, they both died young, in todays standards.  The ag
2 CONC e obviously was the result of a relatives best memory, at the time. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ben and Polly [Nix] White, had the following children:
2 CONT Thomas, Marion, William, Susan, Benjamin, Louise, Charles, John G White.
2 CONT
2 CONT We know that Ben and Polly arrived in Bowie Co Tx, 1846, from the Poll tax that Ben is recorded on, in 1850 there were no other White families in Bowie County Texas, other than that of Ben and his Parents family, Elias White, and 
2 CONC his siblings, and surnames married into this family; Bobo, Harlan, Nix all from Union County South Carolina. 
2 CONT
2 CONT An Article on Polly's mother written 1948, SARAH NIX, PIONEER STORY, Texarkana Ark-Tex, December 16, 1948, Two State Press, Chris Hobson's Column, states after he interviewed relatives, that the family had arrived Feb 17, 1846. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Nix, Polly's mother, is considered the first White settler in Texarkana AR, Benjamin White, is considered by some to the the first to settle on the Texarkana Texas side, at the time, they were both in Texas, the borders were
2 CONC  redone, and Sarah Nix ended up in Arkansas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Ben and Polly were to young, to live on their own, after their parents deaths. Were distributed among family, to care for them, until they were of age.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/9069060/benja
2 CONC min-white Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 15 2023, 23:31:30 UTC''
