0 @I6000000002217825792@ INDI
1 NAME Thomas Monroe /White/
2 GIVN Thomas Monroe
2 SURN White
2 _MARNM White
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Center Ridge Cemetery, Maud, Bowie County, Texas, USA
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 15 SEP 1841
2 PLAC Union County, South Carolina, USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 20 JUL 1923
2 PLAC Maud, Bowie County, Texas, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas M White married Marthia Olivia [Harris] White on Aug 11, 1875 in Corley Bowie Co TX. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Benjamin & Polly [Nix] White.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marthia the daughter of John Calvin Harris (CSA), and Mary Jane (Molly) [Johnson] Harris. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas was a Farmer & Blacksmith.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas & Marthia and children were recorded in a Bible belonging to their son Richard Rex White, he listed their Marriage date, and the Births & Deaths of his siblings, until his death in 1956, Richard's wife Illie continued recor
2 CONC ding, at some point passed the Bible to Richard's brother Leo and his wife Sally, after their deaths, was passed to their daughter Frances White Townsend, who passed it on to one of their living sons, who now care for the Bible. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas was a humble and modest man, of quite disposition, content with his farming and blacksmith shop.  A Christian, his whole life, he never held a man in bondage, after the civil war, he rode home, from Dallas, where his unit h
2 CONC ad surrendered, sharing a Mule Ride with a blackman, testiment to his true character, a kind and good man. At his death, he did not request a Civil War Marker, or grave, only that he be buried with his wife, Marthia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Both Thomas and Marthia attended the Maud Methodist Church, with most of their children while in Maud.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas and Marthia had the following children:
2 CONT Marion, Charles, Lola McDaniel, Della Lawrence, Milton, Inez, Leo, Richard, John and Newton White.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Monroe White was a PVT in the Civil War (CSA), served in Co. F, 19th Texas Infantry Regiment, 3rd Brigade, in Walker's Division, Trans-Mississippi Department.  They were also known as the Waterhouse Regt., and Walker's Grey
2 CONC hounds.  
2 CONT
2 CONT This unit engaged at Vicksburg MS, Milliken's Bend, Perkin's Landing, Bayou Teche Campaign, Red Water Campaign, Battle of Mansfield, Battle of Pleasant Hill, and Jenkins Ferry. The unit was part of an effort to prevent the Federal
2 CONC  Army from entering East Texas, one of the successes of the Civil War, preventing the destruction and burning of Texas towns as Sherman's troops had done through out the Southern States.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/73471511/thomas-monroe-white Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 15 2023, 23:25:18 UTC''
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/73471511/thomas-monroe-white
2 CONT ----
