1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://www.lds.org/churchhistory/library/pioneerdetails/1,15791,4018-1-42007,00.html Mormon Pioneer Overland Travel, 1847–1868 Willard Richards Company (1848)]  Age 13
2 CONT
2 CONT Departure: 3 July 1848 Arrival: 10-19 October 1848
2 CONT
2 CONT Company Information: 526 individuals were in the company when it began its journey from the outfitting post at Winter Quarters, Nebraska. This company was divided into two sections, Willard Richards section and Amasa Lyman Section
2 CONC . The Lyman section left the outfitting post on 1 July and the Richards section left on 3 July. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=Sproul&GSfn=A&GSiman=1&GSbyrel=all&GSdyrel=all&GSst=47&GScnty=2800&GScntry=4&GSob=n&GRid=22150735&df=all& Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Jan. 1, 1835 Weakley Giles County Tennessee, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Sep. 26, 1911 Washington Washington County Utah, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Randolph Alexander & Murza Nix Alexander
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Milo Andrus, 27 Mar 1852, Salt Lake City, Salt Lake, Utah
2 CONT
2 CONT Children - Liona Andrus, Laron Alexander Andrus, Randolph Andrus, Lewis Andrus, Henrietta Andrus
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Andrew Sproul, 1 Apr 1868, Washington, Washington, Utah
2 CONT
2 CONT Children - Andrew Sproul, Wright M. Sproul, Angus Sproul, Annie Sproul, Isabell Sproul, Myrza Sproul, Mary Sproul, Adaline Sproul
2 CONT
2 CONT History - The year after her birth, two Mormon missionaries, David W. Patten and Wilford Woodruff, came to the Alexander home.
2 CONT
2 CONT Adeline was seventeen years old when she and Milo were united in marriage on 27 March 1852. Milo was often away on Church duties or with his other wives and families. Milo was with Adeline shortly before the birth of her fifth chi
2 CONC ld, in July 1862, but he left to some urgent matters, and the baby was born before his return.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the course of the birth, Adeline hemorrhaged and so was unable to care for the little one. This incident brought the strained relationship head. When Adeline unburdened her feelings to President Young, he canceled her sealing t
2 CONC o Milo. 
2 CONT
