3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Was in the Journal of the House of Burgess of Virginia in 1743.
1 TITL Pvt
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Petrus, Peiter, and Peter are the same name in different languages. The area where he was born used Dutch, French, and English in everyday usage, and Dutch and Latin in church records.
2 CONT Baptism: MACHACKEMECK Church, Deerpark New York; 28 Jan 1719, Parents: Mattheus Kuykendael, Jannette Westfield. Child; Petrus. Witnesses; Petrus Kuykendal, Reymerig Quick
2 CONT
2 CONT  Peter Kuykendall (baptized 1719, NY - d. NC) moved south in NC with wife Mary (possibly surname Hampton).  Was listed on Samuel Cobrin's 1748 Spanish Alarm roster.  Early affiliation in Augusta Co, VA, with Hamptons and Coburns. 
2 CONC Was in the Journal of the House of Burgess of Virginia in 1743.  Researchers have tried to identify his wife Mary as a Hampton or a Harden but the will of Benjamin and Sarah Harden probated in the counties of Surry and Isle of Wig
2 CONC ht, VA, do not mention a daughter Mary or otherwise married to a Kuykendall.  Some researchers claim this Peter as the Peter Kuykendall of the 1783 Washington Co, NC/TN will.  Children have not been identified.  His age positively
2 CONC  identifies him in NC.
2 CONT --------------------
