1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John and Lucinda were natives of Jasper County, Georgia where he joined the Methodist church on 25 October 1840. They arrived in Choctaw County, Mississippi in 1848 by ox wagon. In the summer of 1850, John organize
2 CONC d the Lebanon Methodist Church of which he and his family were charter members. He and his wife, Lucinda, were the parents of ten children. They both passed away in the year of 1872 and were laid to rest in the Lebanon Methodist C
2 CONC hurch Cemetery. At the time of their death, John was 70 and Lucinda 62. (From http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/p/r/u/Oscar-K-Pruitt/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0624.html), death date is from elsewhere)
