1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Funeral Rites for James Monroe Lamb
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral rites for James Monroe Lamb, 67, who died at his farm home east of Ardmore Friday, were held the first Orthodox-Baptist church 2:30 Saturday afternoon, conducted by the pastor, the Rev. W. Lee Rector. Burial was in Rose Hi
2 CONC ll cemetery with Bettes funeral home in charge of ar­rangements.
2 CONT
2 CONT Escorts for the body were Dr. R.M. Parish, Ed Martin, E.T. Barnett, Roy Pettitt, Stanley Kinney and Henry Mitchell.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include his widow; four sisters, Mrs. Jennie Keith, Cleveland, Texas; Mrs. Pearlie Murphy, Cleveland, Texas; Mrs. Lonia Smith, Tulsa, and Mrs. Mary Tipps, Wilson, and two brothers. Charles Lamb, Clarksville, Texas, and J
2 CONC ohn Lamb, Cleveland, Texas.
