1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Funeral for Charles E. Lamb Held Sunday
2 CONT
2 CONT By Paris News Correspondent
2 CONT
2 CONT CLARKSVILLE —
2 CONT Funeral service for Charles E. Lamb, 67, who died Saturday of a heart attack at home here, was held Sunday afternoon at McKenzie Methodist Church by the pastor, the Rev. Richard Irvin, Jolley-Weaver Funeral Home making burial in F
2 CONC airview Cemetery. Pallbearers were M.L. Wren, Dean Wren, Eugene Bowers, Wilford Witmer, Max Witmer and Bailey Rains.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are Mrs. Lamb, the former Miss Lou Taylor, whom he married at Detroit, Nov. 28, 1898; these children, Tommie Lamb and Mrs. Lindsay McAllister, Clarksville, and Mrs. Nelson Gilbreath, Sulphur Springs; three sisters: Mrs. 
2 CONC Grover Tipps, Oklahoma City, Okla.; Mrs. Tom Keith, Cleveland and Mrs. Pearl Murphy, Bay City.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Lamb, a cotton buyer and owner-operator of a neighborhood grocery here, was born at Emory, Rains County, June 15, 1879. He had been a member of the Methodist Church 47 years and belonged to the Masonic Lodge.
