1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Buell McGough
2 CONT BIRTH
2 CONT 29 Apr 1864 (Date inscribed on gravestone, however narrative shows 29 Apr 1862), born before father's death.)
2 CONT DEATH
2 CONT 1 Apr 1936 (aged 71)
2 CONT BURIAL
2 CONT East Dora Cemetery
2 CONT Dora, Walker County, Alabama, USA
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID
2 CONT  17655436 
2 CONT
2 CONT Book, "A Glimpse of The Past", by Carolyn McGough ROWE, 2000, page 30-- William Buell McGough, born 29 April 1862 in Thorn Hill, Marion County, Alabama was the only child born to Joseph McGOUGH and Martha Jane GIST. William is pos
2 CONC sibly named after his grandfather William B. McGOUGH. William's father Joseph served in the War Between the States when William Buell was only 5 months old. Four and on-half months later while in the service, his father Joseph die
2 CONC d of measles, with William Buell was just nine months old. On June 3, 1865 William B. and his mother lived in Paducah, KY where they applied for Joseph's Civil War Pension, but they later returned to Marion County, Alabama and liv
2 CONC ed with his grandfather Christopher GIST. On the 1870 census they are living in his household along with Martha's sister Angeline PACE and her daughter
2 CONT
