2 ADDR
3 STAE Texas
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Surveyor
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Richard Hooper arrived in Texas Feb 1836, a memeber of the First Congress of the Texas Republic.  Entering the Texas Army as a Commander of a company of Cavalry from San Augustine, July 6, 1836.  He served until ho
2 CONC norably discharged Oct6.  Three days before his discharge the Session of First Congress of Republic began with Hooper attending as Representative from Shelby Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1839-40 he acted as County Surveyor of Shelby, a draft of $622.25 was issued him in January 1840 for his services in this position, he having run the Shelby County lines.  In August 1848, Richard Hooper was again elected County
2 CONC  Surveyor of Shelby, his last recorded office.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard's children occurred in Tenn., in 1811 thru 1830.  
