1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT John Word Hooper, said son of Richard Brooks/Brookes Hooper and Elizabeth Adams Word, was the first white settler of St. Clair Co., AL, the only one listed in the 1810 census for this county. He was married to Easter/Ester Goodwin
2 CONC  about 1815, according to some published accts, but I haven't been able to locate a marriage record as of yet. The known children of John Word Hooper were Member Silverside Hooper (possible adopted Indian child), James Adams Hoope
2 CONC r, Thomas Hooper, Rachel Hooper Montgomery, John Cleveland Hooper, and Martha Hooper Cornelius.</p><p><p></p></p><p><p>It is published in some books that his birth date was Jan. 16, 1782, a detailed date that could only come from 
2 CONC a tombstone, bible record, court record, church record, or first hand account letter from the 1800s, but I have never found such proof, even though his siblings found listed in books and online, also have exact dates of birth, wit
2 CONC h no proof offered. John Word Hooper's parents are said to be Richard B. Hooper and Elizabeth Adams who married in Halifax Co., VA on January 13, 1783 (which is recorded in said county). If Elizabeth was indeed his mother, then it
2 CONC  is very unlikely John was born in 1782, prior to their marriage. I also haven't determined if John was born in VA, SC, or GA where Richard B. Hooper was known to have lived over the years. Any help in locating concrete proof of h
2 CONC is place of origin would be greatly appreciated. - RCJ
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members
2 CONT Parents
2 CONT Richard Brookes Hooper 1756-1846 
2 CONT Elizabeth Adams Hooper 1753-1834
2 CONT Esther Goodwin Hooper (m. 1815)
2 CONT Siblings
2 CONT Jesse Carter Hooper 1791-1880
2 CONT Amelia Monroe Hooper Cleveland 1798-1870
2 CONT Children
2 CONT Member Silverside Hooper 1818-1894
2 CONT James Adams Hooper 1820-1890
2 CONT Thomas C. Hooper 1821-1896
2 CONT Rachel Hooper Montgomery 1822-1878
2 CONT Martha Hooper Cornelius 1833-1892</p>
