2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/65279283/johnson-monroe
2 CONT
2 CONT Johnson witnesses a deed from William Owen to Peter Crews in Lunenburg, VA (Deed Book 11, p. 88) on 8 Oct 1767 - so likely born before 1746. He is deceased prior to 16 Sep 1929 per Barren Co., KY Deed Book L p 569 when an indentur
2 CONC e made selling his land to his son James Monroe by other heirs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Transcript of a letter from Simon Peter Monroe (b. 1829), grandson of Johnson Monroe and son of Mathew Hooper Monroe (b. 1800), to his nephew Elmer Ellsworth Monroe (b. 1876), son of Mathew Hooper Monroe (b. 1840). Comments in [ ]
2 CONC  are by the transcriber, Evelyn A. Swan.
2 CONT
2 CONT Chase, Kans.
2 CONT May the 27th, 1912
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. E E Monroe Lyons [Kansas]
2 CONT
2 CONT Dear Sirs Just got your letter and as you are a [better] scribe than I will let [you] fill out the blank. You now [know? the word "now" might be "name"] all your Fathers Brothers. My Father [Mathew Hooper Monroe] was the youngest 
2 CONC boy in the home. His brothers, Wm. the oldest, James, Jonson, David and Matthew. My grandfather had neither brother or sister. He was born after his father was killed by a tree falling on him. His name was Jonson and the babe was 
2 CONC named for his father. Grandfather was born in Virginia. My father in Ky. Hope when your father comes you and wife will visit us.
2 CONT
2 CONT Yours truly,
2 CONT
2 CONT S. P. Monroe
2 CONT .......
2 CONT Marriage record:
