1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Elisabeth is not one of the heirs in the 1829 Deed Book L which lists children of Johnson and Amelia. Did Johnson and Amelia have a daughter, Elisabeth? If so did she die prior to 1829? Could she be the mother of the 2 unidentifie
2 CONC d males in Johnson's 1820 census and the 1 udentified male in Amelia's 1830 census?
2 CONT
2 CONT The only place Elisabeth (or Elizabeth) is mentioned is in the bible of William H. Monroe, the son of Matthew. William H. had a sister named Amelia Elizabeth who died about age 1 so possibly this is the source of the confusion.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Elizabeth Monroe who married Alexander Adair in Barren County is not Johnson's daughter. She is the daughter of Andrew Monroe.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her birth date is a guess based on census data.
2 CONT
2 CONT Compiled and edited by Allen Alger, Genealogist, Clan Munro Association, USA 
