2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-230214054/john-a-day-in-familysearch-family-tree FamilySearch Family Tree] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 5 2020, 11:57:29 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/52595847/john-day
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT At this time the parents of John Day are unknown. His place of birth is listed as Tennessee on the 1860 US Federal Census and in his obituary. John Day married Elizabeth Smith on 10 March, 1809 in Harrison Township, Gallia Co., Oh
2 CONC io
2 CONT
2 CONT John Day's will contains the names of his heirs and living children. The known children listed in the will are:
2 CONT - Robert Hamilton (m. Jane Amanda Hay), (1810-1890) 
2 CONT - George Washington 
2 CONT - Mary Polly (m. George Rader), (1816-1912) 
2 CONT - John Jr. (Jack)
2 CONT - Maria Ann (m. John Robinson), (1823-1870)
2 CONT - James Morgan (m. Minerva Barker), (?- 1880)
2 CONT - Elizabeth Jean 
2 CONT - William 
2 CONT His son, Thomas J. (1828-1840) is not included in the will because he died before his father. Thomas Day's stone, in this same cemetery, lists him as one of their children.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Day is found in the following US Federal Census records:
2 CONT - 1820 for Harrison Township, Gallia Co., Ohio, he is listed by name, occupation farmer
2 CONT - 1830 for Harrison Township, Gallia Co., Ohio, he is listed by name, occupation farmer
2 CONT - 1840 for Harrison Township, Gallia Co., Ohio, he is listed by name, occupation farmer
2 CONT - 1850 for Harrison Township, Gallia Co., Ohio, with his spouse and daughters, Elizabeth and Mary, occupation farmer, birth place listed as Virginia
2 CONT - 1850 Special Agricultural Census 
2 CONT - 1860 for Clay, in Gallia Co., Ohio, with his spouse and daughter, Elizabeth, and granddaughter, Amanda, occupation farmer, birth place listed as Tennessee. His nearest neighbor is the family of his daughter, Mary Polly Rader 
2 CONT
2 CONT This is what we know from his obituary:
2 CONT Gallipolis Journal, Gallipolis, Ohio
2 CONT March 24, 1870
2 CONT Transcribed by Sandy Lee Milliron    
2 CONT
2 CONT Day, John
2 CONT DIED 
2 CONT      In Harrison township, Gallia County, Ohio, Mr. John Day, Sr., died in the 85th year of his age. Mr. Day was born in Tennessee, February 10th, 1786, moved with his parents to Virginia, then to Gallia County, where he has resid
2 CONC ed ever since. He leaves an aged partner to mourn his loss - one who has shared his joys and sorrows for a period of sixty-one years - they having been married March 10th, 1809.
2 CONT      Mr. Day has been a member of the Baptist Church since 1844, and was distinguished for his strict honesty and moral habits.
2 CONT
2 CONT age 84y, 22d
2 CONT
2 CONT - compiled by Gaynelle Hobt Morton
2 CONT - Jan 2017
