2 CONT U.S., Family History Books
2 CONT Captain Isaac Williams
2 CONT Gender Male
2 CONT Birth Date 17 Mar 1779
2 CONT Birth Place Surry County, NC
2 CONT Marriage Date 1 May 1801
2 CONT Death Date 13 Feb 1856
2 CONT Father Isaac Williams
2 CONT Mother Rachel Pike
2 CONT Spouse Rebecca D RibelinAmeliaLucy Dye
2 CONT Child AbelAndrew Jackson JacksonRichardGarrett GibsonLaban
2 CONT Title Captain Isaac Williams and His Grand Children: the Story of A Fighting Quaker and Three Generations of Indiana Pioneers  
2 CONT Author Dixon, Ben F. (Benjamin Franklin), 1892- 
2 CONT 3em>He was the son of Isaac Williams, Sr. and Rachel Pike.
2 CONT 3em>
2 CONT 3em>He was born in Surry Co., NC., March 17, 1779; and died Feb. 13, 1856, in Lawrence Co. , Indiana.
2 CONT 3em>
2 CONT 3em>He married, 1st, Amelia, daughter of Garrett Gibson, May 1, 1801.  She was born in Surry county June 6, 1786, and died July 2, 1841, in Lawrence county.  Tradition says the wedding took place at Asheville NC.  As Amelia was no
2 CONC t yet fifteen, it appears that this may have been a runaway marriage, without church sanction.  At any rate, Isaac was disowned immediately thereafter.  Both Isaac and Amelia are buried at Old Union in Lawrence county.
2 CONT 3em>
2 CONT 3em>Married, 2nd, April 14, 1844, Lucy Dye.  She was born July 4, 1801; and died in Lawrence co., Aug. 24, 1844 burial, Ferguson cemetery.
2 CONT 3em>
2 CONT 3em>Married, 3rd, May 31, 1846, Rebecca D. Dibelin: born Dec. 23, 1797; died March 23, 1857;  
2 CONT 3em>
2 CONT 3em> Isaac Williams died Feb. 13th, 1856.  His funeral was conducted at the Bedford New School Presbyterian Church at 3:00 PM the 14th.  The oration was by a famous "Campbellite" preacher, Elder James M. Mathes.  What a brave Vale
2 CONC ntine it was that he sent to St. Michael the Archangle and Patron of Brave Soldiers!  Rebecca passed away March 23, 1857.  Capt. Isaac sleeps eternally at Old Union, with his first and last loves.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/53859210/isaac-williams Capt Isaac Williams  ]
2 CONT Birth 17 Mar 1779 Surry County, North Carolina, USA
2 CONT Death 13 Feb 1856 (aged 76) Lawrence County, Indiana, USA
2 CONT Burial Old Union Cemetery Fayetteville, Lawrence County, Indiana, USA
