1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''William Ashburn "''Old Billy''" Ross''' was born 10 Sep 1814 in Tennessee and on died 19 Jul 1898 in Gennesee, Latah County, Idaho of heart failure.  He was buried in the Yellow Rose / Ross Cemetery near Moscow,
2 CONC  Latah Country, Idaho, United States. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Abijah Ross and Elizabeth Jackson.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Billy" married before 1834 in TN, Mahala Mary "Haley" Cunningham, b. 7 Dec 1816, KY; d. 14 Mar 1889 ID.  She was the daughter of Joseph Cunningham and Phoebe Fine.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the '''1850''' federal census, '''William A. Ross''', a farmer, lived at Hopkins County, Kentucky, with his wife and children at Hopkins County, Kentucky.  The family at the time consisted of:
2 CONT * Head  '''William A Ross''' 36  
2 CONT * Wife  '''Mahala Ross''' 34  
2 CONT * Son  '''William R Ross''' 15  
2 CONT * Daughter  '''Elizabeth Ross''' 14  
2 CONT * Daughter  '''Rebecca Ross''' 13  
2 CONT * Son  '''Abijah Ross''' 11  
2 CONT * Son  '''John Ross''' 10  
2 CONT * Daughter  '''Charlotte Ross''' 8  
2 CONT * Son  '''Ashburn Ross''' 6  
2 CONT * Daughter  '''Eliza Ross''' 4  
2 CONT * Daughter  '''Susan Ross''' 2 
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Obituary
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~tnlincol/queries/query10.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Died in Genesee, on Tuesday July 19, 1898, of heart failure, Mr. William Ashburn Ross, at the advanced age of 84 years.  Mr. Ross ate a hearty dinner and was about to take a stroll when he suddenly dropped to the floor dead. Mr.
2 CONC  Ross was born near Nashville, Tenn., September 10, 1814.  He moved to Kentucky in 1847, and from Kentucky to Arkansas in 1859.  He came to Idaho in 1875, crossing  the plains by wagon. The deceased leaves ten children to mourn hi
2 CONC s death.  The funeral took place Thursday at 11 a.m., conducted by Rev. McPherson.  The remains were buried near Yellow Rose school house on the Potlatch."
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Aged 83 yrs., 10 mos, 9 days.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Namesake: I believe that William Ashburn Ross was named after Joseph Ashburn who was one of Elizabeth "Betsy" Griscom Ross husbands. Joseph Ashburn died in captivity on 3 March 1782 in Old Mill, England."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT In the book, [http://books.google.com/books?id=7vZkoiIPkq4C&lpg=PA351&ots=YNQt5n1eE3&dq=Abijah%20Ross&pg=PA351#v=onepage&q=Abijah%20Ross&f=false Boone County, AR, by the Turner Publishing Company,]  (1988), page 351:
2 CONT
2 CONT >William Ashburn Ross ... was born Sept 10, 1814, Davidson County, TN.  By 1820 his parents relocated to Lincoln County where, about 1834, he married Mahala Mary Cunningham, born Dec 7, 1816, in Kentucky.  After 1846, Billy moved 
2 CONC his family to Hopkins County, KY.  In early 1858 they moved into Jackson Township, Carroll County, AR.  They settled about one mile from the present town of Batavia, Boone County.  In 1875 Billy and Haley left Arkansas, traveling 
2 CONC by covered wagon over the Oregon Trail to the frontier of the Idaho Territory.  They lived the remainder of their lives among many of their descendants who also shared in the that trek.    They are buried in the Ross Cemetery near
2 CONC  Moscow, Latah Country, ID.  
2 CONT
2 CONT - submitted by Delores Y. (Buell) Eveland
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT In the book Early and Present History of Fix Ridge, Latah County, Idaho, 1877-1964 (second edition 1966) was found this information concerning five other people who it states were buried in the Ross Cemetery:
2 CONT
2 CONT >"William Ashburn (Old Billie) Ross and his wife, Mahala, are both buried on Fix Ridge in the Ross Cemetery." This would be Mahala M. (Cunningham) Ross, born 1816 in Kentucky or Alabama, died in Idaho; nicknamed Haley. (pp. 107 an
2 CONC d 121)
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Haley Ross, Cintha and Ella Johnson died soon after we came to the Ridge (1887) and are buried in the Ross Cemetery. I attended all the funerals and I remember they were each buried in a pine wooden box." (Cintha Johnson, wife o
2 CONC f Hubb Johnson.) (p. 121)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.internetbaglady.com/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I0539&tree=Rea [dead link] comment by Delores Y. (Buell) Eveland  Sat Mar 29 16:50:31 1997
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ROSS/CUNNINGHAM/JACKSON/HOWTON/REA/JEROME/ROARK/ HINZEMAN/GILLIAM/JOHNSON/SHIELDS/KING/CLARK/JONES/EVANS/ RAY 
2 CONT
2 CONT >Researching ancestors and descendants of William Ashburn "Billy" ROSS, b. 10 Sep 1814 TN; d. 19 Jul 1898 ID; son of Abijah and Elizabeth (JACKSON) ROSS. "Billy" m. bef. 1834 in TN, Mahala Mary "Haley" CUNNINGHAM, b. 7 Dec 1816, K
2 CONC Y; d. 14 Mar 1889 ID, of unknown parents. "Billy" and "Haley" ROSS lived in Lincoln and/or Davidson Co., TN until about 1848 when they moved to Hopkins Co., KY. By the Spring of 1858 they had moved into Carroll Co. (later Boone Co
2 CONC .), AR, settling near Batavia. They remained in Boone Co., until about 1875-80 when they traveled by wagon train to Nez Perce or Latah Co., ID where they lived the remainder of their lives. They were the parents of 13 children, th
2 CONC e eldest of whom m. and remained in Kentucky. Several others married and settled in Boone Co., AR., while others moved to MO and ID. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
