1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Silas Coleman Ross''' was born 14 Nov 1819 in Tennessee, USA, and died 03 May 1874 in Lincoln, Tennessee, USA. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT They lived in a log house on Short Creek. One boy and ten girls were born. The girls married into families in the area. These families were Bryant, Hogan, Hobbs, George, Bradley and Gill. 
2 CONT It is said that Silas Ross rode off from the house on a horse to hide some valuables. Upon his return to the house, he decended from the horse and slumped dead before he was able to tell anyone where he hid the valuables. They wer
2 CONC e never found by the family.  Source:The Volunteer, Fall 1985, Fayetteville, TN via http://www.internetbaglady.com/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I0653&tree=Rea
2 CONT ==Family==
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:  son of Abijah Ross and Elizabeth Jackson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
