1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/52877900/mary-hutchens Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 12 2021, 13:58:44 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was born Nov. 7, 1831 in Indiana, the 7th child of Samuel and Jemima (Cox) Jackson.  (Samuel b. 1789, was the son of Samuel Jackson Jr She married James Hutchens June 3, 1848.  James was born May 16, 1829 in Indiana, the son 
2 CONC of Hezekiah Hutchens born in Surry Co, NC, a descendant of Strangman Hutchens.  James was a brother of Thomas Hutchens who married Mary's sister Anna Jackson.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Springfield MM in Wayne Co, IN, reported James marring contrary to discipline, and condemned his misconduct on Apr. 20, 1850.  Mary was received into the Springfield MM on June 13, 1850, and they both were disowned Aug. 19, 18
2 CONC 54 for non attendance and for joining two secret organizations.  Mary's organizations were called "Daughters of Temperance" and "Good Tempers".
2 CONT
2 CONT (Samuel b. 1789, was the son of Samuel Jackson Jr b 1738, who was the son of Samuel Jackson b 1725.)* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/52877900/mary-hutchens Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/S
2 CONC martCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Sep 21 2022, 17:01:26 UTC''
