2 CONT April 13, 1815 Pickens Co., SC Deed book C-1 page. 279
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Alexander gave 2 acres of land on Crow Creek to KeoweeBaptist Church, whereon the meeting house now stands. Witnesses:Manoah Stephens and Samuel Barron. Recorded 1-5-1837.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pickens Co. estate records Estate of Daniel Alexander
2 CONT
2 CONT a) William Littleton petitioned for letters of Administration. Dated12-13-1850.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Micajah was administrator of estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT b) Micajah Alexander petitioned for order to sell the personalestate. Granted 1-11-1851.
2 CONT
2 CONT c) Estate of Daniel Alexander, dated April 2, 1851. Paid heirs:Janney (sic) Nix, Emilia (sic) Field, Tyry
2 CONT
2 CONT Boon, Margaret Hudson, and William Littleton, their share. PaidThomas Alexander, his account $60.00, Letty Nix $25.00,and E. Alexander $2.93.
2 CONT
2 CONT d) Estate of Daniel Alexander and wife, deceased, dated: 1-20-1852.Heirs: William Hudson, Tyre Boon, Janens Nix, and MicajahAlexander, administrator and heir.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pickens Co., Probate records, Inventories, Appraisements and Sales, Book. 2 pages PP. 115 & 116. Sale of personal property of DanielAlexander.
