0 @N6000000004851298193@ NOTE 26. i. Jesse PATY married Sarah Sallie West, daughter of Joseph West and Jane Owen, at Never married. He was born in 1744/45 at Brunswick County, Virginia. He married Delilah Doss, daughter of James Doss and Frances Nix, circa 176
1 CONC 3 at Virginia. He died after 9 November 1795 at Union County, SC.
1 CONT Reference: 160. He A Jesse Paty served in the Bedford County, Virginia Militia in Sept , 1758. Jesse was then about fifteen, if his dates are right. *6 Mar 1767 Jesse received 400 acres on Beach Tree Creek, adjacent t o James Paty
1 CONC  on North side. (ref ltr. Corinne H Diller) *June 1767 Jesse listed with tithables taken. (Ref Hisroty of Pittsylv anis County Virginia pg 289) *1768 James Paty of Berkely County SC gave Jesse Paty of Pittsylvania County , Virgini
1 CONC a. power of Atty. to sell land left 'by the will of James Paty'. *Jesse is listed on both the Virginia and South Carolina census, thi s happened because he was still living in Virginia, but had already bought lan d in South Caroli
1 CONC na, and was preparing to move his family there. I do not know t he exact date Jesse made this move. Jesse was still buying land in Virginia i n 1771. James Doss, father of Jesse's wife Delilah, bought land next to Jess e in 1783. 
1 CONC But Jesse had sold land on Pateys Creek by 1791 to Benjamin Canafax. This does not mean he had to be still living in Virginia. Je sse had bought land in South Carolina in 1788, and could have moved t here, while still owning land 
1 CONC in Virginia. He was living in South Car olina when he died in late 1795, early 1796. *Union Dist: SC, Book A, page 94. Indenture 21 June 1788 between George McWhorter and Jesse Patty of Un ion County, South Carolina, McWhorter for
1 CONC  150 pounds sells Patty land o n west side Broad River by McKissicks line also part of two other tra cts formerly laid for James Love and Henry Clark of 31 acres and in t he whole 231 acres. *Wit: John McWhorter; George McWhorter;
1 CONC  and Elizabeth McWhorter. Recor ded 23 June 1788. *Copy of Jesse Patty's will is on record in the Union County,  Courthous e. I have a copy. DCL *Good Source books: Virginia Colonial Militia By William Armstrong Crozier. List of t
1 CONC he Colonial Soldiers of Virginia By H.J. Eckenrode and Colo nial. Colonial Solders of the South 1732-1774 by Murtie June Clark. *.
