0 @N6000000005425268236@ NOTE [Lowrey from Family Origins by Robert Jacob on RootsWeb.ged]
1 CONT
1 CONT History: 1842 Moved to Farmington, MS., located four miles from thepresent town of Corinth, MS. Here he became a brick mason.184? Servedin the Mexican War. 18 50 Tishomingo Co. MS. no children.1860Tishomingo Co., MS. seven childre
1 CONC n. 1861 At start of Civil War he wasliving at Kossuth, MS. nine miles southwest of Cori nth, MS. He was
1 CONT pastor of the Baptist churches at Kossuth and Ripley. He serve d in the32nd Mississippi Regiment and was a Colonel at the begining of thewar. He was wounded at the battle of Perryville, KY. When GeneralLowery was wounded and retur
1 CONC ned home to convalesce he realized hecould not return to Kossuth as th e Yankees were nearby. He had hisbrother Calvin go get his family and bring the m to a cabin he hadrented at Tippah, located eight miles south of Ripley, close
1 CONC  to hisbrother Calvin. Here they lived three years. In Oct.1865 Mark bought apl ace two miles nearer Ripley. Four years later he traded it for theBrougher Plac e, the present location of Blue Mountain College. Afterthe war for sev
1 CONC en years he was the editor of the MississippiDepartment of "The Baptist" which was publs hed in Memphis. 1869 Markdecided to undertake the founding of a school for girl s in thenorthern partof the state. It was opened Sept. 1873 w
1 CONC ith fortystudents enrolled, a few of them boys. Fourteen were boaders ($12.00 amonth) for forty s essions. Named Blue Mountain Female Institute. Forten years in sucession he was elected President of the MississippiBaptist State Co
1 CONC nvention. Several times he served as Trustee of theState University and also of the Mississippi College a t Clinton. WhenModena married Rev. W. E. Berry in 1876 Rev. Berry bought a half interest in the school and the owners became
1 CONC  the firm of "Lowrey &Berry". In187 7 the school was chartered as Blue Mountain College.[MP Lowrey from Hirt-Klooz Saga on GenCircles.ged]
1 CONT
1 CONT This individual was found on GenCircles at: http://www.gencircles.com/users/hirt-klooze/4/data/4262[Adam Lowrey from Hirt-Klooz Saga on GenCircles.ged]
1 CONT
