0 @N6000000002217814500@ NOTE Will of Mary Howard--Records Old Will Book B. pg. 256
1 CONT Will was recorded Jan. 31, 1839
1 CONT Box 25  Pkg. 9
1 CONT
1 CONT South Carolina
1 CONT Union District
1 CONT
1 CONT I, Mary Howard, of the state and district aforesaid being of sound and disposing mind but weak body do make this my last will and testament in the name of God--Amen--first it is my wish that all my just debts be paid.  With my  fu
1 CONC neral expenses next.  It is my wish that all my property whether real or personal be divided between my beloved children Clara Little her heirs and Sarah Nix and her heirs.  With the daughters and son of my beloved son Aaron Howar
1 CONC d May Sarah and Aaron Clemmons, except ten dollars I give and bequeath to my daughter Dicey Rogers and ten dollars I give and bequeath to my grandchildren sons and daughters of Clemmons Howard.  My property consists of one tract o
1 CONC f land near Union courthouse containing one hundred and eighty acres more/or less together with five Negroes Milley, Finder, Harvey, Bill and Dianna--and I nominate and appoint William Crenshaw of state and district my Executors t
1 CONC o this my last will and testament in witness whereof I hereunto set my hand and seal this ninth day of January, 1839.
1 CONT
1 CONT Signed sealed in presence ofMary Howard
1 CONT Wm. Murphy
1 CONT Jason Greer
1 CONT Halley Sparks
