0 @N6000000000911661345@ NOTE [Jeffer~1.ftw]
1 CONT
1 CONT [LEEFTM~2.ftw]
1 CONT
1 CONT Isaac jr Williams (34.Rachel4 , 19.Abigail3 , 4.Ephraim2 , 1.Jacob1 ) b. 17 Mar 1779, Surry Co.,NC, occupation Soldier, farmer, m. 1 May 1801, in Asheville,NC, Amelia Gibson, b. 6 June 1786, Surry Co.,NC, (daughter of Garrett Gibs
1 CONC on and Prudence Sumner) d. 2 July,1841, Lawrence Co, Ind, buried: Old Union Cemetery,Lawrence Co, Indiana.  Isaac died 13 Feb 1856, Lawrence Co, Ind, buried: 14 Feb 1856, Old Union Cemetery, Beford, Ind.  Called "Capt." for his mi
1 CONC litary rank in War of 1812. Isaac jr., wife Amelia and 7 children moved from Tenn to Ind. in 1817. His uncle, Wm.Williams, a Quaker preacher, had seen Indiana.  Isaac came in the 1815-16 winter to file claim and pay for a cabin to
1 CONC  be built. His sister,Rachael, husb,Thos Adamsen,& children also in the party. Amelia: Married before she was 15.  Isaac disowned in June for marriage to minor.
